E["npc:athridas-bearmantle"] = {t="npc",n="Athridas Bearmantle",z="teldrassil",s="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf sentinel residing in Dolanaar within the boughs of Teldrassil. Tasked with safeguarding the local settlement, he directs young adventurers to investigate the encroaching corruption affecting the local wildlife and the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs.",h="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf sentinel residing in Dolanaar within the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of Dolanaar",b="Stationed within Dolanaar, Athridas Bearmantle stands as an early line of defense for the night elves emerging from Shadowglen. As the boughs of the newly grown world tree Teldrassil exhibit unnatural signs of decay and unrest, Athridas works tirelessly to coordinate local scouting efforts and protect the peaceful township from surrounding threats.",sp=0},{t="The Furbolg Affliction",b="Much of Athridas's concern centers on the neighboring Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs. Once peaceful neighbors, the Gnarlpine have succumbed to a spreading madness and corruption that poisons their shamans and chieftains, driving them into violent frenzy against the Kaldorei. Athridas mobilizes willing champions to contain the threat and unearth the deeper taint taking root in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a night elf stationed in Dolanaar on the island of Teldrassil. He serves as an organizer for local defense, enlisting adventurers to combat the dark forces creeping through the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"who is athridas","athridas bearmantle lore","athridas dolanaar"}},{q="Where can I find Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas is located in Dolanaar, the first major town night elf adventurers reach after leaving Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"athridas location","where is athridas","find athridas bearmantle"}},{q="What threats does Athridas focus on?",a="Athridas primarily focuses on the aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs who have fallen prey to a corrupting influence, directing travelers to quell their attacks, investigate their madness, and recover vital relics.",al={"athridas quests","what does athridas want","athridas bearmantle tasks"}},{q="Is Athridas related to Broll Bearmantle?",a="While Athridas shares the prominent Bearmantle surname with renowned night elf figures such as Broll Bearmantle, the exact nature of their familial relationship is not explicitly chronicled.",al={"is he related to broll","broll bearmantle relation","athridas and broll"}},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking Dolanaar?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen victim to a dark, unnatural corruption seeping through Teldrassil, which has driven their shamans and warriors mad with hostility toward the night elves.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine corruption","furbolg hostility teldrassil"}},{q="What role does Athridas play in securing Teldrassil?",a="Athridas acts as an early sentinel and organizer, ensuring that the spreading corruption among the beasts and furbolgs of Teldrassil is confronted before it can overrun the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"athridas role","athridas importance"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young Kaldorei leaving Shadowglen, Athridas represents the grounded reality of Teldrassil's struggles, pointing out that their new home is already threatened from within.",["class:Druid"]="Athridas's missions against the corrupted Gnarlpine and his concern for ancient relics directly touch upon the balance of nature that druids are sworn to restore."},kw={"athridas","bearmantle","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","kaldorei","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:476","quest:475","quest:483","quest:486","topic:night-elf"},src={"Athridas Bearmantle"}}
E["npc:corithras-moonrage"] = {t="npc",n="Corithras Moonrage",z="teldrassil",s="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He guides newly arrived adventurers in understanding the nature of the great World Tree and tasks them with maintaining its sacred moonwells. Through his lessons, he reveals both the spiritual importance of Teldrassil and the growing burdens carried by the kaldorei.",h="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Scholar of Dolanaar",b="Residing in the shaded settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage serves as an instructor to travelers leaving the sheltered bounds of Shadowglen. As young kaldorei venture into the wider boughs of Teldrassil, Corithras ensures they understand the history of their new home. He teaches that survival in this changing era requires vigilance and reverence for the natural order.",sp=0},{t="Crown of the Earth",b="Much of Corithras's duty revolves around overseeing the ritual purification of the Crown of the Earth. He directs adventurers to collect pure waters from moonwells across Teldrassil and cleanse sacred phials throughout the forest. Through these trials, he monitors the health of the World Tree and seeks to maintain the delicate balance of the wilderness against creeping corruption.",sp=0},{t="The Burden of the Kaldorei",b="Beneath Corithras's guidance lies an uneasy truth regarding Teldrassil's creation. Unlike the ancient Nordrassil, this new World Tree was raised without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, who refused Fandral Staghelm's ambitious creation. Corithras reflects on the loss of night elven immortality and the fragile, uncertain future the kaldorei now face under the boughs of an unblessed bough.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar located in Dolanaar. He introduces adventurers to the history of Teldrassil and tasks them with tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the waters of the World Tree.",al={"corithras moonrage role","who is corithras","dolanaar quest giver"}},{q="Where can Corithras Moonrage be found?",a="He can be found standing outdoors in Dolanaar, the central crossroads village situated in the southern reaches of Teldrassil.",al={"corithras location","where is corithras","find corithras"}},{q="What is the Crown of the Earth questline about?",a="The Crown of the Earth quests involve drawing water from various moonwells scattered across Teldrassil and applying it to sacred groves. Corithras uses these rituals to observe the vitality and purity of the boughs.",al={"crown of the earth meaning","corithras quests","moonwell quests"}},{q="Why is Corithras concerned about Teldrassil's origins?",a="Corithras shares the history of how Teldrassil was planted after the Third War to restore night elven immortality. Because the Dragon Aspects refused to bless the tree, Corithras remains acutely aware that the tree lacks divine protection and that his people remain mortal.",al={"why burden of kaldorei","aspects refusal","why no immortality"}},{q="What does Corithras teach new adventurers?",a="He imparts lessons on the recent sacrifices of the Third War, the founding of Teldrassil, and the responsibility each kaldorei bears to defend their new woodland home.",al={"corithras lore","dolanaar history","what does corithras tell you"}},{q="Is Corithras aligned with the Cenarion Circle or Darnassus?",a="He serves as a loyal citizen and scholar of Darnassus in Dolanaar, working closely with druids and priests alike to monitor the well-being of the forest and its waters.",al={"corithras faction","is corithras a druid"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, speaking with Corithras is a foundational lesson in the post-Third War reality, confronting the loss of ancient immortality and the disputed creation of Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Corithras's tasks deeply connected to their calling, as his moonwell rites directly track the health and creeping ailments of the World Tree.",["class:Priest"]="Priests of Elune assist Corithras in carrying the blessed waters of the moonwells, maintaining the spiritual and physical harmony of Dolanaar's surrounding wilds."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","kaldorei","moonwell","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:929","quest:7383","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Corithras Moonrage"}}
E["npc:dazalar"] = {t="npc",n="Dazalar",z="teldrassil",s="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer stationed in Dolanaar within Teldrassil. He guides fledgling sentinels and scouts as they hone their marksmanship and learn the sacred art of bonding with the wild beasts of the great boughs.",h="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer stationed in Dolanaar within Teldrassil.",sec={{t="The Dolanaar Encampment",b="Standing within the settlement of Dolanaar, Dazalar serves as a primary mentor for young hunters venturing beyond the sheltered glade of Shadowglen. Night elf society relies heavily on its rangers and sentinels to patrol the wilderness, and Dazalar ensures newcomers possess the discipline and patience necessary to protect Teldrassil's fragile ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="A critical rite of passage under Dazalar's guidance is learning to tame and care for beasts. Rather than bending creatures to a hunter's whim through sheer force, the Kaldorei way emphasizes forming a mutual pact with forest predators like nightsabers, owls, and strigid hunters, training them to fight alongside their masters with respect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dazalar?",a="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer located in the village of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. He teaches novice hunters new combat abilities and guides them in the ways of taming wild beasts.",al={"who is dazalar","dazalar lore","dazalar identity"}},{q="Where can I find Dazalar?",a="He is stationed outdoors in Dolanaar, the central hub of Teldrassil that adventurers reach shortly after leaving the starting grounds of Shadowglen.",al={"dazalar location","where is dazalar","dolanaar hunter trainer"}},{q="What training does Dazalar provide?",a="Dazalar teaches various ranged attacks, traps, and survival techniques suitable for developing hunters, and he sends novices on trials to master the taming of wilderness animals.",al={"what does dazalar teach","dazalar skills","hunter training dazalar"}},{q="Does Dazalar offer any special quests?",a="Yes, Dazalar offers pivotal hunter training quests, including The Hunter's Path, the multi-part trial Taming the Beast, and Training the Beast, which teach young hunters how to bond with and maintain animal companions.",al={"dazalar quests","hunter quests dolanaar","taming the beast quest"}},{q="Why do night elves rely so heavily on hunters?",a="For millennia, the Kaldorei have lived in harmony with the ancient forests of Kalimdor. Archers and scouts form the backbone of the Sentinel army, utilizing stealth, marksmanship, and animal allies to safeguard their lands without disrupting nature.",al={"night elf hunters lore","why sentinels use hunters","kaldorei hunters"}},{q="What kind of beasts does Dazalar send hunters to tame?",a="He directs hunters to track down native Teldrassil fauna, including local spiders, nightsabers, and birds of prey, testing the hunter's ability to approach and calm wild predators.",al={"what beasts to tame","dolanaar taming trial","tame beasts teldrassil"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Dazalar is one of the earliest mentors a night elf hunter encounters, guiding them through the foundational trials of beast mastery and pet training.",["race:NightElf"]="He upholds the traditions of the Kaldorei sentinels and scouts, teaching young night elves how to live in balance with nature's fierce predators."},kw={"dazalar","dolanaar","hunter","night elf","taming the beast","teldrassil","the hunter's path","trainer"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:6061","quest:6065","quest:6081","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Dazalar"}}
E["npc:denalan"] = {t="npc",n="Denalan",z="teldrassil",s="Denalan is an accomplished night elf herbalist and botanist who tends a quiet lakeside plot along the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth. Working under a simple awning, he devotes his days to studying the island's plant life and seeking botanical remedies for the strange corruption affecting Teldrassil. He frequently enlists young adventurers to gather samples, study violent timberlings, and test enchanted soils.",h="Denalan is an accomplished night elf herbalist and botanist who tends a quiet lakeside plot along the eastern...",sec={{t="A Botanist at Lake Al'Ameth",b="While many kaldorei focus on martial vigilance or high druidic rites, Denalan pursues the patient, meticulous craft of herbalism. Stationed along the tranquil eastern banks of Lake Al'Ameth, he has established a modest research camp consisting of a cloth awning, simple field tools, and tidy rows of cultivated planter boxes. Rather than retreating to the grand barrows of Darnassus, he prefers to remain close to the loam, directly examining the unusual flora that has sprouted since the planting of the new World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Teldrassil's Blemishes",b="Denalan's research is far more than an academic curiosity; it addresses the growing unrest among Teldrassil's native wildlife. The timberlings, normally docile woodland beings of wood and sprout, have turned increasingly aggressive. Denalan enchants specialized soil to nurse wild seeds in captivity and analyze how malignant forces seep into the root systems. By studying strange specimens like shimmering fronds, glowing fruit, and moss-twined growths, he seeks to isolate whatever dark taint is troubling the forest boughs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Denalan?",a="Denalan is located on the eastern bank of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil, just east of Shadowglen and south of Dolanaar. He maintains a small camp with an awning and several cultivated planting beds right near the water's edge.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan","denalan map"}},{q="What is Denalan researching at his campsite?",a="Denalan is an herbalist studying the unusual flora of Teldrassil and the aggressive behavior of local woodland spirits. He uses enchanted planter boxes to grow timberling seeds, analyze curious wild plant specimens, and find ways to cleanse corruption seeping into the new World Tree's ecosystem.",al={"what does denalan do","denalan purpose","why is denalan at the lake"}},{q="Why are the timberlings attacking people?",a="Timberlings are plant-like nature spirits native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Normally peaceful parts of the forest ecology, they have become violent and erratic due to an unnatural corruption spreading through the soil and roots of the World Tree, prompting researchers like Denalan to investigate their seeds.",al={"why are timberlings aggressive","timberling lore","corrupted timberlings"}},{q="What are Denalan's planter boxes used for?",a="Denalan keeps specially prepared planter beds filled with enchanted earth. He uses them to cultivate wild seeds and strange botanical cuttings, allowing him to safely observe how the forest's flora reacts to purified soil away from wild contaminants.",al={"denalan planter","denalans earth","denalan dirt boxes"}},{q="Who does Denalan work with?",a="Denalan has worked closely with fellow herbalists such as Sylvia Whisperbloom and stays in regular communication with druidic researchers and scholars across Teldrassil, including Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.",al={"denalan allies","who does denalan report to"}},{q="What is the Moss-twined Heart that Denalan examines?",a="The Moss-twined Heart is a blighted botanical core recovered from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling in Teldrassil. Denalan studies it in his enchanted soil to understand the unnatural sickness twisting the island's plant life.",al={"moss twined heart","moss-twined heart quest","blackmoss heart"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan exemplifies the kaldorei tradition of botanical study, demonstrating how gathering and cultivating wild plants can diagnose deeper ailments in the natural world.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common cause with Denalan's lakeside experiments, as his work directly assists the Cenarion Circle's efforts to trace and purge the taint spreading through Teldrassil's roots.",["race:NightElf"]="Denalan's research at Lake Al'Ameth represents early kaldorei attempts to understand the unexpected flaws and growing pains of their new home, Teldrassil."},kw={"blackmoss","botany","denalan","herbalist","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","planter","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:997","quest:918","quest:919","quest:927","quest:941","quest:922"},src={"Denalan"}}
E["npc:elder-bladeleaf"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Bladeleaf",z="teldrassil",s="Elder Bladeleaf is an honored night elf ancestral spirit who appears in Dolanaar during the Lunar Festival. Revering the ancestors is a core aspect of the festival, and Bladeleaf welcomes travelers wishing to pay their respects beneath the canopy of Teldrassil.",h="Elder Bladeleaf is an honored night elf ancestral spirit who appears in Dolanaar during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit of Dolanaar",b="Standing amidst the trees of Dolanaar, Elder Bladeleaf manifests as a spectral ancestor during the Lunar Festival. Night elves hold their forebears in high regard, and during this auspicious season, the barrier between the living and the honored dead thins. Bladeleaf bestows blessings and festival tokens upon any who seek him out in friendship, offering a quiet reminder of the wisdom and longevity carried within night elf heritage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Bladeleaf?",a="Elder Bladeleaf is a night elf ancestral spirit who manifests in Dolanaar during the annual Lunar Festival. He exists to share wisdom, receive the honor of visiting adventurers, and offer traditional festival tokens.",al={"elder bladeleaf lore","who is bladeleaf","bladeleaf ghost"}},{q="Why is Elder Bladeleaf only here sometimes?",a="Elder Bladeleaf is tied to the Lunar Festival, a time when spirits and ancestors across Azeroth return to walk among the living. When the festival concludes, his spirit returns to the realm beyond until the next cycle.",al={"where is elder bladeleaf","can't find elder bladeleaf","is bladeleaf seasonal"}},{q="Is Elder Bladeleaf related to the other Bladeleafs in Dolanaar?",a="Given that several living night elves in Dolanaar—such as Syral Bladeleaf—share his surname, he is believed to be an ancient forebear of their family line watching over his kin's modern settlement.",al={"syral bladeleaf related","bladeleaf family","hannah bladeleaf relation"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Honoring Elder Bladeleaf is a sacred observance in your homelands, connecting you to ancient forebears who walked Kalimdor long before Teldrassil was grown.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers visiting Teldrassil during the Lunar Festival can easily pay homage to Elder Bladeleaf just outside the barrow dens of Dolanaar."},kw={"ancestor","bladeleaf the elder","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","lunar festival","spirit","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:8715","subzone:dolanaar","npc:syral-bladeleaf","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Elder Bladeleaf"}}
E["npc:fandral-staghelm"] = {t="npc",n="Fandral Staghelm",z="teldrassil",s="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Stepping into power after Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream, he championed the planting of the new World Tree, Teldrassil. Proud, abrasive, and relentlessly ambitious, Fandral advocates for an aggressive Kaldorei resurgence that frequently pits him against High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",h="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",sec={{t="Architect of Teldrassil",b="Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil atop Mount Hyjal, the night elves lost their immortality and their sacred sanctuary. While Malfurion Stormrage cautioned patience and warned against vanity, Fandral championed the bold creation of a new World Tree off the coast of Kalimdor. When Malfurion subsequently fell comatose within the Emerald Dream, Fandral seized the initiative and led the druids in raising Teldrassil. He envisioned the colossal bough as a monument to Kaldorei endurance and a vessel to restore their lost supremacy, even though the Dragon Aspects pointedly withheld their blessings from the unapproved endeavor.",sp=0},{t="Tragedy in the Shifting Sands",b="A millennium before the First War, Fandral served as the Kaldorei field commander in Silithus during the War of the Shifting Sands. Renowned among the insectoid qiraji as 'Kar'sis'—the Hand of Earth—he held the front lines alongside his beloved only son, Valstann. Exploiting Fandral's devotion, the qiraji General Rajaxx engineered a feint against Southwind Village and captured Valstann, ruthlessly executing him directly in front of the horrified Archdruid. The loss shattered Fandral's spirit, precipitating a devastating retreat and cementing an abiding, bitter hatred for the swarm that remains etched into his haughty demeanor.",sp=0},{t="Rivalry and Hubris",b="Within the marble boughs of Darnassus, Fandral governs Kaldorei affairs with a haughty, unyielding hand. Unlike High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, who favors spiritual preservation and cautious diplomacy, Fandral views military expansion and decisive strength as paramount to the survival of their people. His past is rife with perilous overreach: millennia ago, he secretly grafted Nordrassil's branches across Azeroth—including Andrassil in the Grizzly Hills—to smother saronite growths, only for the roots to breach an Old God prison and introduce deep rot into the dreamways. Despite such catastrophes, Staghelm remains thoroughly unrepentant.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fandral Staghelm?",a="Fandral Staghelm is the acting Archdruid of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus, presiding over Kaldorei druids in Malfurion Stormrage's absence. Known for his fiery temperament and imperial ambitions, he is the primary visionary behind the creation of Teldrassil.",al={"fandral lore","who is the archdruid","archdruid of darnassus"}},{q="Why doesn't Fandral get along with Tyrande?",a="Fandral advocates for Kaldorei military resurgence, aggressive expansion, and reclaiming lost immortality. Tyrande Whisperwind pursues cautious spiritual guidance through Elune. Their competing visions for the night elves' post-Hyjal future spark fierce political friction within Darnassus.",al={"fandral and tyrande","why do druids and priestesses disagree","staghelm vs whisperwind"}},{q="Why was Teldrassil planted against Malfurion's wishes?",a="Malfurion believed planting a replacement for Nordrassil was an act of hubris that nature would not condone. When Malfurion vanished into his coma, Fandral rallied the remaining druids to plant Teldrassil regardless, seeking to restore Kaldorei power and reclaim their lost immortality.",al={"who created teldrassil","why did fandral plant teldrassil","origin of teldrassil"}},{q="What happened to Fandral's son?",a="During the War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus, Fandral's son Valstann was lured into an ambush at Southwind Village. The qiraji General Rajaxx captured Valstann and slaughtered him in front of Fandral, leaving the Archdruid grief-stricken and permanently embittered.",al={"fandral son","who was valstann","valstann staghelm"}},{q="What was Andrassil?",a="Thousands of years ago, Fandral stole branches from Nordrassil and planted them without Cenarion approval to quarantine saronite. The grandest was Andrassil in Northrend. Its roots burrowed into the Old God Yogg-Saron's prison, corrupting the land and forcing the druids to fell it as Vordrassil.",al={"crown of the snow","vordrassil","first tree planted by fandral"}},{q="Where can Fandral Staghelm be found?",a="Fandral stands atop the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, surrounded by his loyal druids and overseeable business of the Kaldorei capital.",al={"where is fandral","fandral location","cenarion enclave leader"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Staghelm commands the Darnassian druids, pushing the Cenarion Circle toward direct worldly authority while clashing with the traditional teachings of the sleeping Malfurion Stormrage.",["race:NightElf"]="As one of Darnassus's primary leaders, Fandral embodies Kaldorei pride and fury, driving the settlement of Teldrassil even as ordinary citizens feel the rift between his enclave and the Temple of the Moon.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though Teldrassil serves as an Alliance bastion in northern Kalimdor, Staghelm views the younger races with thinly veiled disdain, tolerating their presence only as political expediency demands."},kw={"andrassil","cenarion circle","darnassus","fandral","malfurion","rajaxx","shifting sands","staghelm","teldrassil","valstann"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:cenarion-circle","npc:malfurion-stormrage","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:southwind-village","zone:silithus","topic:nordrassil"},src={"Fandral Staghelm"}}
E["npc:gaerolas-talvethren"] = {t="npc",n="Gaerolas Talvethren",z="teldrassil",s="Gaerolas Talvethren is a night elf sentinel standing watch over the ruins of Starbreeze Village in Teldrassil. Appointed as the protector of the Sleeping druids, he seeks aid in confronting the aggressive furbolgs and dark corruption unsettling the boughs.",h="Gaerolas Talvethren is a night elf sentinel standing watch over the ruins of Starbreeze Village in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Sleeping",b="Positioned amid the troubled settlement of Starbreeze Village, Gaerolas Talvethren bears the solemn mantle of protecting the Sleeping druids who slumber in communion with the Emerald Dream. His vigilance has grown fraught as unnatural corruption creeps through the forest, unsettling the balance of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Menace",b="Gaerolas directs travelers to push back against the Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs, whose minds have turned to madness and savagery. By investigating the taint spreading from their shamans and finding the roots of their distress, he hopes to preserve what sanctity remains in eastern Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="He is a night elf defender stationed at Starbreeze Village, charged with safeguarding the slumbering druids and investigating the strange corruption afflicting the area.",al={"gaerolas","who is gaerolas","gaerolas role"}},{q="Where can I find Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="He is located in Starbreeze Village, in the eastern boughs of Teldrassil, east of Dolanaar.",al={"gaerolas location","where is gaerolas talvethren","find gaerolas"}},{q="Who are 'the Sleeping' that Gaerolas protects?",a="The Sleeping refers to the night elf druids who entered long slumbers in barrows and sanctuaries to traverse the Emerald Dream, leaving their physical forms vulnerable to physical harm.",al={"the sleeping","who are the sleeping","sleeping druids"}},{q="What threats is Gaerolas concerned about?",a="He is deeply troubled by the corruption afflicting the local wildlife and the sudden, maddened hostility of the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe.",al={"starbreeze threats","gaerolas quests","gnarlpine trouble"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves departing Dolanaar, assisting Gaerolas offers a sobering look at how deeply the taint has penetrated Teldrassil's sacred boughs.",["class:Druid"]="Gaerolas's duty as guardian of the slumbering druids makes aiding his efforts a personal matter of protecting fellow practitioners of the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"a troubling breeze","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine corruption","starbreeze village","teldrassil","the sleeping"},rel={"subzone:starbreeze-village","quest:475","quest:476","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Gaerolas Talvethren"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-keldamyr"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Keldamyr",z="teldrassil",s="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages the hearth and lodgings of the central inn in Dolanaar, Teldrassil. He offers food, drink, and a resting place for young night elves venturing forth from Shadowglen into the wider boughs of the World Tree.",h="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages the hearth and lodgings of the central inn in Dolanaar, Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Hearth of Dolanaar",b="Dolanaar is the primary village newcomers reach after departing the sheltered glade of Aldrassil. Innkeeper Keldamyr maintains the community's central haven, providing bread, spring water, and soft beds beneath the canopy of Teldrassil. Travelers, sentinels, and young novices bound for Darnassus frequently pause at his counter to rest their spirits, secure their hearthstones, and stock rations for the journey through the boughs.",sp=0},{t="Town Deliveries",b="Running an inn high within the branches requires steady supply lines from nearby settlements and tradesfolk. Local couriers often find themselves directed straight to Keldamyr's desk to drop off goods, linking him directly into the daily trade and logistics keeping the settlement of Dolanaar running smoothly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Keldamyr is located inside the main inn building at the heart of Dolanaar, the first major settlement south of Shadowglen on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"keldamyr location","where is keldamyr","dolanaar innkeeper location"}},{q="What services does Innkeeper Keldamyr offer?",a="He serves as the local innkeeper, meaning you can bind your Hearthstone to his hearth, purchase basic provisions such as water, milk, juice, and bread, or log out rested beneath his roof.",al={"keldamyr wares","what does keldamyr sell","dolanaar inn food"}},{q="What quests involve Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="He is the recipient of the local courier task 'Dolanaar Delivery,' receiving parcels meant for the upkeep and supply of the settlement's inn.",al={"keldamyr quests","dolanaar delivery turn in"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves freshly setting out from the training grounds of Shadowglen, Keldamyr's inn is usually the very first home away from home where they bind their hearthstones."},kw={"dolanaar","hearthstone","inn","innkeeper","keldamyr","night elf","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:2159","topic:night-elf"},src={"Innkeeper Keldamyr"}}
E["npc:jocaste"] = {t="npc",n="Jocaste",z="teldrassil",s="Jocaste is a night elf hunter trainer residing within the verdant Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Working alongside the Cenarion Circle, she mentors young night elf marksmen and beastmasters who arrive from the wilds of Teldrassil.",h="Jocaste is a night elf hunter trainer residing within the verdant Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.",sec={{t="A Mentor in the Enclave",b="Stationed among the tranquil groves of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, Jocaste serves as an instructor for night elf hunters. When fledgling trackers finish their initial training in Shadowglen and venture into the capital city, Jocaste guides their transition into seasoned survivalists. She teaches the arts of marksmanship, wilderness survival, and the sacred bond between a hunter and the wild beasts of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jocaste?",a="Jocaste is a night elf hunter trainer located within the Cenarion Enclave in the capital city of Darnassus, offering instruction and guidance to practitioners of the hunt.",al={"jocaste lore","who is jocaste","jocaste darnassus"}},{q="Where can I find Jocaste?",a="She can be found among the trees and pavilions of the Cenarion Enclave, in the northwest district of Darnassus on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"jocaste location","where is jocaste","jocaste spot"}},{q="What role does she play for young hunters?",a="Hunters directed to Darnassus seek her out to advance their discipline through tasks like The Hunter's Path and learn how to properly train and master wild beasts.",al={"jocaste quests","the hunter's path jocaste","training the beast"}},{q="Is Jocaste affiliated with the Cenarion Circle?",a="Yes. While training hunters rather than druids, she operates within the Cenarion Enclave and explicitly welcomes visiting hunters into the presence of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"is jocaste cenarion circle","jocaste faction"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For night elf hunters stepping into Darnassus for the first time, Jocaste is a key teacher who refines your combat techniques and helps solidify the bond with your animal companions.",["race:NightElf"]="Rooted in the Cenarion Enclave, Jocaste reflects the close harmony between night elf wayfarers, the wild beasts of Teldrassil, and the teachings of the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","hunter trainer","jocaste","night elf hunter","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:cenarion-enclave","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:night-elf","zone:teldrassil","quest:6065","quest:6081"},src={"Jocaste"}}
E["npc:laurna-morninglight"] = {t="npc",n="Laurna Morninglight",z="teldrassil",s="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priest trainer residing in the tranquil settlement of Dolanaar within Teldrassil. Devoted to the Sisterhood of Elune, she guides budding acolytes emerging from Shadowglen in the spiritual rites and healing graces of the Moon Goddess. Her teachings prepare young night elf priests for the growing threats encroaching on the boughs of the World Tree.",h="Laurna Morninglight is a night elf priest trainer residing in the tranquil settlement of Dolanaar within...",sec={{t="A Guide in Dolanaar",b="Situated amidst the boughs of Dolanaar, Laurna Morninglight serves as one of the primary mentors for young priests who have completed their initial rites in Shadowglen. As new initiates step out into the broader reaches of Teldrassil, she instructs them on expanding their communion with Elune, balancing the light of healing with defensive rites necessary to survive an increasingly hostile wild.",sp=0},{t="Devotion to the Moon Goddess",b="Priestcraft among the kaldorei is deeply intertwined with the worship of Elune rather than the abstract Holy Light revered by humans and dwarves. Laurna tasks her students with spiritual labors such as receiving sacred robes and communing directly with lunar shrines. Through these traditions, acolytes learn that their powers are direct gifts of the Mother Moon, meant to preserve and mend the kaldorei people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight is stationed in the village of Dolanaar, located in the central reaches of Teldrassil just down the road from Shadowglen.",al={"laurna location","where is laurna","dolanaar priest trainer"}},{q="What does Laurna Morninglight do?",a="She is a priest trainer for night elf characters. She teaches new spells, refines ranks of known abilities, and provides early guidance through class-specific rites.",al={"what does she do","laurna role","laurna priest trainer"}},{q="What kind of quests does she offer?",a="She initiates class quests for fledgling priests, directing them to aid wounded allies and seek Elune's divine favor through ceremonial vestments and prayers.",al={"laurna quests","priest quests dolanaar"}},{q="Does she train other races?",a="While she is culturally rooted in the Sisterhood of Elune, priest trainers in the Alliance will instruct any allied priest who comes seeking spiritual discipline.",al={"can humans train here","priest trainer any race"}},{q="Is she affiliated with the Temple of the Moon?",a="Yes, as a kaldorei priestess, her vows and magic are dedicated entirely to the Goddess Elune and the broader traditions overseen by the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.",al={"is she sisterhood of elune","laurna temple of the moon"}},{q="Does she share a family name with other night elves?",a="She shares the surname Morninglight with Norana Morninglight, an innkeeper serving the kaldorei elsewhere on the continent.",al={"morninglight family","laurna relatives"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For night elf priests arriving from Shadowglen, Laurna Morninglight is your first major mentor outside the starting vale, teaching foundational spells and guiding your early devotion to Elune.",["race:NightElf"]="Laurna embodies the traditional kaldorei devotion to the Moon Goddess, reminding adventurers that priestcraft in Teldrassil draws from Elune rather than the Holy Light."},kw={"dolanaar","elune","kaldorei","laurna","morninglight","priest trainer","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","quest:5621","quest:5622","quest:5634","quest:5628"},src={"Laurna Morninglight"}}
E["npc:moon-priestess-amara"] = {t="npc",n="Moon Priestess Amara",z="teldrassil",s="Moon Priestess Amara is a night elf priestess stationed along the main road west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Flanked by loyal huntress guards, she keeps watch over the woodland pathways connecting the heart of the bough to the capital city of Darnassus.",h="Moon Priestess Amara is a night elf priestess stationed along the main road west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Boughways",b="Stationed at a quiet wayside post west of Dolanaar, Moon Priestess Amara represents both the spiritual authority of the Sisterhood of Elune and the practical vigilance required to keep Teldrassil's roadways secure. She travels and watches with two huntress companions, Nhemai and Yaeliura. To travelers journeying westward, Amara acts as a guiding hand, directing adventurers along the road toward Darnassus and tasking those with burdened spirits to seek out paths of redemption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Moon Priestess Amara?",a="Moon Priestess Amara, also known in sentinel duties as Amara Nightwalker, is a priestess of the Sisterhood of Elune stationed on the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus in Teldrassil. She oversees the security and spiritual health of travelers heading through the bough.",al={"who is amara","priestess amara","sentinel amara nightwalker"}},{q="Where can I find Moon Priestess Amara?",a="She is located along the paved highway just west of Dolanaar in Teldrassil, standing watch beside two sentinel huntresses.",al={"where is amara","amara location","priestess amara map"}},{q="Who are the huntresses standing with her?",a="She is guarded and accompanied by Huntress Nhemai and Huntress Yaeliura, two night elf sentinels who assist in protecting the thoroughfare from beasts and hostile corruption.",al={"amara companions","nhemai and yaeliura","amara guards"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a member of the Sisterhood of Elune, Priestess Amara embodies the night elven devotion to the Moon Goddess, serving as a pastoral and spiritual guide to young acolytes venturing out from Shadowglen.",["race:NightElf"]="Amara marks an important milestone on your journey away from Dolanaar, offering guidance and tasks that lead into the great city of Darnassus."},kw={"amara nightwalker","dolanaar","elanaria","moon priestess amara","nhemai","teldrassil","the road to darnassus","yaeliura"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","npc:elanaria","quest:487","quest:489","topic:night-elf"},src={"Moon Priestess Amara"}}
E["npc:oben-rageclaw"] = {t="npc",n="Oben Rageclaw",z="teldrassil",s="Oben Rageclaw is the restless spirit of a night elf druid haunting the corrupted depths of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil. While his spirit wanders trapped in the barrow den, his slumbering physical form has fallen under the sway of foul furbolg magic.",h="Oben Rageclaw is the restless spirit of a night elf druid haunting the corrupted depths of the Ban'ethil...",sec={{t="A Slumber Desecrated",b="Like many Druids of the Claw, Oben Rageclaw retreated into the subterranean sanctum of Ban'ethil Barrow Den to commune with nature and wander the Emerald Dream. However, when the native Gnarlpine furbolgs fell to corruption and overran the barrows, Oben was caught entirely defenseless in his trance. Rather than simply slaying him, the corrupted Gnarlpine shaman used dark rituals to seize control of his comatose mortal frame, leaving his displaced spirit lingering as an anguished ghost unable to pass on or wake.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Vessel",b="Unable to reclaim his own flesh from the shaman's enthrallment, Oben relies on travelers navigating the dangerous tunnels to end his torment. Only by locating and destroying his puppeted physical body can his mortal ties be severed. Once his hijacked vessel is slain, Oben's tortured ghost is finally released from the subterranean gloom to find eternal rest within the Emerald Dream.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben Rageclaw is a night elf Druid of the Claw whose ghost haunts Ban'ethil Barrow Den in Teldrassil after being severed from his physical body by corrupted furbolgs.",al={"who is oben","oben rageclaw lore","spirit in barrow den"}},{q="Why is Oben Rageclaw a ghost?",a="While Oben slept in a deep druidic trance communing with the Emerald Dream, Gnarlpine furbolg shamans infiltrated the den and cast foul magic on his body, taking control of it and trapping his spirit outside as an apparition.",al={"why is oben dead","how did oben die","why is oben a ghost"}},{q="Where is Oben's physical body?",a="His physical body lies deeper within the winding corridors of Ban'ethil Barrow Den, guarded and manipulated by the Gnarlpine shamans who corrupted the den.",al={"find oben body","where is oben body","sleeping druid location"}},{q="What happens after Oben's body is destroyed?",a="Destroying his puppeted body breaks the Gnarlpine shamans' dark hold over him, allowing his spirit to peacefully depart Teldrassil and rest forever in the Emerald Dream.",al={"oben fate","what happens to oben spirit","saving oben"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Oben's fate is a harrowing reminder of the vulnerability of druids during their trance-like communion with the Emerald Dream when sacred barrow dens are left undefended.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Oben Rageclaw by the Gnarlpine furbolgs illustrates just how deeply corruption has tainted Teldrassil's native denizens and sacred sanctuaries."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","druid of the claw","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:2541","quest:2561","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf"},src={"Oben Rageclaw"}}
E["npc:orenthil-whisperwind"] = {t="npc",n="Orenthil Whisperwind",z="teldrassil",s="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf resident of Teldrassil, commonly encountered resting under the boughs of Dolanaar. He serves as an welcoming liaison for rare travelers, presenting gifts sent across the world to newly arrived champions. Given his prominent surname, many wonder whether he shares kinship with High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind herself.",h="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf resident of Teldrassil, commonly encountered resting under the boughs of...",sec={{t="A Friendly Face in Teldrassil",b="Standing amidst the shaded terraces of Dolanaar, Orenthil Whisperwind offers a quiet welcome to fledgling adventurers emerging from Shadowglen. While he remains modest and keeps mostly to himself beneath the canopy of the World Tree, he is notably tasked with greeting select travelers and delivering special companion creatures to those carrying rare tokens from abroad.",sp=0},{t="The Whisperwind Line",b="Bearing the name Whisperwind immediately invites speculation in night elven lands. While Orenthil has never made grand claims of nobility or spiritual authority, his surname suggests potential ties to High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. Whether he belongs to an extended branch of her ancestral line or merely shares an ancient Kaldorei family name remains a point of quiet curiosity among passing travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="He is a night elf found in Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He serves as a welcoming figure for adventurers setting out into the boughs of the World Tree.",al={"orenthil","orenthil whisperwind info","who is this elf"}},{q="Is Orenthil related to Tyrande Whisperwind?",a="His surname suggests he may be part of the extended family or ancestral lineage of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, though he does not flaunt high station or claim direct power in Darnassus.",al={"orenthil tyrande brother","tyrande relative","is he related to tyrande"}},{q="Where can I find Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="Orenthil resides in Dolanaar, the first major settlement night elf adventurers encounter after departing Shadowglen in central Teldrassil.",al={"orenthil location","where is orenthil","orenthil map"}},{q="What quest does Orenthil offer?",a="He offers the quest 'Welcome!', which allows travelers bearing special collector tokens to claim an exotic companion pet to accompany them on their journeys.",al={"orenthil quest","welcome quest dolanaar","collector quest teldrassil"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Meeting a Kaldorei who shares the name of High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind in humble Dolanaar serves as an early reminder of the sprawling, ancient history behind Kalimdor's elven bloodlines."},kw={"collector","dolanaar","orenthil","shadowglen","teldrassil","welcome","whisperwind"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:5805","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","subzone:shadowglen","topic:night-elf"},src={"Orenthil Whisperwind"}}
E["npc:saelienne"] = {t="npc",n="Saelienne",z="teldrassil",s="Innkeeper Saelienne manages the inn situated on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. She provides weary travelers and local artisans with food, drink, and a peaceful hearthstone retreat in the heart of the night elven capital.",h="Innkeeper Saelienne manages the inn situated on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus.",sec={{t="Hospitality on the Terrace",b="Situated amidst the bustling workshops and trade stalls of the Craftsmen's Terrace, Innkeeper Saelienne offers a calm respite for both residents and visitors to Darnassus. As a keeper of the hearth, she caters to adventurers arriving from across Kalimdor and beyond, serving staple night elven refreshments alongside goods brought into the city port. Her establishment serves as a primary gathering place for tradesfolk seeking rest after long hours at the forge or loom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Saelienne?",a="Saelienne is located on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, running the local inn tucked among the trade trainers and crafting shops.",al={"saelienne location","where is saelienne","darnassus innkeeper location","craftsmens terrace inn"}},{q="What services does Saelienne provide?",a="She acts as an innkeeper, allowing players to bind their Hearthstone to Darnassus. She also sells various food and drink items suitable for restoring health and mana.",al={"what does saelienne do","saelienne vendor","bind hearthstone darnassus"}},{q="Does Saelienne offer any seasonal tasks?",a="During the Hallow's End festivities, Saelienne participates in holiday celebrations, offering Alliance adventurers the quest Dancing for Marzipan in exchange for holiday treats.",al={"saelienne quests","hallows end saelienne","dancing for marzipan"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elf adventurers returning from the wild reaches of Teldrassil, Saelienne's inn offers a familiar hearth among the artisans of Darnassus.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance envoys and tradesfolk traveling to the remote canopy of Teldrassil rely on Saelienne for food, drink, and a warm hearthstone sanctuary."},kw={"craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","hallow's end","hearthstone","innkeeper","saelienne","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:darnassus","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:8357","topic:alliance"},src={"Saelienne"}}
E["npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak"] = {t="npc",n="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",z="teldrassil",s="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf guardian stationed within the serene groves of the Oracle Glade on Teldrassil. Charged with monitoring the sacred balance of the northern boughs, she keeps a wary watch over the glade's enchanted waters and woodland wildlife.",h="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf guardian stationed within the serene groves of the Oracle Glade on...",sec={{t="Watcher of the Oracle Glade",b="Arynia Cloudsbreak serves the Sentinel army in one of the most secluded and mystical reaches of Teldrassil: the Oracle Glade. Amid ancient trees and ethereal springs, she carries out her watch far from the bustling avenues of Darnassus, ensuring the sanctity of the wilderness remains undisturbed.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Glade",b="Despite Teldrassil's sacred birth, creeping disharmony has begun to unsettle its creatures. Arynia relies on passing adventurers and young night elves to investigate local disruptions, such as strange behaviors among the glade's wildlife and mystical phenomena around the enchanted springs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="She is a night elf Sentinel standing guard in the Oracle Glade, deep in northern Teldrassil. She looks after the mystical glade and recruits travelers to assist in preserving its natural harmony.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","who is arynia","sentinel arynia"}},{q="Where can Arynia Cloudsbreak be found?",a="Arynia is stationed out in the open at the Oracle Glade, located in the northwestern reaches of Teldrassil, north of Dolanaar.",al={"arynia location","where is arynia","arynia cloudsbreak map"}},{q="What duties does she perform in the Sentinels?",a="As a Sentinel stationed in the wilderness, she patrols the outlying forest boughs, monitoring the local spirits, wildlife, and natural phenomena for any signs of corruption or imbalance.",al={"arynia role","what does arynia do"}},{q="Is she related to anyone else on Teldrassil?",a="She shares her surname with Mavoris Cloudsbreak, suggesting a familial bond among the night elves dwelling on the world tree.",al={"arynia family","mavoris cloudsbreak"}},{q="What tasks does she give to adventurers?",a="She offers tasks that involve investigating the enchanted glade and tending to mysterious disturbances and wandering beasts nearby, including aiding creatures caught in distress.",al={"arynia quests","oracle glade quests"}},{q="Why is the Oracle Glade significant to the night elves?",a="The Oracle Glade is a sacred sanctuary within Teldrassil known for its tranquil pools and spiritual reverence, overseen by druids and Sentinels seeking guidance and omen from nature.",al={"why oracle glade","oracle glade lore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves coming of age on Teldrassil, assisting Sentinel Cloudsbreak offers practical experience in protecting the wild balance of their new homeland.",["faction:Alliance"]="Arynia represents the vigilance of the Kaldorei Sentinels, maintaining defense over the Alliance's vital woodland stronghold in Kalimdor."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","enchanted glade","kaldorei","mist","night elf","oracle glade","sentinel","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","quest:937","quest:938","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak"}}
E["npc:shanda"] = {t="npc",n="Shanda",z="teldrassil",s="Shanda is a night elf priestess and mentor located within the hollow trunk of Aldrassil in Shadowglen. Serving the Sisterhood of Elune, she instructs novice night elf priests in the fundamental prayers, wards, and rites of the Moon Goddess. Her guidance helps fledgling acolytes balance the light of Elune with their duties in defending Teldrassil.",h="Shanda is a night elf priestess and mentor located within the hollow trunk of Aldrassil in Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Acolyte of the Moon Mother",b="Standing within the tranquil sanctuary of Aldrassil, Shanda serves as one of the first spiritual guides for young night elves dedicated to Elune. While the druids tend to the waking roots and boughs of Teldrassil, priestesses like Shanda ensure that the spiritual heart of the Kaldorei remains tethered to the White Lady. She instructs new initiates on channeling lunar grace for healing and protective wards, preparing them to face the corruption creeping into the boughs of the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Guiding New Initiates",b="When young priests awaken to their calling in Shadowglen, they are directed to Shanda to prove their devotion and learn their first prayers. Through rites such as In Favor of Elune, she tests their resolve and provides them with blessed regalia and basic incantations. Under her tutelage, students learn that a priestess of the Kaldorei must be both a gentle hand to the wounded and a steadfast shield against the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shanda?",a="Shanda is a night elf priest trainer located inside Aldrassil, the central hollow tree settlement of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. She instructs newly awakened night elf priests in the teachings of the Sisterhood of Elune.",al={"who is this npc","shanda lore","priest trainer aldrassil"}},{q="What role does Shanda play for new priests?",a="She introduces novice priests to basic prayers, curative spells, and protective magic gifted by Elune. She also offers early quests to equip young acolytes with their initial robes and holy sigils.",al={"priest trainer role","what does shanda teach","what does shanda do"}},{q="Where can I find Shanda?",a="Shanda is found on the ground level inside the hollow trunk of Aldrassil, the massive tree that serves as the starter hub in Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",al={"where is shanda","shanda location","how to find shanda"}},{q="What organization does Shanda belong to?",a="Shanda is a member of the Sisterhood of Elune, the ancient religious order of night elf priestesses that has guided Kaldorei spiritual and cultural life for thousands of years.",al={"shanda faction","sisterhood of elune","is shanda a priestess of the moon"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For night elf priests starting their journey in Shadowglen, Shanda is the very first mentor to bestow sacred words, holy sigils, and guidance in Elune's grace.",["race:NightElf"]="Shanda represents the enduring tradition of the Sisterhood of Elune, tending to the spiritual well-being of the Kaldorei youth as they take their first steps on Teldrassil."},kw={"aldrassil","elune","night elf","priest trainer","shadowglen","shanda","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","quest:5622","quest:940"},src={"Shanda"}}
E["npc:syral-bladeleaf"] = {t="npc",n="Syral Bladeleaf",z="teldrassil",s="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil who serves as a liaison for the Council of the Forest. She guides young adventurers who arrive from Shadowglen, directing them toward local caretakers, herbalists, and elders who watch over the crown's delicate boughs.",h="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil who serves as a liaison for the Council of...",sec={{t="A Voice in Dolanaar",b="Found standing near the heart of Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf helps organize local affairs in the shadow of Teldrassil's canopy. Acting on behalf of the Council of the Forest, she directs newly arrived night elves to community leaders and herbalists across the village and the nearby wilderness. Through her guidance, travelers connect with the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth and replenish supplies for the village elders.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Village",b="Bearing the Bladeleaf surname, Syral shares ties with other prominent villagers in Dolanaar, including Elder Bladeleaf. Her responsibilities keep her focused on communal welfare, ensuring that medicinal elixirs reach those in need and that any disruptions in the local ecosystem receive swift attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Syral Bladeleaf?",a="Syral Bladeleaf is a night elf in Dolanaar who conveys directives on behalf of the Council of the Forest, helping incoming adventurers assist the surrounding woodland communities.",al={"who is syral","syral bladeleaf lore","syral dolanaar"}},{q="Where can Syral Bladeleaf be found?",a="She is located in Dolanaar, the central settlement of Teldrassil situated just southwest of Shadowglen along the main road.",al={"syral bladeleaf location","where is syral","syral map"}},{q="Is she related to Elder Bladeleaf?",a="She shares her family name with Elder Bladeleaf and Hannah Bladeleaf in Dolanaar, pointing to deep family roots in the settlement.",al={"elder bladeleaf relative","syral family","bladeleaf family"}},{q="What tasks does she assign to adventurers?",a="Syral sends travelers to assist botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth, helps organize delivery of herbal elixirs for the elders, and points adventurers toward tasks that aid Teldrassil's natural balance.",al={"syral bladeleaf quests","what does syral want","syral tasks"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves stepping out of the secluded barrows of Shadowglen, Syral Bladeleaf is one of the first voices of Dolanaar's civic and natural leadership.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Syral works closely with local naturalists and herbal supply chains, directing travelers to assist botanical research at Lake Al'Ameth and ensure fresh elixirs reach the elders."},kw={"bladeleaf","council of the forest","denalan","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","syral","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","npc:elder-bladeleaf","npc:denalan","quest:997","quest:1581","quest:489","topic:night-elf"},src={"Syral Bladeleaf"}}
E["npc:tallonkai-swiftroot"] = {t="npc",n="Tallonkai Swiftroot",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Concerned with the emerging corruption tainting the great boughs, he enlists young adventurers to recover enchanted relics and stem the foul forces plaguing the woods.",h="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of Dolanaar",b="Dwelling in the canopy settlement of Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot keeps a watchful eye over the surrounding woods. Like many night elves living beneath the boughs of the newly grown World Tree, he is alarmed by the unnatural agitation of the wildlife and the unsettling shadows gathering at the edges of their settlements.",sp=0},{t="Threats in the Canopy",b="Tallonkai directs adventurers to confront foul entities disturbing Teldrassil's peace. His concerns include corrupted dream catchers crafted to protect sleeping druids, vicious gnarlpine furbolgs succumbing to a dark malaise, and the foul harpies led by figures such as Ferocitas the Dream Eater. To Tallonkai, cleansing these disturbances is crucial to defending the fragile home of the Kaldorei.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf quest giver stationed in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil, dedicated to safeguarding the settlement from local threats.",al={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot","dolanaar questgiver"}},{q="Where can I find Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="He is located in the town of Dolanaar, the central night elf village found just outside Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"tallonkai location","where is tallonkai","find tallonkai swiftroot"}},{q="What tasks does Tallonkai give?",a="He asks travelers to retrieve the Emerald Dreamcatcher from the gnarlpine furbolgs, defeat the harpy Ferocitas the Dream Eater, and confront the warped gnarlpine threat in quests like Twisted Hatred.",al={"tallonkai quests","what does tallonkai want"}},{q="Why is he concerned about the dreamcatchers?",a="Dreamcatchers are sacred night elf talismans tied to the Emerald Dream, used to ward against nightmares and dark visions. Their theft and corruption by hostile creatures poses a spiritual danger to the local druids and denizens of Teldrassil.",al={"emerald dreamcatcher lore","why dreamcatchers"}},{q="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is a notorious harpy matriarch in Teldrassil who feeds on the lingering nightmares and corrupted energies of the land, threatening the balance of the forest.",al={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore"}},{q="What is causing the unrest Tallonkai fights against?",a="A growing sickness and unnatural corruption has seeped into Teldrassil, driving previously peaceful creatures like the gnarlpine furbolgs into violent madness.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","twisted hatred lore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Tallonkai Swiftroot represents the vigilance needed to protect Teldrassil during its vulnerable early years, asking young Kaldorei to purge corruption taking root in their new home.",["class:Druid"]="Tallonkai's concerns center on relics that tether minds safely to the Emerald Dream, making his requests deeply relevant to druidic spiritual traditions."},kw={"dolanaar","dreamcatcher","ferocitas","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:2438","quest:2459","quest:932","topic:emerald-dream","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tallonkai Swiftroot"}}
E["npc:tenaron-stormgrip"] = {t="npc",n="Tenaron Stormgrip",z="teldrassil",s="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf druid situated high within Aldrassil, the central great bough of Shadowglen. Serving the Cenarion Circle, he oversees the early ritual purifications that young kaldorei perform across the crown of Teldrassil.",h="Tenaron Stormgrip is a night elf druid situated high within Aldrassil, the central great bough of Shadowglen.",sec={{t="Watcher of Aldrassil",b="Perched upon the winding wooden platforms of Aldrassil, Tenaron Stormgrip stands as an early mentor to young night elves stepping forth from the boughs of Shadowglen. From his vantage point, he monitors the health of the local woods and the vital moonwells that sustain them. His role is to instruct novices in understanding their profound spiritual connection to the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Crown of the Earth",b="Tenaron is best known for directing initiates in the sacred rite known as Crown of the Earth. By having acolytes gather pure moonwell water and carry it across the reaches of Teldrassil, he seeks to nourish and purify the land's boughs while observing whether the young tree is flourishing or afflicted by hidden sickness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tenaron Stormgrip located?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip stands atop the wooden ramp structures of Aldrassil, the massive central tree at the heart of Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",al={"tenaron location","where is tenaron","tenaron stormgrip spot"}},{q="What is Tenaron Stormgrip's role in Shadowglen?",a="He is an elder guide and member of the Cenarion Circle who instructs young night elves in tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the vitality of the World Tree through the ritual of the Crown of the Earth.",al={"what does tenaron do","tenaron stormgrip purpose","who is tenaron"}},{q="What is the Crown of the Earth quest?",a="It is a rite overseen by Tenaron where initiates take purified water drawn from the moonwells of Shadowglen and pour it into ritual phials and sacred spots across Teldrassil to nurture the boughs and investigate the health of the tree.",al={"crown of the earth lore","why carry moonwell water"}},{q="Why is Tenaron concerned about Teldrassil's waters?",a="The moonwells are essential vessels of Elune's grace and natural purity. Because Teldrassil is young and lacks the full blessing of the Aspects, caretakers like Tenaron closely monitor every water source for signs of corruption or taint.",al={"why precious waters","teldrassil water issues"}},{q="Does Tenaron send adventurers beyond Shadowglen?",a="Yes. Once an initiate demonstrates reverence and competence in handling the sacred waters, Tenaron directs them outward into greater Teldrassil, sending them down to Dolanaar to continue serving the kaldorei.",al={"tenaron next quest","where does tenaron send you"}},{q="Is Tenaron a druid or a priest?",a="Tenaron operates closely with the Cenarion Circle, focusing on the ecological health and balance of Teldrassil's boughs, while honoring the sacred lunar magic of the moonwells.",al={"tenaron stormgrip class","is tenaron druid"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, Tenaron Stormgrip provides one of the very first introductions to the communal and spiritual duties required to keep Teldrassil alive and pure.",["class:Druid"]="Tenaron's tasks highlight the druidic stewardship needed to monitor Teldrassil's unprecedented growth and guard against subtle corruption."},kw={"aldrassil","cenarion circle","crown of the earth","moonwell","shadowglen","stormgrip","teldrassil","tenaron"},rel={"subzone:aldrassil","zone:teldrassil","quest:929","quest:940","topic:night-elf"},src={"Tenaron Stormgrip"}}
E["npc:zarrin"] = {t="npc",n="Zarrin",z="teldrassil",s="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor located in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil. Tending an open hearth behind the village inn, he instructs young night elves and visitors in traditional Kaldorei cooking techniques.",h="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor located in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Hearthkeeper of Dolanaar",b="Situated behind the Dolanaar inn away from the main thoroughfare, Zarrin tends an open fire where he shares the culinary arts of the Kaldorei. Survival in Teldrassil requires utilizing the native flora and fauna of the giant tree, and Zarrin serves as an instructor for those seeking to sustain themselves through foraging and home-cooked meals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zarrin?",a="Zarrin stands behind the inn in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, working over a cooking fire in the open yard opposite the road.",al={"zarrin location","where is zarrin","dolanaar cooking trainer"}},{q="What does Zarrin teach?",a="He is a Cooking trainer who teaches the basics of culinary preparation and traditional night elf recipes to novices.",al={"zarrin trainer","what does zarrin teach"}},{q="What tasks does Zarrin offer?",a="Zarrin asks travelers to help him prepare traditional dishes, offering the quest 'Recipe of the Kaldorei' to teach newcomers local culinary practices.",al={"zarrin quest","recipe of the kaldorei quest"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For adventurers beginning their journey in Teldrassil, Zarrin is the primary mentor for learning how to turn wild beast meats and foraged goods into nourishing meals.",["race:NightElf"]="Zarrin preserves everyday Kaldorei foodways, ensuring that traditional tastes and methods endure within the canopy of the World Tree."},kw={"cooking","dolanaar","kaldorei","teldrassil","trainer","zarrin"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","quest:4161","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},src={"Zarrin"}}
E["npc:zenn-foulhoof"] = {t="npc",n="Zenn Foulhoof",z="teldrassil",s="Zenn Foulhoof is an exiled satyr lingering just east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. While he feigns innocence to passersby and tries to trick young adventurers into helping him, the local night elves keep a close eye on his scheming. Though tolerated for a time through minor punishments, his affinity for dark magic makes him an unwelcome presence on the boughs of the World Tree.",h="Zenn Foulhoof is an exiled satyr lingering just east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Schemer in the Woods",b="Unlike most satyrs, who are outright hostiles serving demonic masters, Zenn Foulhoof somehow secured a tenuous tolerance just outside Dolanaar. He maintains a friendly facade, claiming he has changed or wants to trade in harmless forest reagents like spider fangs and tiger lily scents. In reality, he manipulates gullible youths to procure ingredients for foul rituals. Dolanaar's council refuses to let him operate unchecked; rather than executing him immediately, they order adventurers to humiliate him by feeding him corrupted forest fruit, temporarily transforming the scheming satyr into a harmless frog.",sp=0},{t="Exile to Darkshore",b="Zenn's petty trickery in Teldrassil quickly escalates into dangerous corruption. After being thoroughly chased out of the World Tree for his dark magic, he establishes a lair in Cliffspring Hollow near Cliffspring Falls in Darkshore. Stripping away all pretense of repentance, Zenn allies with grell and rogue alchemists, actively spreading a foul blight that maddens the local wildlife until Tharnariun Treetender marks him for death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why isn't Zenn Foulhoof immediately attacked by the night elves?",a="Zenn maintains a friendly veneer and has not yet openly committed atrocities on the World Tree, leading the council of Dolanaar to discipline him through public humiliation and watchfulness rather than an immediate death sentence.",al={"why is zenn friendly","why don't night elves kill zenn","is zenn foulhoof evil"}},{q="What happens when you feed Zenn the corrupted cones and berries?",a="As penance ordered by the elders of Dolanaar, an adventurer forces Zenn to ingest the tainted woodland flora he sought to exploit. The foul magic backfires instantly, turning him into a small, squawking frog.",al={"zenn redemption quest","seek redemption quest","zenn frog"},sp=1},{q="Where does Zenn Foulhoof go after leaving Teldrassil?",a="Once driven off the World Tree, Zenn flees to Darkshore and takes up residence in Cliffspring Hollow near Cliffspring Falls, abandoning all deception and actively corrupting the forest's bears and rats.",al={"where is zenn foulhoof in darkshore","zenn foulhoof location","cliffspring hollow satyr"},sp=1},{q="What is a satyr?",a="Satyrs are night elves who were warped into horned, cloven-hoofed fiends during the War of the Ancients after pledging service to the Burning Legion. Most are utterly corrupted and violently hostile to their uncorrupted kin.",al={"what are satyrs","satyr lore"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Satyrs represent the ultimate betrayal of kaldorei heritage. Seeing one lounging on the sacred boughs of Teldrassil is an insult to Elune and the spirits of the wild.",["class:Druid"]="Zenn's tampering with wild reagents and deliberate spreading of corrupting taints directly offends Cenarion teachings, which seek to keep Teldrassil pristine."},kw={"cliffspring falls","corrupted cone","dolanaar","satyr","seek redemption","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"topic:satyr","subzone:dolanaar","quest:488","quest:489","zone:darkshore","subzone:cliffspring-falls","npc:tharnariun-treetender","zone:teldrassil"},src={"Zenn Foulhoof"}}
E["quest:1581"] = {t="quest",n="Elixirs for the Bladeleafs",z="teldrassil",s="In the boughs of Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf seeks an alchemist to restock her family's burgeoning trade. Her husband spends endless hours over brewing cauldrons, and Syral hopes a batch of fresh elixirs will lighten his workload and earn the contributor a bundle of rare herbs.",h="In the boughs of Dolanaar, Syral Bladeleaf seeks an alchemist to restock her family's burgeoning trade.",sec={{t="A Burden of Prosperity",b="The settlement of Dolanaar serves as a vital crossroad for travelers, sentinels, and druids navigating Teldrassil's canopy. With so many wanderers passing through, the herb and alchemy trade run by Syral Bladeleaf and her husband has flourished. However, high demand brings its own cost. Her husband spends nearly all his hours bent over vials and cauldrons to keep shelves stocked, leaving the couple almost no time to spend together.",sp=0},{t="A Trader's Exchange",b="Rather than letting her partner burn out beneath compounding orders, Syral turns to passing herbalists and brewers. By commissioning pre-mixed draughts—specifically Elixirs of Lion's Strength and Minor Defense—she shores up the shop's inventory while offering freshly harvested, uncommon herbs in exchange. For a fledgling alchemist practicing their craft beneath the Great Tree, it is an ideal opportunity to turn common forest flora into coveted regional flora.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Syral Bladeleaf need these potions?",a="Their family herbal and alchemy shop in Dolanaar has grown extremely busy. Her husband spends all his time brewing potions to keep up with demand, leaving them no personal time together. Outsourcing the work gives him a much-needed break.",al={"why need elixirs","syral bladeleaf motive","bladeleaf shop problem"}},{q="What potions are required for the task?",a="Syral asks for six Elixirs of Lion's Strength and two Elixirs of Minor Defense. Both are staple draughts frequently purchased by adventurers and local sentinels in Teldrassil.",al={"which elixirs","what do i need to brew","potions needed"}},{q="What herbs are needed to brew the required elixirs?",a="Brewing the requested batch requires Silverleaf and Earthroot, both of which grow abundantly across the forest floor of Teldrassil, alongside standard Crystal Vials.",al={"ingredients needed","mats for elixirs","what herbs do i pick"}},{q="Who can undertake this request?",a="Only practitioners of Alchemy who have attained a basic competence in the craft are offered the task. Syral seeks dependable, well-mixed remedies for her shop rather than amateur brews.",al={"level requirement","profession requirement","can anyone do this quest"}},{q="What does Syral offer in exchange for the elixirs?",a="Syral rewards helpful alchemists with a bundle of freshly gathered, uncommon herbs that are difficult to locate casually along the woodland trails of Teldrassil.",al={"reward lore","what does syral give","bladeleaf trade reward"}},{q="Where is Syral Bladeleaf located?",a="She can be found outside the northern building in Dolanaar, near the central road that runs through the forest village.",al={"where is syral","bladeleaf location","where do i turn this in"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Teldrassil's rich soil teems with Silverleaf and Earthroot, making it straightforward to forage the raw greens needed to satisfy Syral's shop order.",["race:NightElf"]="Supporting local tradesfolk like the Bladeleafs helps sustain the fledgling settlement of Dolanaar as it grows beneath the canopy of Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="Keeping Dolanaar well-supplied with restorative and defensive draughts ensures defenders and traveling allies are prepared for woodland threats."},kw={"alchemy","dolanaar","earthroot","elixir of lion's strength","elixir of minor defense","elixirs for the bladeleafs","silverleaf","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Syral Bladeleaf",faction="Alliance",id=1581},src={"Elixirs for the Bladeleafs"}}
E["quest:2159"] = {t="quest",n="Dolanaar Delivery",z="teldrassil",s="Dolanaar Delivery is an errand entrusted to young night elves leaving the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen for the wider reaches of Teldrassil. Porthannius, detained by affairs with the local druids, tasks travelers with carrying a parcel of herbs south to Innkeeper Keldamyr. The simple journey marks an initiate's transition into the bustling hub of Dolanaar.",h="Dolanaar Delivery is an errand entrusted to young night elves leaving the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen for...",sec={{t="A Messenger for Shadowglen",b="Before new adventurers depart the training grounds of Shadowglen, Porthannius seeks someone heading down the road toward the rest of Teldrassil. Entangled in pressing business with the druids tending the glade, he cannot step away to run routine errands himself. Instead, he places a bundle of freshly harvested herbs into the hands of an aspiring hero to ensure vital supplies make it south along the forest path.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Dolanaar",b="Following the southern road out of the secluded vale leads travelers to Dolanaar, one of the foremost night elf settlements upon the great boughs of Teldrassil. There, Innkeeper Keldamyr oversees hospitality, rest, and supplies for wanderers, sentinels, and druids alike. Receiving the herbs on Porthannius's behalf, Keldamyr uses the occasion to urge young adventurers to rest their minds and spirits before confronting the growing corruption across the world tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Porthannius?",a="Porthannius is a night elf residing in Shadowglen, Teldrassil's starting glade. While working closely alongside the local druids, he enlists travelers leaving the glade to ferry supplies southward on his behalf.",al={"porthannius","who gives dolanaar delivery","quest giver porthannius"}},{q="Why can't Porthannius deliver the herbs himself?",a="Porthannius has urgent, unfinished business with the druids of Shadowglen. Because his duties keep him occupied within the sheltered vale, he must rely on passing adventurers to make the journey south.",al={"why does porthannius need help","why cant porthannius go"}},{q="What is inside the package?",a="The package contains a collection of herbs gathered within Shadowglen, destined for use at the inn in Dolanaar.",al={"dolanaar delivery package contents","what are the herbs"}},{q="Who is Innkeeper Keldamyr?",a="Innkeeper Keldamyr manages the inn in Dolanaar. Aside from providing hospitality, lodging, and hearthstones to travelers, he frequently coordinates trade and supply exchanges with other settlements across Teldrassil.",al={"keldamyr","dolanaar innkeeper","who receives the herbs"}},{q="Where is Dolanaar located?",a="Dolanaar lies south of Shadowglen. Following the primary road leading out of the glade's exit takes travelers directly into the town center.",al={"where is dolanaar","dolanaar location","directions to dolanaar"}},{q="Why is this delivery important for young adventurers?",a="It serves as an introduction to the world beyond Shadowglen, encouraging novitiates to venture outside their training grounds and discover Dolanaar's inn, trainers, and service providers.",al={"significance of delivery","why deliver herbs"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Taking this task marks a night elf's departure from the protected cradle of Aldrassil out into the broader responsibilities of safeguarding Teldrassil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The delivery illustrates how vital raw herbs from Shadowglen's verdant soils are to the healers, cooks, and caretakers of Dolanaar.",["class:Druid"]="Porthannius's preoccupation with Shadowglen's druids hints at the deeper spiritual duties and natural imbalances occupying the Cenarion Circle within the boughs."},kw={"delivery","dolanaar","dolanaar delivery","herbs","innkeeper keldamyr","night elf","porthannius","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","npc:innkeeper-keldamyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},m={start="Porthannius",["end"]="Innkeeper Keldamyr",faction="Alliance",id=2159},src={"Dolanaar Delivery (quest)"}}
E["quest:2399"] = {t="quest",n="The Sprouted Fronds",z="teldrassil",s="Following Denalan's botanical experiments at Wellspring Lake, the planted frond seeds take root and bloom. This quiet moment marks a successful harvest in understanding Teldrassil's strange and vital flora. Travelers inspecting the garden beds can witness the rapid growth firsthand.",h="Following Denalan's botanical experiments at Wellspring Lake, the planted frond seeds take root and bloom.",sec={{t="A Garden by Wellspring Lake",b="Tucked away near Wellspring Lake, the botanist Denalan dedicates himself to cataloging the peculiar plant life of Teldrassil. After sowing the seeds recovered from a mysterious shimmering frond, the soil quickly yields result. In his tended planter, strange, trembling fronds shoot up from the rich loam, eager to be gathered and examined.",sp=0},{t="The Strange Flora of the World Tree",b="Teldrassil is young, vast, and teeming with rapid natural development that both fascinates and troubles night elf herbalists. The shimmering fronds and their sprouted offshoots are emblematic of how swiftly life takes hold on the boughs of the great tree, hinting at the powerful yet unpredictable vitality woven into the island's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the sprouted fronds?",a="They are the mature plants that sprouted from seeds sown by Denalan at his lakeside camp. Cultivated from the shimmering fronds found elsewhere in Teldrassil, these peculiar plants tremble with energy when ready for harvest.",al={"sprouted fronds","what are these plants","denalans fronds"}},{q="Where is Denalan's garden located?",a="Denalan keeps his garden and research camp along the southern shores of Wellspring Lake, situated in the central wilds of Teldrassil.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan","wellspring lake garden"}},{q="Why does Denalan plant these fronds?",a="Denalan studies the curious and rapid growth patterns of Teldrassil's plant life. By planting seeds in controlled soil, he investigates their nature and tests whether they possess useful restorative or herbal properties.",al={"why plant fronds","denalan experiment","purpose of fronds"}},{q="Are the sprouted fronds dangerous?",a="No. Unlike some of the corrupted or hostile flora elsewhere on the boughs of Teldrassil, these sprouted fronds are harmless botanical specimens waiting to be plucked.",al={"are fronds dangerous","do fronds attack","is the plant harmful"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Adventurers first discover a shimmering frond in the wilds of Teldrassil and bring it to Denalan, who plants the seeds in his garden planter to await their sprouting.",al={"prereq for sprouted fronds","what quest comes first"}},{q="Why do the fronds tremble?",a="The soil and magic coursing through Teldrassil imbue native plants with vibrant, restless energy. The fronds tremble as a sign of their vitality and readiness to be harvested.",al={"trembling fronds","why do they shake"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan's research reflects the practical arts of gathering and studying Teldrassil's unique vegetation, demonstrating how quickly local seeds adapt to nurtured soil.",["race:NightElf"]="Tending the newly sprouted flora reflects the kaldorei responsibility to monitor and nurture the life taking root across their young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids observing Denalan's planter can appreciate the quiet balance of nature, seeing life flourish under attentive care even amid Teldrassil's growing perils."},kw={"denalan","herbalism","planter","seeds","shimmering frond","sprouted fronds","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},rel={"quest:931","npc:denalan","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Sprouted Frond",faction="Alliance",id=2399},src={"The Sprouted Fronds"}}
E["quest:2438"] = {t="quest",n="The Emerald Dreamcatcher",z="teldrassil",s="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar asks adventurers to recover a cherished heirloom from his abandoned home in Starbreeze Village. The Emerald Dreamcatcher, gifted to him by the druid warden Gaerolas Talvethren, was left behind when corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs overran the tranquil settlement. Reclaiming this amulet prevents its gentle nature-magic from falling into foul hands.",h="Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar asks adventurers to recover a cherished heirloom from his abandoned home in...",sec={{t="A Druidic Talisman",b="The emerald dreamcatcher is far more than a decorative trinket. Fashioned by Gaerolas Talvethren, the honored warden of the sleeping druids within Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the amulet was crafted to channel the serene currents of the Emerald Dream. By siphoning this pure spiritual energy, the dreamcatcher bestows peace and fortune upon its bearer. Such tokens are exceedingly rare, bestowed upon only a trusted few whose lives are intertwined with the forest's stewardship.",sp=0},{t="Fleeing Starbreeze Village",b="Until recently, Starbreeze Village was a peaceful settlement nestled amid the boughs of Teldrassil. That quiet life ended when the local Gnarlpine furbolgs succumbed to a violent madness, driving the night elves from their ancestral dwellings. In the terror and confusion of the evacuation, Tallonkai was forced to leave his most treasured possession hidden inside his dresser in the village's southeastern quarter, powerless to reclaim it on his own.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Corruption",b="Leaving a focus of Emerald Dream magic in the heart of an overrun village carries grave risks. The Gnarlpine have proven susceptible to dark influences, and an artifact pulsing with the energies of the Dream could easily be tainted or weaponized. Recovering the dreamcatcher safely returns a piece of Starbreeze's heritage to Tallonkai before the furbolgs or other foul denizens can defile its lingering magic.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Emerald Dreamcatcher?",a="It is a rare amulet crafted by Gaerolas Talvethren, warden of the druids in Ban'ethil Barrow Den. The dreamcatcher siphons energy from the Emerald Dream to bestow good luck and spiritual harmony upon whoever carries it.",al={"what is the dreamcatcher","dreamcatcher lore","emerald dreamcatcher"}},{q="Why was the dreamcatcher left behind in Starbreeze Village?",a="Starbreeze Village was rapidly overrun when the local Gnarlpine furbolgs fell into a violent, corrupted frenzy. Tallonkai Swiftroot was forced to flee for his life to Dolanaar, leaving the precious heirloom tucked away in his bedroom dresser.",al={"why leave it behind","starbreeze village dresser","tallonkai dresser"}},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai is a night elf refugee currently staying in Dolanaar. Having escaped the fall of Starbreeze Village, he seeks brave travelers to venture back into the occupied ruins to salvage his family heirlooms and safeguard druidic relics.",al={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot"}},{q="Who made the dreamcatcher?",a="It was crafted and gifted by Gaerolas Talvethren, the warden who watches over the slumbering druids inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"who made it","gaerolas talvethren dreamcatcher","gaerolas"}},{q="Where in Starbreeze Village is the dreamcatcher located?",a="It rests inside Tallonkai's personal dresser, situated inside the far south-eastern house of Starbreeze Village, which is now heavily prowled by hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"where is the dresser","starbreeze dresser location","find dreamcatcher"}},{q="What happens after the dreamcatcher is returned?",a="Once Tallonkai inspects the recovered amulet, he discovers that the dreamcatcher's magic has already attracted the attention of a terrifying forest predator, leading directly into the hunt for Ferocitas the Dream Eater.",al={"quest continuation","next quest after dreamcatcher"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The amulet is a direct work of Gaerolas Talvethren, the warden tending to your sleeping kin in Ban'ethil Barrow Den, making its recovery a matter of druidic honor.",["race:NightElf"]="Starbreeze was once a tranquil haven for your people. Helping Tallonkai recover his heritage strikes a small blow against the madness seizing Teldrassil's wildlife.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the displaced Kaldorei of Dolanaar secures local stability as Teldrassil struggles with spreading corruption among the furbolg tribes."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","emerald dream","emerald dreamcatcher","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","quest:2459","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:emerald-dream","topic:furbolg"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=2438},src={"The Emerald Dreamcatcher (quest)"}}
E["quest:2459"] = {t="quest",n="Ferocitas the Dream Eater",z="teldrassil",s="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is an Alliance quest given by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar. After recovering his damaged heirloom dreamcatcher, Tallonkai discovers its potent emerald core was pried away by Gnarlpine furbolgs north of Starbreeze Village. Adventurers are sent to slay the corrupted mystics and recover the stolen jewel from their leader, Ferocitas.",h="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is an Alliance quest given by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Defiled Heirloom",b="When Tallonkai Swiftroot examined the dreamcatcher recovered from the corrupted wilds, relief quickly turned to dismay. The sacred artifact had been vandalized, its vibrant emerald centerpiece pried from the woven frame. Word among the night elves held that a band of Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze Village had fallen under the influence of an owlbeast-like figure known as Ferocitas the Dream Eater, who brazenly wore a brilliant green stone around his neck. Knowing the sacred gem was useless and perverse in the creature's clutches, Tallonkai sent defenders to wrest it back.",sp=0},{t="Purging the Mystics",b="The Gnarlpine furbolgs inhabiting Teldrassil's northern reaches were once peaceful neighbors, but the growing corruption seeping into the World Tree drove them into frenzy and madness. Their mystics, who once practiced harmonious nature rites, began tapping into distorted magical energies. By tracking down Ferocitas and cutting through the mystic retinue guarding his woodland enclave, travelers restore balance to the woods and recover Tallonkai's jewel so the dreamcatcher can finally be made whole.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is located in the forest north of Starbreeze Village on Teldrassil, surrounded by corrupted Gnarlpine mystics and other woodland hazards.",al={"ferocitas location","where is ferocitas","find dream eater"}},{q="Who is Ferocitas?",a="Ferocitas is an owlbeast leader who commands a band of corrupted Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze Village. He took the emerald from Tallonkai Swiftroot's dreamcatcher and fashioned it into a crude necklace.",al={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore","what is dream eater"}},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want the jewel back?",a="The missing emerald is the core power source of Tallonkai's dreamcatcher. Without it, the talisman cannot be repaired or channel the protective energies of the Emerald Dream.",al={"why tallonkai wants jewel","tallonkai jewel purpose"}},{q="Can the Gnarlpine actually use the emerald's magic?",a="No. According to Tallonkai Swiftroot, the emerald's magical properties are completely useless to creatures like Ferocitas and the Gnarlpine mystics, who coveted it merely as a glowing bauble.",al={"can gnarlpine use dreamcatcher","does ferocitas use emerald"}},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="This quest is the final chapter of the two-part chain that began with The Emerald Dreamcatcher. Once you deliver the jewel to Tallonkai in Dolanaar, he can finally repair his heirloom.",al={"quest after ferocitas","next quest dreamcatcher"}},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine mystics hostile?",a="Like much of the wildlife and furbolg tribes across Teldrassil, the Gnarlpine have succumbed to a strange corruption warping the boughs of the newly planted World Tree, twisting their minds and turning them aggressive.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","gnarlpine corruption"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine were once allies of the Kaldorei, making the corruption of their mystics and their thievery of sacred talismans a poignant tragedy for any night elf defending Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Dreamcatchers are potent instruments tied to the Emerald Dream; seeing one defiled by a corrupted owlbeast demands swift natural retribution."},kw={"dolanaar","dream eater","emerald dreamcatcher","ferocitas","gnarlpine mystics","starbreeze village","tallonkai swiftroot","tallonkai's jewel","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:2438","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:dolanaar","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=2459},src={"Ferocitas the Dream Eater (quest)"}}
E["quest:2498"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Denalan",z="teldrassil",s="Return to Denalan is an Alliance quest connecting the botanists investigating corruption within Teldrassil. After studying the mossy tumors afflicting local timberlings, Rellian Greenspyre sends you back south to Lake Al'Ameth to assist Denalan with an alarming new discovery.",h="Return to Denalan is an Alliance quest connecting the botanists investigating corruption within Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Message Across the Boughs",b="While examining the strange mossy tumors afflicting Teldrassil's timberlings, Rellian Greenspyre receives urgent word from his colleague Denalan. Stationed beside the tranquil waters of Lake Al'Ameth, Denalan believes he has finally isolated what is causing these unnatural growths on the forest's nature spirits. Recognizing the gravity of the situation, Rellian dispatches you back south immediately to lend a hand.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at the Lake",b="Denalan's research at Lake Al'Ameth is critical to understanding the ailments creeping across the young World Tree. What began as an investigation into corrupted plant life and diseased timberlings quickly escalates into a direct confrontation with the blighted entities poisoning the boughs, starting with the ancient treant Oakenscowl.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf researcher and naturalist stationed at Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil. He dedicates his time to studying the island's flora, strange seedling mutations, and the unnatural afflictions spreading among the local timberlings.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","denalan lake al'ameth"}},{q="Why does Rellian Greenspyre send you back to Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Rellian receives word that Denalan has discovered the likely root cause behind the tumors corrupting the timberlings. Because the situation is developing rapidly and poses a growing danger to the forest, Rellian sends you to provide immediate field assistance.",al={"why go to denalan","rellian greenspyre mission"}},{q="What are the tumors afflicting the timberlings?",a="Timberlings are peaceful nature spirits born from the island's plant life, but a pervasive corruption taking root in Teldrassil causes them to sprout bizarre mossy growths. These tumors drive the creatures hostile and maddened.",al={"timberling tumors","why do timberlings have tumors","mossy tumors"}},{q="Where can I find Denalan?",a="Denalan makes his camp along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth, just south of Dolanaar in the southern woodlands of Teldrassil.",al={"denalan location","where is denalan"}},{q="What happens after you reach Denalan?",a="Upon arriving, Denalan reveals that a corrupted treant named Oakenscowl is responsible for the blighted tumors spreading through the grove, tasking you with destroying the beast to halt the contamination.",al={"what comes next","oakenscowl follow up"},sp=1},{q="Why did this quest disappear in later eras?",a="In later updates, Denalan relocated from his lakeside camp directly to the Wellspring Hovel beside Rellian Greenspyre, rendering a travel quest between the two botanists unnecessary.",al={"why was this quest removed","return to denalan removed"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The timberlings are living manifestations of Teldrassil's vitality; aiding Denalan is part of the sacred duty to heal the growing corruption threatening your people's new home.",["class:Druid"]="Investigating unnatural tumors on woodland spirits cuts to the core of the Cenarion mandate to maintain the natural balance and cleanse insidious blights."},kw={"denalan","dolanaar","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","rellian greenspyre","teldrassil","timberlings","tumors"},rel={"quest:923","quest:2499","npc:denalan","quest:922","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Rellian Greenspyre",["end"]="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=2498},src={"Return to Denalan"}}
E["quest:2499"] = {t="quest",n="Oakenscowl",z="teldrassil",s="Denalan asks adventurers to put an end to Oakenscowl, a powerful timberling corrupted by a massive growth. Dwelling in a cave along the southern bank of Lake Al'Ameth, the maddened creature now spreads blight across the local wildlife.",h="Denalan asks adventurers to put an end to Oakenscowl, a powerful timberling corrupted by a massive growth.",sec={{t="A Fallen Guardian",b="Oakenscowl was once a grand leader among the timberlings, the wood spirits that tend to the lush boughs of Teldrassil. Tragically, the corruption creeping through the world tree does not discriminate between humble wildlife and ancient protectors. Driven wild by a gargantuan tumor swelling upon its bark, Oakenscowl has become a vessel of blight rather than a steward of growth.",sp=0},{t="Purging Lake Al'Ameth",b="Lurking in a cavern on the southern shore of Lake Al'Ameth, Oakenscowl's toxic presence actively poisons surrounding waters and woodland beasts. Denalan, unable to face the beast alone, seeks the creature's destruction not out of malice, but to mercifully sever the source of corruption and study the bizarre, overgrown tumor plaguing the lake's spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Oakenscowl?",a="Oakenscowl is a massive timberling—a forest spirit tied to Teldrassil's plant life. He was once regarded as a noble leader among his kind before falling victim to a malignant growth.",al={"who is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lore","what kind of creature is oakenscowl"}},{q="Why must Oakenscowl be destroyed?",a="Oakenscowl is afflicted by a gargantuan tumor that has twisted his mind and made him violently aggressive. His presence in the cavern along Lake Al'Ameth actively spreads the strange blight to neighboring timberlings and beasts.",al={"why kill oakenscowl","oakenscowl hostile"}},{q="Where does Oakenscowl reside?",a="Oakenscowl dwells deep within a cavern situated along the southern shore of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil.",al={"oakenscowl location","where is oakenscowl cave"}},{q="Who is Denalan and why is he studying the tumor?",a="Denalan is an herbalist and naturalist living on an island in Lake Al'Ameth. He studies the flora and fauna of the world tree, striving to understand and cure the strange rot that infects the local timberling population.",al={"who gives oakenscowl quest","denalan oakenscowl"}},{q="What caused the tumor on Oakenscowl?",a="The tumor is a symptom of a deeper, insidious sickness creeping through the soil and roots of Teldrassil, corrupting nature spirits from within.",al={"why do timberlings have tumors","source of corruption"}},{q="Is Oakenscowl beyond saving?",a="By the time adventurers encounter him, the affliction has progressed too far. The tumor has completely warped the creature, leaving Denalan no choice but to call for a mercy kill.",al={"can oakenscowl be healed","cure oakenscowl"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a guardian timberling corrupted by strange tumors is a harrowing reminder to druids that Teldrassil's burgeoning ecosystem is deeply unwell.",["race:NightElf"]="The tragic downfall of Oakenscowl strikes near the heart of night elf society, threatening the very lake beneath the shadow of Aldrassil.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists aiding Denalan observe firsthand how botanical life can warp into malignant, mossy blights under the influence of unseen rot."},kw={"corruption","denalan","gargantuan tumor","lake al'ameth","mossy tumors","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=2499},src={"Oakenscowl (Classic)"}}
E["quest:2541"] = {t="quest",n="The Sleeping Druid",z="teldrassil",s="Deep within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the slumbering night elf Oben Rageclaw faces a dire magical predicament. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolg shamans have severed his dreaming spirit from his physical body, using foul enchantments to animate his flesh into a rampaging guardian.",h="Deep within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, the slumbering night elf Oben Rageclaw faces a dire magical predicament.",sec={{t="A Slumber Disrupted",b="Night elf druids enter barrow dens across Kalimdor to commune with nature through centuries of slumber, wandering the Emerald Dream while their mortal frames rest securely in stone alcoves. However, the corruption afflicting Teldrassil has driven the local Gnarlpine tribe of furbolgs to acts of desperate savagery. In Ban'ethil Barrow Den, Gnarlpine shamans uncovered a method to breach the sanctified rest of Oben Rageclaw, prying his living spirit away from his sleeping vessel.",sp=0},{t="Voodoo and Corruption",b="Rather than killing Oben, the Gnarlpine shamans used a sinister talisman—a Shaman Voodoo Charm—to forcibly animate his empty shell. Trapped helplessly in the Emerald Dream, Oben's displaced spirit can only watch as his physical form stalks the corridors, blindly attacking any who enter the den. To unravel the enchantment and find a path toward restoring his body, his ethereal projection tasks adventurers with retrieving one of the Gnarlpine charms for study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben Rageclaw is a night elf druid who entered a sacred slumber inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to commune with the Emerald Dream. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs hijacked his physical vessel, leaving his spirit displaced.",al={"oben rageclaw","who is the sleeping druid","sleeping night elf in barrow den"}},{q="Why is Oben's body attacking people?",a="Gnarlpine shamans performed a ritual separating Oben's consciousness from his flesh. They animated his empty, physical form with dark magic to serve as an aggressive guardian guarding the depths of the barrow den.",al={"why is oben hostile","why is oben attacking","oben rageclaw body attacking"}},{q="What is the Shaman Voodoo Charm?",a="It is an enchanted focus carried by the Gnarlpine shamans inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den. They use its dark power to wrench sleeping druids' spirits out of their bodies and animate their physical husks.",al={"shaman charm","voodoo charm teldrassil","what is shaman voodoo charm"}},{q="Where is Oben's true spirit during the quest?",a="Oben's consciousness is trapped wandering the Emerald Dream, unable to rejoin his mortal shell. He can only communicate with the waking world as a shimmering spirit near his resting place.",al={"where is oben","oben spirit location","emerald dream oben"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs in Ban'ethil Barrow Den hostile?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen victim to the rising taint and madness corrupting Teldrassil's wildlife and forests, causing them to turn against their former night elf allies and desecrate sacred druidic sites.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","furbolg corruption teldrassil","why furbolgs aggressive"}},{q="Can Oben's body be saved without killing it?",a="Studying the Shaman Voodoo Charm is Oben's first hope of breaking the ritual. By examining the vile enchantments binding his flesh, he hopes to understand the magic and find a way to resolve the crisis.",al={"save oben rageclaw","can oben be saved","cure oben"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, Oben's situation is a waking nightmare: having one's body hijacked while communing in the Emerald Dream violates the very foundation of druidic slumber.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Ban'ethil Barrow Den demonstrates how deeply the Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen from their ancient kinship with the Kaldorei."},kw={"ban'ethil barrow den","barrow den","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","shaman voodoo charm","teldrassil","the sleeping druid"},rel={"npc:oben-rageclaw","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Oben Rageclaw",faction="Alliance",id=2541},src={"The Sleeping Druid"}}
E["quest:2561"] = {t="quest",n="Druid of the Claw",z="teldrassil",s="Deep within the barrows of Teldrassil, the spectral form of Oben Rageclaw asks for a tragic release. Corrupted furbolgs have placed a dark enchantment over his physical vessel, forcing you to destroy his soulless shell and break the bond so his spirit may return to the Emerald Dream.",h="Deep within the barrows of Teldrassil, the spectral form of Oben Rageclaw asks for a tragic release.",sec={{t="A Severed Spirit",b="While resting in the barrows beneath Teldrassil, Oben Rageclaw suffered a terrible fate. The corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs subjected his slumbering body to a foul voodoo enchantment, severing his spirit from his mortal flesh. Trapped in a ghostly state, Oben lingers nearby, unable to return to the Emerald Dream or reclaim his own body.",sp=0},{t="Mercy for the Flesh",b="Examining the Gnarlpine's voodoo charm revealed the grim truth: Oben's physical shell is entirely under the furbolgs' dominion. To break the enchantment, an adventurer must enter the nearby chamber, strike down the mindless, hostile husk of Oben Rageclaw, and use the furbolg charm over his remains to finally shatter the magic binding his soul.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do I have to kill Oben Rageclaw?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs cast a powerful voodoo enchantment over Oben while he slumbered, turning his physical body into a soulless puppet. Because his flesh is fully under their thrall, destroying the physical vessel is the only way to sever the enchantment and free his lingering spirit.",al={"why kill oben","kill sleeping druid","oben rageclaw body"}},{q="What is the Voodoo Charm used for?",a="The charm holds the key to the enchantment controlling Oben. Once you slay his corrupted, soulless body, activating the charm over his fallen remains unravels the dark magic holding his spirit hostage.",al={"voodoo charm use","how to use voodoo charm","gnarlpine charm oben"}},{q="Where does Oben go after this quest?",a="Once his physical body is slain and the enchantment is dispelled, Oben Rageclaw's spirit is released from the mortal world. He is finally able to journey into the Emerald Dream to rest in peace.",al={"oben fate","what happens to oben rageclaw","does oben survive"},sp=1},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine using voodoo magic?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen deep into corruption and madness, turning away from their ancestral harmony to dabble in foul sorceries and crude dark magic to subjugate the creatures and sleeping druids around them.",al={"furbolg voodoo","gnarlpine voodoo magic","why do furbolgs have charms"}},{q="Who was Oben Rageclaw?",a="Oben was a night elf Druid of the Claw who entered a sacred slumber in the barrows of Teldrassil, communing with the Emerald Dream before the Gnarlpine furbolgs disturbed his rest and enslaved his mortal shell.",al={"who is oben","oben lore","oben rageclaw background"}},{q="Is Oben's spirit still talking to me while his body is alive?",a="Yes. The dark enchantment severed Oben's soul from his flesh. His spirit manifested as a ghost near the chamber entrance, completely unable to control or re-enter the enchanted, empty shell inside.",al={"oben ghost and body","two obens","why is oben in two places"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a slumbering Druid of the Claw desecrated by corrupted furbolgs is a chilling reminder of the perils of leaving one's physical body unattended while communing with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="Teldrassil was meant to be a refuge for the night elves, but the rapid corruption of native furbolgs like the Gnarlpine poses an immediate threat even within their sacred barrows."},kw={"ban'ethil","druid of the claw","emerald dream","gnarlpine","oben rageclaw","teldrassil","the sleeping druid","voodoo charm"},rel={"quest:2541","npc:oben-rageclaw","topic:druid","topic:emerald-dream","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Oben Rageclaw",faction="Alliance",id=2561},src={"Druid of the Claw (quest)"}}
E["quest:4161"] = {t="quest",n="Recipe of the Kaldorei",z="teldrassil",s="Recipe of the Kaldorei is a lesson in balance taught by Zarrin, a culinary instructor in Dolanaar. By gathering a precise number of spider legs across Teldrassil, aspiring cooks learn that sustaining oneself from nature requires restraint and respect.",h="Recipe of the Kaldorei is a lesson in balance taught by Zarrin, a culinary instructor in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="Children of the Stars",b="Behind the inn in Dolanaar, Zarrin tends a bubbling cauldron and instructs young adventurers on the traditions of his people. Long before the modern age, night elves knew themselves as the kaldorei, meaning 'children of the stars.' For Zarrin, understanding that ancestral heritage begins not on the battlefield, but in the relationship between a hunter, their food, and the surrounding boughs of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Taking Only What Is Needed",b="The core of the lesson lies in restraint. Zarrin charges his pupils with gathering small spider legs from the woodland arachnids outside Shadowglen, but specifically commands that only seven be taken—no more. In night elven culture, living in harmony with nature demands taking strictly what is necessary and returning kindness to the wild. This delicate balance must be upheld even in troubled times, a philosophy that transforms a simple spider kabob into a moral discipline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zarrin?",a="Zarrin is a night elf culinary mentor found tending a cauldron behind the inn in Dolanaar. He instructs young adventurers in cooking while emphasizing the importance of ancestral kaldorei values.",al={"zarrin","who is zarrin","dolanaar cook","cooking trainer dolanaar"}},{q="Why does Zarrin insist on collecting exactly seven spider legs?",a="Zarrin emphasizes that the kaldorei must live in harmony with nature, taking only what is needed to survive. Gathering strictly the required amount instills respect for the living forest and preserves the natural balance.",al={"why seven legs","why only seven","take no more than seven"}},{q="What does the word 'kaldorei' mean?",a="In the Darnassian tongue, kaldorei translates to 'children of the stars,' the ancient name by which the night elf people have known themselves for thousands of years.",al={"what does kaldorei mean","kaldorei meaning","children of the stars"}},{q="Where are the spider legs gathered?",a="The legs can be harvested from webwood spiders roaming the forests of Teldrassil outside of the sheltered borders of Shadowglen.",al={"where do spiders drop legs","spider leg location","which spiders"}},{q="What do night elves prepare with spider legs?",a="Zarrin teaches adventurers how to prepare Kaldorei Spider Kabobs, a traditional wilderness dish that turns woodland spider meat into a nourishing, travel-ready meal.",al={"what is the recipe","kaldorei spider kabob","spider food"}},{q="Do all spiders in Teldrassil yield the legs needed?",a="No. The immature spiders found within the protected vale of Shadowglen do not yield the proper legs for Zarrin's recipe; one must hunt the spiders wandering the broader woods of Teldrassil.",al={"do shadowglen spiders work","shadowglen spider legs"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="This task serves as an early introduction to wilderness cooking in Teldrassil, rewarding the recipe for Kaldorei Spider Kabobs.",["race:NightElf"]="The lesson reinforces the core kaldorei worldview: maintaining harmony with nature by exercising restraint and taking only what is necessary."},kw={"cooking","dolanaar","kaldorei","recipe of the kaldorei","spider kabob","teldrassil","zarrin"},rel={"npc:zarrin","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","subzone:shadowglen","topic:alliance"},m={start="Zarrin",level="7",faction="Alliance",id=4161},src={"Recipe of the Kaldorei"}}
E["quest:475"] = {t="quest",n="A Troubling Breeze",z="teldrassil",s="A Troubling Breeze is an early task given by Athridas Bearmantle in Teldrassil to investigate missing reports from Starbreeze Village. Great Warden Gaerolas Talvethren guards the hibernating Druids of the Talon nearby, and his sudden silence suggests an unnatural danger creeping across the World Tree.",h="A Troubling Breeze is an early task given by Athridas Bearmantle in Teldrassil to investigate missing reports...",sec={{t="A Silent Watcher",b="In the bough settlements of Teldrassil, communication is normally swift and measured. Athridas Bearmantle relies on word from Gaerolas Talvethren, the Great Warden entrusted with watching over the Druids of the Talon resting within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. These slumbering druids maintain the sacred pact with Ysera in the Emerald Dream, making their sanctuary vital to the spiritual balance of the young World Tree. When reports from the east ceased, an unsettling foreboding settled through the forest canopy.",sp=0},{t="Unease in Starbreeze",b="Athridas asks travelers to venture east across the forest to Starbreeze Village to seek out Gaerolas in person. The lack of messengers is no mere oversight; foul corruption and agitated wildlife have begun stirring in the wilderness. Reaching Gaerolas reveals that Athridas's intuition was accurate: trouble has descended upon the village, jeopardizing the security of the nearby barrow dens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a prominent night elf overseer in Teldrassil who tracks the well-being of the forest and ensures the sanctuaries of his slumbering druidic brethren remain undisturbed.",al={"athridas bearmantle","athridas lore","quest giver athridas"}},{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is the Great Warden chosen to protect the sleeping Druids of the Talon within the nearby Ban'ethil Barrow Den, ensuring their safety while their spirits wander the Emerald Dream.",al={"gaerolas talvethren","great warden gaerolas","who is gaerolas"}},{q="What is the Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred underground hollow on Teldrassil where night elf druids sleep for extended periods to commune with Ysera and honor their pacts in the Emerald Dream.",al={"ban'ethil barrow den","banethil","what is ban'ethil"}},{q="Why was Gaerolas out of contact?",a="Gaerolas was unable to deliver his regular reports because sudden danger and corruption began threatening Starbreeze Village and the surrounding forest, trapping him in a struggle to maintain control.",al={"why was gaerolas silent","what happened to gaerolas","trouble in starbreeze"}},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Upon finding Gaerolas Talvethren in Starbreeze Village, he directs you to confront the nearby Gnarlpine furbolgs, who have succumbed to a spreading, unnatural corruption.",al={"next quest","a troubling breeze followup","what comes after a troubling breeze"},sp=1},{q="What is the pact with Ysera mentioned in the quest?",a="Night elf druids enter prolonged, meditative slumbers to walk the Emerald Dream alongside the Green Dragonflight and Ysera, serving as custodians of nature's pristine blueprint.",al={"pact with ysera","ysera druid pact","druids of the talon sleep"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, guarding the sacred rest of the Druids of the Talon is essential to safeguarding the delicate balance of their newfound home upon Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold an intimate reverence for the Ban'ethil Barrow Den and the sleepers bound to Ysera, making any disturbance to their wardens an urgent personal matter."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil","druids of the talon","emerald dream","gaerolas talvethren","starbreeze village","teldrassil","troubling breeze","ysera"},rel={"npc:athridas-bearmantle","npc:gaerolas-talvethren","quest:476","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",["end"]="Gaerolas Talvethren",faction="Alliance",id=475},src={"A Troubling Breeze"}}
E["quest:476"] = {t="quest",n="Gnarlpine Corruption",z="teldrassil",s="Gnarlpine Corruption is an urgent courier task in Teldrassil delivered on behalf of the wounded scout Gaerolas Talvethren. It warns the night elf leadership in Dolanaar that the Gnarlpine furbolgs have succumbed to demonic corruption and overran Starbreeze Village. This report sets the stage for military and druidic interventions to prevent the taint from reaching the sleeping druids of Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",h="Gnarlpine Corruption is an urgent courier task in Teldrassil delivered on behalf of the wounded scout...",sec={{t="A Desperate Warning",b="Gaerolas Talvethren lies grievously wounded near the ruins of Starbreeze Village after being ambushed by his former allies. The Gnarlpine furbolgs, long considered peaceful neighbors and stewards of the wild, have abruptly turned feral. Too injured to carry the news back to civilization himself, Gaerolas entrusts an adventurer to carry word swiftly to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar before the madness spreads any further across the boughs of Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of Fel Moss",b="The report delivered to Athridas reveals a disturbing truth: the furbolgs have not simply grown restless, but are actively being subjected to fel magic. Their chieftain, Ursal the Mauler, has harnessed the corrupted Fel Moss festering within the World Tree, driving his people into a violent frenzy. This revelation threatens more than just settlements like Starbreeze—it directly imperils the nearby Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where slumbering druids remain completely defenseless against the deranged tribe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Starbreeze Village?",a="Starbreeze Village was overrun and pillaged by the Gnarlpine furbolgs after they were corrupted by fel magic. The sudden ambush drove out or slaughtered the inhabitants, leaving scouts like Gaerolas Talvethren trapped and wounded.",al={"why is starbreeze abandoned","starbreeze village attacked","who destroyed starbreeze"}},{q="Why have the Gnarlpine furbolgs turned violent?",a="Their chieftain, Ursal the Mauler, has begun wielding the evil powers of Fel Moss found on Teldrassil. The dark magical essence has driven the tribe into an uncontrollable, violent frenzy against their former night elf allies.",al={"why are gnarlpine mad","gnarlpine madness","why attack furbolgs"}},{q="Who is Gaerolas Talvethren?",a="Gaerolas Talvethren is a night elf scout who was ambushed by the Gnarlpine tribe while traveling toward Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Too injured to make the trek to Dolanaar, he relies on travelers to deliver word of the catastrophe.",al={"gaerolas","injured night elf starbreeze"}},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a prominent night elf authority stationed in Dolanaar. He oversees regional security and helps coordinate the response to emerging threats against the World Tree and its inhabitants.",al={"athridas","athridas bearmantle dolanaar"}},{q="Why are the night elves worried about Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den houses numerous druids who are deep in the Emerald Dream. If the frenzied Gnarlpine furbolgs reach the barrows, the slumbering night elves would be utterly defenseless against their assault.",al={"ban'ethil threat","why ban'ethil barrow den matters","sleeping druids danger"}},{q="What is Fel Moss?",a="Fel Moss is a corrupted organic growth appearing in Teldrassil, tainted by dark demonic energies. Its corruptive influence drives local wildlife and furbolgs mad when touched or wielded.",al={"what is fel moss","fel moss teldrassil"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The fall of Starbreeze Village is a tragic shock, proving that even the newly grown World Tree is already vulnerable to the demonic taint the night elves fought so hard to eradicate.",["class:Druid"]="The threat toward Ban'ethil Barrow Den is an existential emergency for the Cenarion Circle, as sleeping brothers lie vulnerable to the corrupted Gnarlpine tribe."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","dolanaar","fel moss","furbolg","gaerolas talvethren","gnarlpine corruption","starbreeze village","ursal the mauler"},rel={"npc:gaerolas-talvethren","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:starbreeze-village","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","quest:475","quest:483","quest:486","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Gaerolas Talvethren",["end"]="Athridas Bearmantle",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=476},src={"Gnarlpine Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["quest:483"] = {t="quest",n="The Relics of Wakening",z="teldrassil",s="The Relics of Wakening is an urgent rescue mission to save the Druids of the Talon slumbering within the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have overrun the sacred mounds, endangering the dormant druids whose spirits wander the Emerald Dream. Without these four specific ritual artifacts, the sleepers cannot safely be roused back into the waking world.",h="The Relics of Wakening is an urgent rescue mission to save the Druids of the Talon slumbering within the...",sec={{t="A Sanctum Defiled",b="Barrow dens serve as the secluded sanctuaries where night elf druids lie in deep hibernation while walking the Emerald Dream. West of Dolanaar, the winding corridors of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den have fallen beneath a swarm of corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven to madness by the foul taint spreading across Teldrassil, these former allies desecrated the sanctum, threatening the defenseless sleepers who remain completely unaware of the danger threatening their physical bodies.",sp=0},{t="The Tools of Return",b="A druid entering the Dream cannot simply be shaken awake; jarring their slumber without proper spiritual anchor can shatter their mind or leave their spirit stranded forever. To perform the delicate awakening ceremony, Athridas Bearmantle requires four sacred relics sealed in chests across the den: the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting. Recovering them is the only hope of stirring the Druids of the Talon before the Gnarlpine butcher or abduct them completely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't the druids just be shaken awake?",a="Druidic hibernation is a deeply delicate trance that bridges the mortal shell with the Emerald Dream. Rouse them improperly or without the protective rites of the Relics of Wakening, and their consciousness risks being stranded in the Dream forever, severed from their physical form.",al={"why need relics to wake druids","why wake ritual","why are relics necessary"}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Talon?",a="They are night elf druids attuned to the powers of Aviana, capable of taking the form of storm crows and commanding the winds. Many entered deep contemplation within the barrow dens of Teldrassil to commune with nature spirits and heal the newborn tree.",al={"druids of the talon","talon druids","who sleeps in ban'ethil"}},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking the barrow den?",a="The Gnarlpine tribe has fallen victim to a dark corruption that is steadily poisoning Teldrassil's wildlife and forests. Once peaceful neighbors to the night elves, their corrupted minds have turned violent, driving them to swarm ancient sanctuaries like Ban'ethil.",al={"why are furbolgs in the barrow den","gnarlpine attacks","why furbolgs aggressive"}},{q="What are the four relics being recovered?",a="Athridas Bearmantle tasks adventurers with gathering the Raven Claw Talisman, the Black Feather Quill, the Sapphire of Sky, and the Rune of Nesting, each stored in a sacred chest inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",al={"which relics","relics needed","names of relics"}},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas is a night elf stationed at Dolanaar who monitors the spiritual health of the surrounding wilds and organizes efforts to counter the sudden corruption afflicting the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the barrow dens.",al={"athridas bearmantle","quest giver dolanaar"}},{q="Where is Ban'ethil Barrow Den located?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is tunneled into the hills directly west of the settlement of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"ban'ethil location","where is banethil","where is the den"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For young druids, the assault on Ban'ethil is a direct strike against their Cenarion brethren. Securing the relics demonstrates your duty to preserve the sacred bridge between mortal soil and the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of a barrow den on the boughs of Teldrassil itself underscores the unsettling speed with which corruption is warping the Gnarlpine tribe and unsettling the balance of your new home."},kw={"athridas bearmantle","ban'ethil barrow den","black feather quill","dolanaar","druids of the talon","emerald dream","gnarlpine","raven claw talisman","relics of wakening","rune of nesting","sapphire of sky"},rel={"npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","quest:476","quest:486","quest:2541","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",faction="Alliance",id=483},src={"The Relics of Wakening"}}
E["quest:486"] = {t="quest",n="Ursal the Mauler",z="teldrassil",s="Ursal the Mauler is the culmination of Athridas Bearmantle's efforts to awaken the slumbering Druids of the Talon in Teldrassil. To break the unnatural sleep binding his brethren within the Barrow Den, the corrupted furbolg chief responsible for disrupting their calling must be slain.",h="Ursal the Mauler is the culmination of Athridas Bearmantle's efforts to awaken the slumbering Druids of the...",sec={{t="A Slumber Turned Nightmare",b="The Druids of the Talon secluded themselves in the Barrow Den of Ban'ethil to slumber and commune with the Emerald Dream. However, their peaceful trance was warped into an inescapable prison. Athridas Bearmantle identified the gnarlpine furbolg, specifically their vicious leader Ursal the Mauler, as the catalyst who meddled with the druids' sacred ritual, leaving them trapped between waking and the Dream.",sp=0},{t="The Den in the Cleft",b="Gathering the Relics of Wakening was only half the struggle. For Athridas's awakening ritual to pierce the spiritual fog binding the druids, the source of the interference had to be extinguished. Ursal the Mauler made his lair deep within the Cleft, a sunken, corrupted crag nestled north of the main road through Teldrassil. Striking down the furbolg warlord breaks his grasp on the sleeper's minds.",sp=0},{t="A Symptom of Deeper Rot",b="While Ursal's demise allows Athridas to conduct the ritual and rescue the Druids of the Talon, his death does not cure what ails Teldrassil. As Athridas notes upon your return, the savage furbolg was merely acting under a darker corruption spreading through the world tree's boughs. Ursal's defeat frees the sleepers, but the root cause of the madness poisoning the Gnarlpine tribe remains lurking in the shadows.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ursal the Mauler?",a="Ursal the Mauler is a ferocious, corrupted Gnarlpine furbolg chieftain residing within the Cleft in Teldrassil. He actively meddled with the reverie of the Druids of the Talon, trapping them within their Barrow Den slumber.",al={"who is ursal","ursal lore","who is the boss in the cleft"}},{q="Why must Ursal be killed to awaken the druids?",a="Even with the sacred Relics of Wakening in hand, Athridas Bearmantle's ritual cannot take effect while Ursal lives. The furbolg's foul interference acts as an ongoing spiritual anchor, preventing the druids' spirits from returning to their bodies.",al={"why kill ursal","why does ursal need to die","relilcs of wakening purpose"}},{q="Where can Ursal the Mauler be found?",a="Ursal lairs inside the Cleft, an overgrown ravine located northwest along the main path from Dolanaar, branching north off the road toward Darnassus.",al={"ursal location","where is the cleft","how to find ursal"}},{q="Does killing Ursal completely save the Gnarlpine furbolgs?",a="No. Ursal's death liberates the sleeping druids, but Athridas warns that the dark corruption plaguing the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the forests of Teldrassil persists deeper within the world tree.",al={"are furbolgs cured","did we save the furbolgs","is teldrassil saved"},sp=1},{q="Who are the Druids of the Talon?",a="The Druids of the Talon are a sect of night elf druids devoted to the stormcrow totem and the guidance of Aviana. They entered deep slumber within the Barrow Den to watch over the wilds from within the Emerald Dream.",al={"druids of the talon","who is sleeping","what druids were saved"}},{q="Who is Athridas Bearmantle?",a="Athridas Bearmantle is a Druid of the Claw stationed outside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. He directs adventurers to recover stolen relics and eliminate Ursal so that his brethren can be safely awakened.",al={"athridas bearmantle","quest giver athridas","who gives ursal quest"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine furbolgs were once ancient allies of the kaldorei. Putting down their maddened leader Ursal is a tragic necessity to protect your kin and the sleeping druids.",["class:Druid"]="Preserving the sacred rites of the Emerald Dream is paramount. Ursal's meddling with the Druids of the Talon represents a severe desecration of Cenarion communion.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Teldrassil's interior roadways and restoring the circle of druids strengthens the night elves' stronghold as they integrate into the wider Alliance."},kw={"athridas","ban'ethil","bearmantle","cleft","druid","furbolg","gnarlpine","mauler","talon","teldrassil","ursal"},rel={"quest:483","npc:athridas-bearmantle","subzone:cleft","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","quest:487","npc:moon-priestess-amara","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Athridas Bearmantle",faction="Alliance",id=486},src={"Ursal the Mauler (quest)"}}
E["quest:487"] = {t="quest",n="The Road to Darnassus",z="teldrassil",s="The main road connecting the settlement of Dolanaar to the night elf capital of Darnassus is under constant threat from corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs. Moon Priestess Amara coordinates scouts and travelers to keep this crucial trade and messenger route clear of ambushes.",h="The main road connecting the settlement of Dolanaar to the night elf capital of Darnassus is under constant...",sec={{t="A Lifeline Under Siege",b="The road spanning west from Dolanaar toward Darnassus is the primary overland artery in Teldrassil. Vital trade goods, political missives, and travelers must move along it daily to maintain connection between the capital city and the boughs of the great tree. Because Teldrassil is relatively young and wild, maintaining secure roads is critical for the fledgling kaldorei communities.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Menace",b="Rather than peaceful forest dwellers, the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe in Teldrassil has fallen victim to a foul corruption. Driven mad by whatever sickness plagues the boughs of the World Tree, they strike outward from hidden dens beneath the ridges. Stalking the tree line alongside the road, Gnarlpine ambushers prey on unwary couriers and travelers, turning what should be a peaceful forest trek into a deadly gauntlet.",sp=0},{t="The Sentinels' Vigil",b="To counter the ambushers, Moon Priestess Amara keeps watch outside Dolanaar. Blending the spiritual authority of Elune's priesthood with the militant vigilance of the Sentinels, she directs capable adventurers to strike down the ambushers near their dens below the road, ensuring safe transit to the gates of Darnassus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus so dangerous?",a="Corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs have established dens along the low ridges below the roadway. Driven mad by the corruption spreading through Teldrassil, they emerge from the underbrush to ambuscade travelers, couriers, and merchants.",al={"why are furbolgs attacking","gnarlpine road attacks","why is the road unsafe"}},{q="Who is Moon Priestess Amara?",a="Moon Priestess Amara—sometimes addressed by her full name, Sentinel Amara Nightwalker—is a night elf commander stationed on the western outskirts of Dolanaar. She oversees the security of the highway and coordinates martial efforts against the nearby Gnarlpine threat.",al={"who gives the road to darnassus quest","amara nightwalker","who is amara"}},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs aggressive?",a="Furbolgs were historically allies and peaceful neighbors of the kaldorei. However, the Gnarlpine tribe on Teldrassil has been twisted by the strange malady infecting the World Tree, turning their minds violent and driving them to attack anyone entering the forest.",al={"why gnarlpine mad","furbolg corruption teldrassil","are gnarlpine evil"}},{q="Where are the ambushers hiding?",a="The ambushers dwell below the bluffs and vantage points just off the main road west of Dolanaar, where their dens allow them to leap onto travelers moving toward Darnassus.",al={"where are gnarlpine ambushers","find ambushers","ambusher den location"}},{q="Why doesn't Darnassus send a full Sentinel garrison to clear the road?",a="The Sentinels are stretched thin across Teldrassil dealing with grell infestations, corrupted timberlings, and threats along the coast. Officers like Amara must rely on competent travelers and volunteers to keep the interior transit routes clear.",al={"where are the guards","why sentinels need help","darnassus patrol"}},{q="Why is Amara called both a Moon Priestess and a Sentinel?",a="In kaldorei society, the sisterhood of Elune and the Sentinel military are closely intertwined. It is common for leaders within the priesthood to command Sentinel troops or to have served as front-line warriors throughout their lives.",al={"amara rank","priestess or sentinel amara","amara nightwalker title"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Gnarlpine were once honorable kindred of the wild; putting down corrupted ambushers along the highway to Darnassus is a grim necessity born of Teldrassil's sickness.",["class:Priest"]="Assisting Moon Priestess Amara serves the Sisterhood of Elune, which provides both spiritual leadership and martial defence for the young tree.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darnassus is the heart of the Alliance presence in northern Kalimdor; keeping trade and communications flowing securely along its main highway is essential."},kw={"amara","ambusher","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","nightwalker","road to darnassus","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:moon-priestess-amara","subzone:dolanaar","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Moon Priestess Amara",level="8",faction="Alliance",id=487},src={"The Road to Darnassus (Classic)"}}
E["quest:488"] = {t="quest",n="Zenn's Bidding",z="teldrassil",s="Zenn's Bidding is an Alliance quest offered by Zenn Foulhoof, a solitary satyr lurking just north of the road between Shadowglen and Dolanaar. He coaxes eager adventurers into hunting local wildlife to gather animal parts for his undisclosed schemes, preying upon the trust and naivety of newcomers to Teldrassil.",h="Zenn's Bidding is an Alliance quest offered by Zenn Foulhoof, a solitary satyr lurking just north of the road...",sec={{t="A Dubious Bargain",b="Travelers emerging from Shadowglen along the path toward Dolanaar may encounter Zenn Foulhoof standing casually beneath the boughs of the Great Tree. Instead of showing outright hostility, the satyr offers promises of material reward and secrets in exchange for mundane errand running. He asks adventurers to harvest nightsaber fangs, strigid owl feathers, and webwood spider silk from the surrounding woodlands, whispering conspiratorially to keep the arrangement between themselves.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Joke",b="Satyrs are ancient enemies of the kaldorei, corrupted by demonic magic during the War of the Ancients, making Zenn's mere presence on Teldrassil an outrage. Unsuspecting adventurers who complete his errand quickly discover they have been mocked. Rather than providing treasures or deep insights, Zenn laughs openly at how gullible the traveler was to serve a satyr, celebrating that he fooled a naive stranger into carrying out his dirty work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Zenn Foulhoof is a sly satyr found lurking by the path west of Shadowglen on the way to Dolanaar. Unlike most satyrs who openly attack on sight, Zenn uses smooth talk and false promises to manipulate naive travelers into doing chores for him.",al={"who is zenn","zenn foulhoof lore","satyr questgiver"}},{q="Why is a satyr giving quests in Teldrassil?",a="Zenn presents himself as non-hostile to dupe fledgling adventurers who do not yet realize the treacherous, corrupt nature of satyrs. He exploits their eagerness for work and silver to gather reagents he cannot openly hunt for himself without drawing the ire of Sentinels.",al={"why is a satyr friendly","why can i talk to zenn","satyr in teldrassil"}},{q="What does Zenn do with the fangs, feathers, and silk?",a="Zenn claims the parts are reagents needed for his mysterious 'business in the forest.' In reality, he relishes exerting influence over mortals and using their labor for his own corrupt ends while privately mocking their gullibility.",al={"why does zenn want silk","zenn's reagents","what are the animal parts for"}},{q="Why shouldn't night elves trust Zenn Foulhoof?",a="Satyrs were once night elves who were transformed by the demonic power of the Burning Legion ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients. They are ancient, sworn enemies of the kaldorei and carriers of corruption, making any bargain with one dangerous and disgraceful.",al={"why hate satyrs","night elf satyr history","are satyrs evil"}},{q="What happens after completing Zenn's Bidding?",a="Upon handing over the items, Zenn openly mocks you for being foolish enough to obey a satyr. Realizing the deceit and the shame of aiding such a creature, adventurers are subsequently directed to seek redemption for their mistake.",al={"after zenn's bidding","seek redemption quest","what next after zenn"},sp=1},{q="Where is Zenn Foulhoof located?",a="He is located in Teldrassil, standing just north of the main road that leads west out of Shadowglen toward Dolanaar.",al={"zenn foulhoof location","where is zenn","zenn map location"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a young night elf, taking orders from a satyr is deeply shameful. Satyrs are ancestral traitors corrupted by the Burning Legion, and aiding one on the boughs of Teldrassil is an offense against nature and kaldorei heritage.",["class:Druid"]="Druids are pledged to preserve nature's balance. Poaching nightsabers, owls, and spiders on behalf of a twisted creature of corruption is an affront to Cenarion teachings."},kw={"dolanaar","foulhoof","nightsaber","satyr","shadowglen","strigid","teldrassil","webwood","zenn"},rel={"npc:zenn-foulhoof","quest:489","topic:satyr","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Zenn Foulhoof",faction="Alliance",id=488},src={"Zenn's Bidding"}}
E["quest:489"] = {t="quest",n="Seek Redemption!",z="teldrassil",s="Seek Redemption! is a quest given in Dolanaar to adventurers who were duped into doing the dirty work of the satyr Zenn Foulhoof. The Council of the Forest demands penance for harming woodland beasts, sending you to trick the deceitful satyr into eating corrupted fel cones.",h="Seek Redemption!",sec={{t="A Fool's Errand Undone",b="Zenn Foulhoof, a solitary satyr lurking just outside Dolanaar, relies on deceit to trick passersby into doing his bidding. Adventurers who unwittingly slaughtered nightsabers, strigid owls, and webwood spiders for his twisted appetites soon draw the sharp disapproval of the Council of the Forest. The council does not suffer the defilement of nature lightly, especially from their own allies.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Atonement",b="Whether warned by Syral Bladeleaf, Sentinel Kyra Starsong, or Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze, the message is plain: to remain welcome in Teldrassil, you must make amends. Rather than confronting Foulhoof with naked steel, the guardians of Dolanaar instruct you to exploit his wicked gluttony. By gathering billowing, corrupted fel cones from the forest floor, you offer the unsuspecting creature a taste of his own foul medicine.",sp=0},{t="A Croaking Retribution",b="Under the guise of another loyal errand-runner presenting a sweet snack, you hand Foulhoof the noxious cones. Unaware of the druidic snare sprung around him, Zenn eagerly devours the offerings—only to be promptly polymorphed into a helpless frog, stripped of his vile schemes and humbled before the wilderness he sought to taint.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Council of the Forest angry with me?",a="You accepted an earlier task from Zenn Foulhoof, slaughtering local wildlife—nightsabers, strigid owls, and spiders—to satisfy a satyr's whims. The Council views the needless killing of nature's creatures as a defilement of Teldrassil, demanding you atone to remain in good standing.",al={"why council mad","seek redemption why","why do i need redemption"}},{q="Who can give me this quest?",a="Several watchers in and around Dolanaar offer this quest once you finish aiding Foulhoof. You can speak to Syral Bladeleaf outside the northern dwelling, Sentinel Kyra Starsong inside the inn, or Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze along the western road.",al={"quest givers","who starts seek redemption","where to get seek redemption"}},{q="What are fel cones?",a="Fel cones are corrupted pine seeds that drop from the twisted branches around Teldrassil. Readily identified by the eerie green vapors billowing from their husks, they carry a foul magic that druids turn against unsuspecting miscreants.",al={"fel cone","what is fel cone","where fel cones come from"}},{q="What happens to Zenn Foulhoof when you feed him the cones?",a="Foulhoof mistakes the fel cones for a tasty tribute from a gullible servant. As soon as he consumes them, the volatile nature of the seed warps him instantly into a harmless, croaking frog.",al={"foulhoof frog","what happens to zenn","foulhoof fate"},sp=1},{q="Why is there a satyr living so close to Dolanaar?",a="Zenn Foulhoof keeps a low profile in a hollowed clearing just outside the settlement, disguising his malicious nature behind false pleasantries. Satyrs across Kalimdor are ancient servants of the Burning Legion, and Zenn's presence shows how deep corruption reaches into the young World Tree.",al={"why is zenn near dolanaar","satyr in dolanaar","zenn foulhoof lore"}},{q="Can you skip or abandon this quest without ruining your standing?",a="Yes. While the Council of the Forest scolds you sternly for helping Foulhoof, choosing not to undertake or complete the quest will not damage your standing or reputation with the night elves of Darnassus.",al={"reputation loss","can i abandon seek redemption","fail seek redemption"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, aiding a satyr is deeply humiliating. Satyrs are ancient enemies warped by the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients, making penance through the Council of the Forest a matter of cultural honor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the balance of Teldrassil sacred; hunting predators and scavengers at the behest of a demon-tainted outcast directly violates the Cenarion circle's tenets of guardianship."},kw={"dolanaar","fel cone","kyra starsong","satyr","seek redemption","shayla nightbreeze","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","zenn foulhoof"},rel={"quest:488","npc:zenn-foulhoof","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Sentinel Kyra StarsongSyral BladeleafSentinel Shayla Nightbreeze",["end"]="Zenn Foulhoof",faction="Alliance",id=489},src={"Seek Redemption!"}}
E["quest:5621"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of the Moon",z="teldrassil",s="Garments of the Moon is an introductory rite of service for young night elf priests in Dolanaar. Assigned by priest trainer Laurna Morninglight, it tasks an initiate with tending to Sentinel Shaya, a wounded defender patrolling the woods south of the settlement. Fulfilling this duty marks an initiate's formal recognition within the Sisterhood of Elune.",h="Garments of the Moon is an introductory rite of service for young night elf priests in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Sacred Calling",b="Within the boughs of Teldrassil, the Sisterhood of Elune tends both to the spiritual life of the kaldorei and the practical defense of their borders. When Sentinel Shaya is wounded while patrolling the dangerous wilderness south of Dolanaar, priest trainer Laurna Morninglight cannot abandon her post to render aid. Instead, she charges a newly trained initiate with proving their devotion by mending Shaya's wounds and bolstering her constitution with protective magic.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Sisterhood",b="Priests who restore Sentinel Shaya's vigor return to Dolanaar to receive their formal robes of office. These garments signify that the young acolyte has moved beyond mere classroom instruction to practical, lifesaving service under the moon's grace. In kaldorei society, supporting the Sentinels is not merely a military task; it is an act of communion with Elune and an essential duty to the safety of Teldrassil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Garments of the Moon?",a="The quest is offered by Laurna Morninglight, the priest trainer residing in the northern building of Dolanaar on Teldrassil.",al={"who gives garments of the moon","where to start garments of the moon","garments of the moon questgiver"}},{q="Who needs help during this task?",a="Sentinel Shaya, a night elf guardian who was wounded while patrolling the wilderness, is stationed just south of Dolanaar awaiting aid.",al={"who do i heal","injured sentinel location","where is sentinel shaya"}},{q="What magic is required to help Sentinel Shaya?",a="You must use healing magic to close Sentinel Shaya's wounds and cast protective wards to fortify her endurance before returning to Dolanaar.",al={"what spells to cast on shaya","how to complete garments of the moon","shaya objective"}},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. Garments of the Moon is exclusively offered to Alliance priests as an early milestone in their spiritual training.",al={"is garments of the moon priest only","garments of the moon class requirement","can druids do garments of the moon"}},{q="What does the robe reward symbolize?",a="The robe awarded by Laurna Morninglight serves as a token of initiation, signifying that you have dutifully served Elune and earned a recognized place among the local priesthood.",al={"garments of the moon robe meaning","robe reward lore","significance of garments of the moon"}},{q="What is the relationship between this quest and In Favor of Elune?",a="In Favor of Elune serves as an introductory summons to visit the trainer in Dolanaar. While not strictly required to receive Garments of the Moon, it cannot be completed once Garments of the Moon is finished.",al={"in favor of elune prerequisite","in favor of elune missed","order of dolanaar priest quests"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This rite demonstrates the twin pillars of the priesthood: restoring wounded allies through restorative prayer and protecting them against future danger with divine wards.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the Sisterhood of Elune and the Sentinels have worked hand in hand for millennia to protect the forests and people from encroaching darkness."},kw={"dolanaar","garments of the moon","in favor of elune","laurna morninglight","sentinel shaya","sisterhood of elune","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","quest:5622","subzone:dolanaar","topic:elune","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Laurna Morninglight",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5621},src={"Garments of the Moon"}}
E["quest:5622"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Elune",z="teldrassil",s="\"In Favor of Elune\" is a rite of passage for young night elf priests ready to step out of the sheltered boughs of Shadowglen. Directed by Priestess Shanda, novitiates travel down the path to Dolanaar to seek further guidance and training under Laurna Morninglight.",h="\"In Favor of Elune\" is a rite of passage for young night elf priests ready to step out of the sheltered...",sec={{t="Leaving the Glade",b="For an initiate serving Elune within Aldrassil's secluded shelter, learning begins with simple prayers and defensive invocations under the watchful eye of Priestess Shanda. Yet the cloistered life of Shadowglen cannot prepare a priestess or priest for the turmoil gripping the wider world. Once an initiate demonstrates steady faith and discipline, Shanda sends them down the shadowed forest path toward Dolanaar to continue their education.",sp=0},{t="A Step Into the Priesthood",b="Reaching Dolanaar marks an essential milestone in a night elf's divine vocation. There awaits Laurna Morninglight, a respected priestess tasked with preparing disciples for the trials facing Teldrassil. Beyond advanced instruction in moonlit spellcraft, arriving in Dolanaar prepares the acolyte to claim their first formal vestments, marking their official standing within the Sisterhood of Elune.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this journey?",a="Priestess Shanda, the night elf priest trainer stationed within the boughs of Aldrassil in Shadowglen, gives you this guidance once your initial training is complete.",al={"quest giver","who starts in favor of elune","where do i get this quest"}},{q="Where do I need to go to find Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight resides in Dolanaar, the first major settlement south of the Shadowglen gates in Teldrassil. She is located near the eastern buildings of the village.",al={"laurna morninglight location","where is dolanaar","where is morninglight"}},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. This quest is specifically designated for young night elf priests taking their initial steps into the Sisterhood and the service of Elune.",al={"is this priest only","who can do in favor of elune","druid quest?"}},{q="What happens after I speak to Laurna Morninglight?",a="Laurna Morninglight will greet you and offer the trial 'Garments of the Moon', which tests your ability to protect and heal wounded defenders before bestowing your first official clerical robes.",al={"what comes next","followup quest","garments of the moon quest"}},{q="Is this quest mandatory to continue priest training?",a="It is an optional breadcrumb quest. If you travel directly to Dolanaar on your own, Laurna Morninglight will still offer her training and subsequent tasks without needing this introduction.",al={"do i have to do in favor of elune","can i skip in favor of elune","optional breadcrumb"}},{q="Why is earning garments so important to the Sisterhood?",a="Vestments in night elf culture are not merely cloth; they are sacred symbols denoting one's official station, devotion, and readiness to channel the Moon Goddess's blessings in service of their people.",al={"why robes matter","significance of garments","station of elune priestess"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This task represents your departure from simple novitiate studies into full service, setting you on the path toward earning your first consecrated clerical vestments.",["race:NightElf"]="The Sisterhood of Elune forms the spiritual heart and historic leadership of kaldorei society, making the journey to Dolanaar a deeply traditional milestone for devotees."},kw={"dolanaar","garments of the moon","in favor of elune","laurna morninglight","priest","shadowglen","shanda","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","npc:shanda","quest:5621","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","topic:elune","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Shanda",["end"]="Laurna Morninglight",level="4",faction="Alliance",id=5622},src={"In Favor of Elune"}}
E["quest:5636"] = {t="quest",n="Desperate Prayer",z="teldrassil",s="Desperate Prayer is an Alliance priest quest directing traveling servants of the Holy Light back to Stormwind City. Initiated by the night elf priestess Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar, it calls human and dwarven priests visiting Teldrassil home to complete vital spiritual training under High Priestess Laurena.",h="Desperate Prayer is an Alliance priest quest directing traveling servants of the Holy Light back to Stormwind...",sec={{t="A Message from Home",b="While visiting the ancestral boughs of Teldrassil, priests faithful to the Holy Light may find themselves noticed by the local Sisterhood of Elune. In Dolanaar, Priestess Laurna Morninglight serves as an unexpected liaison, delivering word that a fellow priest traveled across continents seeking you out. Recognizing the urgency of the summons, Laurna encourages you to return to your homeland without delay, offering Elune's blessing alongside well-wishes for your own faith.",sp=0},{t="The Summons to Stormwind",b="The journey requires crossing the Great Sea to the grand Cathedral of Light situated in the heart of Stormwind City. There, High Priestess Laurena oversees the spiritual growth of the Alliance's faithful. Acolytes who have demonstrated early promise are summoned before her to master deeper mysteries of devotion, specifically the emergency invocation known as Desperate Prayer—a life-saving gift granted only to dedicated disciples in their darkest hour.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Desperate Prayer in Teldrassil?",a="Laurna Morninglight, a night elf priest trainer stationed in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, offers the quest. She passes along an urgent message left by a visiting priest from your home lands.",al={"who gives desperate prayer","desperate prayer quest giver teldrassil","laurna morninglight quest"}},{q="Where does this quest lead?",a="The quest directs you to the Cathedral of Light within Stormwind City, where you must speak directly with High Priestess Laurena.",al={"where do i go","turn in desperate prayer","where is laurena"}},{q="Why is a night elf directing a priest to Stormwind?",a="Night elf priests revere Elune, but foreign priests—such as humans or dwarves—who venture to Teldrassil still belong to the traditions of the Holy Light. Laurna Morninglight graciously respects their beliefs and relays messages sent from their homeland's religious hierarchy.",al={"why does a night elf send me to stormwind","night elf holy light"}},{q="What is the reward for completing this quest?",a="Reporting to High Priestess Laurena opens advanced spiritual mentorship and grants access to learn Desperate Prayer, an instantaneous healing prayer exclusive to human and dwarven priests.",al={"desperate prayer reward","what spell do i get"}},{q="Can night elf priests take this specific quest?",a="No. Night elf priests worship Elune and learn Starshards rather than Desperate Prayer. This particular summons exists specifically for human or dwarven priests who find themselves exploring Kalimdor at early levels.",al={"can night elves do desperate prayer","night elf priest desperate prayer"}},{q="How do you travel back to Stormwind from Teldrassil?",a="You must head through Darnassus to Rut'theran Village, catch a boat to Auberdine in Darkshore, take another ship across the sea to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, and then travel south through Loch Modan, Dun Morogh, and the Deeprun Tram into Stormwind.",al={"how to get to stormwind from dolanaar","teldrassil to stormwind route"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This quest marks an important rite of passage at level 10, bringing priests back into the fold of the Cathedral of Light to learn distinctive racial blessings of faith.",["faction:Alliance"]="The summons demonstrates the growing cooperation across the Alliance, as night elf priestesses readily coordinate with the church leadership in Stormwind.",["race:NightElf"]="Although night elves revere the Moon Goddess Elune, Priestess Laurna Morninglight shows polite respect for foreign devotees of the Holy Light walking under the boughs of Teldrassil."},kw={"cathedral of light","desperate prayer","dolanaar","high priestess laurena","laurna morninglight","priest quest","stormwind","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:laurna-morninglight","npc:high-priestess-laurena","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:teldrassil","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light","topic:elune"},m={start="Laurna Morninglight",["end"]="High Priestess Laurena",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=5636},src={"Desperate Prayer (Dolanaar)"}}
E["quest:5842"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome!",z="teldrassil",s="This quest greets newly arrived adventurers in Teldrassil carrying a special Dolanaar Gift Voucher. By bringing the token to Orenthil Whisperwind in the village of Dolanaar, travelers receive a rare companion to accompany them on their journeys across Azeroth.",h="This quest greets newly arrived adventurers in Teldrassil carrying a special Dolanaar Gift Voucher.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Gift in Dolanaar",b="Young night elves venturing south from Shadowglen soon come across the tree-shaded settlement of Dolanaar. Among its residents stands Orenthil Whisperwind, an attendant ready to greet select newcomers. Those carrying a Dolanaar Gift Voucher are directed straight to Orenthil, who eagerly exchanges the parchment for a curious, loyal companion pet.",sp=0},{t="An Honored Arrival",b="While most initiates must earn every scrap of equipment and companionship through trials against corruption in the boughs of Teldrassil, this voucher marks the bearer as a celebrated arrival. Orenthil welcomes the adventurer to Azeroth, bestowing a unique creature to follow them through wilderness, barrow dens, and beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The quest directs holders of a special voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind in Dolanaar. Handing over the voucher grants the adventurer a unique vanity pet to accompany them throughout their adventures.",al={"what does this quest do","welcome quest goal","why do i have this voucher"}},{q="Who is Orenthil Whisperwind?",a="Orenthil Whisperwind is a night elf stationed in Dolanaar within Teldrassil. He assists travelers by receiving their gift vouchers and presenting them with a companion creature.",al={"who is orenthil","where is orenthil whisperwind","orenthil lore"}},{q="Where is Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary village in central Teldrassil, located just south down the road from the novice grounds of Shadowglen and east of Darnassus.",al={"how to get to dolanaar","dolanaar location"}},{q="Can any adventurer take this quest?",a="This quest is only available to adventurers who possess the Dolanaar Gift Voucher, an exclusive parchment provided to select travelers upon entering the world.",al={"who can get welcome quest","is this quest available to everyone"}},{q="What kind of companions can you receive?",a="Orenthil Whisperwind offers a choice among rare and exotic creatures, giving the traveler a small animal companion to follow them across Azeroth.",al={"what pet do you get","what are the gifts"}},{q="Does this quest affect your standing in Teldrassil?",a="No. The quest is a ceremonial welcome and does not alter the political conflicts, demonic corruption, or spider infestations threatening the boughs of Teldrassil.",al={"does this give reputation","is it part of a main storyline"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves departing Shadowglen, receiving a companion in Dolanaar provides comfort and fellowship before facing the troubled woods of Teldrassil.",["faction:Alliance"]="The gesture marks the recipient as a celebrated arrival in Alliance territory, welcomed personally by local caretakers like Orenthil Whisperwind."},kw={"companion","dolanaar","gift voucher","orenthil whisperwind","pet","teldrassil","welcome"},rel={"npc:orenthil-whisperwind","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Dolanaar Gift Voucher",["end"]="Orenthil Whisperwind",level="1",faction="Alliance",id=5842},src={"Welcome! (Dolanaar)"}}
E["quest:6063"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="This quest is the first trial in a night elf hunter's journey to mastering beast companionship. Instructed by Dazalar in Dolanaar, an aspiring hunter must use an enchanted taming rod to bond with a wild Webwood Lurker. It tests the hunter's ability to respect and commune with nature rather than attempting to violently dominate it.",h="This quest is the first trial in a night elf hunter's journey to mastering beast companionship.",sec={{t="A Sacred Bond",b="For the kaldorei, hunting is not merely about tracking quarry or surviving in the wilds; it is a sacred relationship with nature. Hunter trainers like Dazalar teach that nature is far greater than any individual mortal. Animals are not beasts of burden or tools to be forcibly bent to one's will, but autonomous creatures that require mutual respect. To prove readiness for a lifelong beast companion, novice hunters must demonstrate mastery over the primal instincts of local wildlife through ancient techniques rather than brute force.",sp=0},{t="The First Trial",b="The trials begin with the giant arachnids infesting the boughs of Teldrassil. Dazalar entrusts the hunter with a specialized taming rod, directing them to seek out a Webwood Lurker. Venturing into the shadowed thickets, the hunter must face the venomous spider and establish an empathetic channel while withstanding its attacks. Successfully establishing this temporary mental bridge proves the hunter can commune even with the eerie, skittering predators of the World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This quest initiates the training sequence required for night elf hunters to permanently tame animal companions. By using a taming rod on designated local beasts, hunters prove they possess the temper and skill to commune with wild predators.",al={"why do this quest","pet quest purpose","what does taming the beast give"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer residing in the settlement of Dolanaar on Teldrassil, offers this quest to young night elf hunters who have reached sufficient experience in their field.",al={"quest giver","where to get taming quest","who starts taming the beast"}},{q="What creature must be tamed in this trial?",a="You are tasked with taming a Webwood Lurker, one of the venomous giant spiders that dwell in the wild thickets and woods outside Dolanaar.",al={"which pet to tame","webwood lurker target","what beast do i tame"}},{q="Do I keep the Webwood Lurker permanently?",a="No. The Webwood Lurker tamed during this quest is a temporary companion meant solely for practicing the basics of pet handling. Once returned to Dazalar, the bond is released as you prepare for the next trial.",al={"do i keep the spider","is the webwood lurker permanent","keep pet"}},{q="Why do night elves test hunters with spiders first?",a="Webwood Lurkers are predatory and aggressive, making them a stern test of a novice's composure. Mastering an unnatural-seeming arachnid proves that a hunter can bridge their consciousness with diverse, hostile manifestations of nature.",al={"why webwood lurker","why tame a spider","spider taming lore"}},{q="What comes after returning to Dazalar?",a="Dazalar sends the hunter to test their bond against other native fauna of Teldrassil—specifically a Nightsaber Stalker and a Strigid Screecher—before granting permanent taming abilities.",al={"what next","after taming the beast","next trial"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage marks a hunter's transition from solitary archer to a true partner of the wilderness, bound to the beasts of the forest.",["race:NightElf"]="Reflecting kaldorei philosophy, pet taming emphasizes communion and reverence for nature rather than subjugation and domination."},kw={"dazalar","dolanaar","hunter pet","kaldorei","taming","taming rod","teldrassil","webwood lurker"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6063},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf)"}}
E["quest:6101"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="This trial marks the second phase of a night elf hunter's pet taming training under Dazalar in Dolanaar. Hunters are tasked with subduing a nightsaber stalker using an enchanted taming rod to better appreciate the shifting diversity of wild beasts. It deepens the bond of understanding between the wilderness of Teldrassil and the sentinel trackers who walk beneath its boughs.",h="This trial marks the second phase of a night elf hunter's pet taming training under Dazalar in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="The Changing Nature of Beasts",b="While early lessons focus on understanding fundamental instincts, Dazalar emphasizes that nature's only constant is its continuous change. Every species of the forest carries a distinct temperament, and a hunter must learn to adapt their will accordingly. In the shadow of Teldrassil's canopy, this means engaging creatures that are cunning, stealthy, and far more predatory than simple webspinners.",sp=0},{t="Subduing the Nightsaber",b="Nightsabers are revered by the kaldorei as sacred predators, fierce guardians, and stealthy companions of the Sentinels. For a novice hunter, channeling the power of the taming rod against a nightsaber stalker requires steady nerve and calm authority. By bending the predatory aggression of the stalker into a receptive bond, the hunter proves they can command more than merely docile or lesser creatures of the woods.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It is the intermediate trial in the night elf hunter chain that unlocks permanent beast taming. Dazalar sends you to tame a nightsaber stalker so you can observe the temperamental differences between varied predatory creatures.",al={"why do this quest","pet taming quest 2","nightsaber taming goal"}},{q="Where can nightsaber stalkers be found?",a="Nightsaber stalkers roam the wooded paths and undergrowth to the south of Dolanaar in central Teldrassil.",al={"where are nightsaber stalkers","stalker location","where to find the cat"}},{q="Do I get to keep the nightsaber stalker as my permanent pet?",a="No. The beast tamed with the rod is temporary and serves solely as a practice subject. Once the full three-part trial is finished and you return the rod, you will learn the true taming ability and can choose a permanent companion.",al={"do i keep the pet","can i keep the nightsaber","is this my pet forever"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer situated in Dolanaar within Teldrassil, issues this instruction after you have completed your first taming test.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","dazalar location"}},{q="Why do night elves revere nightsabers so deeply?",a="Nightsabers have lived alongside the kaldorei for millennia as companions, scouts, and war mounts for the Sentinels and Priestesses of Elune. Taming one is considered a proud hallmark of kaldorei woodland mastery.",al={"night elf cats lore","why nightsabers matter","lore on nightsabers"}},{q="What comes after completing this task?",a="Dazalar will grant a final taming task involving another Teldrassil creature before teaching the innate ability to tame, feed, and manage permanent companion beasts across Azeroth.",al={"next quest","what is after nightsaber stalker","hunter trial next"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite represents the core education of a hunter, teaching you how to respect diverse animal temperaments before you are trusted with a lifelong companion.",["race:NightElf"]="Nightsabers are deeply entwined with kaldorei history and culture, making the taming of a stalker a traditional milestone for local woodland scouts."},kw={"beast taming","dazalar","dolanaar","hunter","nightsaber stalker","taming rod","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:6061","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6101},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf 2)"}}
E["quest:6102"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="This quest marks the final trial in a young night elf hunter's basic training. Under the direction of Dazalar in Dolanaar, hunters must tame a predatory owl of the skies before unlocking the power to choose a true, lifelong companion.",h="This quest marks the final trial in a young night elf hunter's basic training.",sec={{t="Mastery of the Canopy",b="Before completing their initial beastcraft, night elf hunters must establish harmony with creatures from every corner of Teldrassil's ecosystem. Having previously proven their will against beasts of the underbrush, Dazalar charges the hunter with bringing down the spirit of the skies: the Strigid Screecher. These watchful birds of prey roost high across the boughs west of Dolanaar, requiring patience and a steady nerve to pacify with the enchanted Taming Rod.",sp=0},{t="A Hunter's Bond",b="Succeeding with the Strigid Screecher fulfills the ancient lessons of communion between kaldorei hunters and nature. Upon returning the spent rod to Dazalar, the apprentice leaves behind training exercises and earns the full art of calling, dismissing, and permanently taming beasts of their own choosing across Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Strigid Screechers found?",a="Strigid Screechers roost in the woods west of Dolanaar. Hunters must seek out these predatory birds among the canopy and roots outside the village to test their rod.",al={"screecher location","where is strigid screecher","owl location"}},{q="Who is Dazalar?",a="Dazalar is a night elf hunter trainer stationed in Dolanaar. He oversees young kaldorei who have reached basic competence in archery and tracking, testing them on land and sky beasts before bestowing the ability to bind a real animal companion.",al={"dazalar role","who teaches pet taming dolanaar","hunter trainer dolanaar"}},{q="Do I get to keep the Strigid Screecher as my pet?",a="No. The screechers tamed during this trial are temporary subjects bound only by the Taming Rod's magic. Once the trial is turned in, the rod is surrendered, and the hunter is taught how to tame a permanent companion of their own choosing in the wild.",al={"keep owl","is screecher permanent","do i keep this pet"}},{q="What happens after completing this trial?",a="Dazalar permanently unlocks your ability to tame, call, and dismiss beasts. He also points you toward further training in Darnassus to learn the vital arts of feeding and teaching your companion in combat.",al={"what comes next","after taming the beast","hunter pet quest finish"}},{q="Why do night elves tame owls specifically?",a="Birds of prey such as owls hold deep cultural significance among the kaldorei as vigilant hunters of the night and trusted scouts. Mastering a creature of the skies proves the hunter understands aerial predators alongside ground-dwelling beasts.",al={"owl lore night elf","why owls","strigid screecher importance"}},{q="Can hunters choose any animal after this quest?",a="Yes. Once Dazalar teaches the permanent taming ability, a hunter is free to seek out any tameable beast of the land, water, or sky across Teldrassil and beyond.",al={"what pets can i get","choosing first pet","any beast tameable"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage is the threshold where a hunter transitions from fighting alone to forging a lifetime partnership with a wild companion.",["race:NightElf"]="Taming Teldrassil's native wildlife reflects the kaldorei path of walking in harmony with nature rather than bending it through force."},kw={"beast","dazalar","dolanaar","hunter pet","screecher","strigid screecher","taming","taming rod","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:dazalar","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:6061"},m={start="Dazalar",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6102},src={"Taming the Beast (night elf 3)"}}
E["quest:6103"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="teldrassil",s="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for fledgling night elf hunters in Teldrassil. After proving their mastery by taming wild beasts across the boughs, hunters are sent to Darnassus to learn the deeper arts of pet care and discipline from Jocaste.",h="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for fledgling night elf hunters in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Rite of Passage",b="Before a night elf hunter can roam Kalimdor with a loyal companion by their side, they must master more than just the taming rod. While subduing a wild creature proves basic strength and will, an untutored beast remains an unpredictable liability. Once an initiate demonstrates their capability in the wilderness surrounding Dolanaar, Dazalar directs them inward to Darnassus to complete their training.",sp=0},{t="Guidance in the Cenarion Enclave",b="Within the serene groves of the Cenarion Enclave, the revered hunter Jocaste imparts the essential arts of companionship. She instructs the young hunter in how to properly nourish their pet, resurrect it should tragedy strike, and nurture its fighting instincts through training. To night elves, this relationship is rooted in deep reverence for nature rather than simple domination.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This quest completes the initial hunter pet questline for night elves. It directs you to Darnassus to unlock the core skills required to maintain and train your permanent animal companion.",al={"why do this quest","pet training quest night elf","what does training the beast do"}},{q="Where do I find Jocaste?",a="Jocaste resides in Darnassus within the Cenarion Enclave, nestled among the towering trees and hunter lodges in the northwest portion of the capital.",al={"where is jocaste","jocaste location","find jocaste"}},{q="Who starts the quest?",a="Dazalar, the hunter trainer in Dolanaar, offers this quest after you have completed all three steps of taming trials across Teldrassil.",al={"quest giver","who gives training the beast","dazalar location"}},{q="What skills do you learn from Jocaste?",a="Speaking with Jocaste unlocks the essential arts of beast mastery: feeding your companion, reviving it if it falls in combat, and training it with new abilities.",al={"what abilities do i get","jocaste rewards","hunter pet spells"}},{q="Why does night elf culture emphasize pet training?",a="Kaldorei hunters view their pets as partners rather than subservient tools. Proper training and care reflect the race's core philosophy of living in balance and awe of nature.",al={"night elf hunter lore","why train beasts night elf"}},{q="Is this quest available to other races?",a="This specific journey to Darnassus is unique to night elf hunters. Other hunter races undergo equivalent training rites under their own racial mentors.",al={"can dwarves do this","can horde do training the beast"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite marks your graduation from novice tracker to a true master of beasts, unlocking the ability to train, feed, and revive your companion.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei tradition of beast companionship centers on respect and coexistence, reflecting the teachings passed down through Darnassus and the Cenarion Enclave."},kw={"cenarion enclave","darnassus","dazalar","hunter pet","jocaste","teldrassil","training the beast"},rel={"npc:jocaste","npc:dazalar","subzone:cenarion-enclave","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:night-elf","quest:6081"},m={start="Dazalar",["end"]="Jocaste",level="10",faction="Alliance",id=6103},src={"Training the Beast (night elf)"}}
E["quest:7383"] = {t="quest",n="Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei",z="teldrassil",s="This quest sends young night elves across Teldrassil to draw water from the island's most sacred moonwell beneath the ancient Oracle Tree. Entrusted by Corithras Moonrage, travelers witness firsthand the spiritual vitality meant to sustain their new home and observe the deep connection between the well waters and the healing boughs of the great World Tree.",h="This quest sends young night elves across Teldrassil to draw water from the island's most sacred moonwell...",sec={{t="Water of the Oracle Glade",b="Corithras Moonrage directs adventurers far to the northwest of Teldrassil to the serene Oracle Glade. Tucked deep beneath the great canopy sits the Oracle Tree and the first, most potent moonwell consecrated upon the new World Tree. Drawing water into an Amethyst Phial, travelers are meant to touch the heart of night elf sacred tradition, tapping into waters deeply suffused with the blessings of the goddess Elune.",sp=0},{t="A Stunted Recovery",b="Upon meeting Corithras outside the gates of Darnassus, the druid shares troubled insights gleaned from the Oracle Tree. While Teldrassil survived its creation and initial blessings, its vigor remains strangely hindered. The druids and ancient spirits watching over the canopy fear that despite their purification rituals, a lingering taint or deep corruption persists within the trunk, threatening the future of the Kaldorei sanctuary.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the moonwell at the Oracle Tree so important?",a="It is the very first and most powerful moonwell created on Teldrassil. Located beneath the ancient Oracle Tree in the far northwest, its waters hold the purest concentration of Elune's divine energy on the island.",al={"oracle tree moonwell","why this moonwell","amethyst phial moonwell"}},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and mystic stationed along the road near Darnassus. He guides promising adventurers through the spiritual history and lingering perils surrounding Teldrassil's unorthodox creation.",al={"corithras","who is corithras moonrage"}},{q="What is wrong with Teldrassil's growth?",a="Despite receiving blessings and tending by the Cenarion Circle, Teldrassil's vitality remains stunted. The druids monitoring the island through the Oracle Tree suspect a hidden corruption still festers inside the boughs, preventing the tree from truly thriving.",al={"teldrassil corrupted","why is the tree sick","teldrassil growth hindered"}},{q="Where does Corithras wait after I fill the phial?",a="After you fill the Amethyst Phial at the Oracle Glade, Corithras leaves his earlier post and waits for you along the main crossroads just outside the eastern gates of Darnassus.",al={"corithras location","where is corithras","where to turn in"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Fetching the waters of the first moonwell is an initiation into the fragile balance of your people's newest home and the hidden rot that endangers it.",["class:Druid"]="The druids of the Cenarion Circle created Teldrassil to restore harmony, making the discovery of its stunted health deeply concerning to your order.",["class:Priest"]="The holy waters of the Oracle Glade represent the purest manifestation of Elune's grace on Teldrassil, central to the rites of the Sisterhood."},kw={"amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","darnassus","elune","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","topic:druid","quest:937","quest:2518"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",faction="Alliance",id=7383},src={"Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}
E["quest:8357"] = {t="quest",n="Dancing for Marzipan",z="teldrassil",s="During the festive season of Hallow's End, adventurers traveling through Darnassus are tasked with collecting festive sweets for a sick orphan in Stormwind. Innkeeper Saelienne upholds the trick-or-treat tradition in full, requiring an impromptu dance performance before parting with her prized Darnassus Marzipan.",h="During the festive season of Hallow's End, adventurers traveling through Darnassus are tasked with collecting...",sec={{t="A Tradition Upheld",b="Even in the sacred forest city of Darnassus, the revelry of Hallow's End brings a lighter spirit to the long-lived night elves. When travelers arrive looking to gather holiday confections on behalf of Jesper, a sick child recovering in Stormwind, Innkeeper Saelienne insists that the rules of the season remain unbroken. Charity or not, a treat requires a proper trick first.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Marzipan",b="To earn the delicate Darnassus Marzipan, adventurers must set aside their dignified demeanor and put on a show right on the inn floor. Saelienne demands nothing less than a dance, gladly rewarding those willing to shed their pride and embrace the festive cheer with the confection needed to complete the cross-continental holiday care package.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dancing for Marzipan?",a="The quest is part of the seasonal Alliance Hallow's End festivities. You perform a dance for Innkeeper Saelienne in Darnassus to obtain Darnassus Marzipan, one of several holiday treats required to cheer up a sick orphan named Jesper in Stormwind.",al={"why dance for marzipan","what is this quest","marzipan quest"}},{q="Who is Innkeeper Saelienne?",a="Innkeeper Saelienne manages the inn within Darnassus, offering shelter and rest to travelers beneath the boughs of Teldrassil. During Hallow's End, she oversees the distribution of local holiday confections to those willing to play along with tradition.",al={"who is saelienne","saelienne lore"}},{q="Why does Saelienne insist on a dance?",a="Saelienne strictly adheres to the spirit of Hallow's End. Even though the treat is destined for an ailing child, she holds fast to the custom of 'trick or treat,' playfully requiring a demonstration of dancing prowess as the trick before handing over the sweet.",al={"why dance","why does saelienne want me to dance"}},{q="Where does the marzipan go after this?",a="Once received, the Darnassus Marzipan is bundled alongside seasonal sweets collected from the other Alliance capital inns—Ironforge, Stormwind, and Menethil Harbor—to fulfill the quest to bring holiday joy to young Jesper in Stormwind.",al={"who gets the marzipan","what to do with marzipan"}},{q="What is Darnassus Marzipan?",a="Darnassus Marzipan is a sugary confection crafted in the night elven capital, traditionally made from ground almonds and sugar. It serves as Darnassus's signature festive treat for visiting trick-or-treaters during Hallow's End.",al={"darnassus marzipan lore","what kind of candy is it"}},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="No. Dancing for Marzipan is an Alliance-only seasonal quest. Darnassus is an Alliance stronghold, and the marzipan is gathered specifically for an Alliance orphan convalescing in Stormwind City.",al={"is this quest alliance only","horde marzipan quest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This festive task showcases the unity and lighthearted camaraderie shared across Alliance capitals, bringing treats from distant Teldrassil all the way to a young orphan in Stormwind.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, participating in Hallow's End is an endearing adoption of Alliance seasonal customs, blending their serene woodland lifestyle with playful revelry."},kw={"dance","darnassus","hallow's end","innkeeper","jesper","marzipan","saelienne","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:saelienne","quest:8311","npc:jesper","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Innkeeper Saelienne",faction="Alliance",id=8357},src={"Dancing for Marzipan (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:8715"] = {t="quest",n="Bladeleaf the Elder",z="teldrassil",s="Bladeleaf the Elder is a Lunar Festival encounter in the night elf settlement of Dolanaar. Standing beneath a shaft of celestial moonlight, Elder Bladeleaf greets travelers celebrating their ancestors and guides seekers onward across the boughs of Teldrassil. Paying respects to this honored spirit offers wisdom on reading the starry skies and honors the heritage of the night elves.",h="Bladeleaf the Elder is a Lunar Festival encounter in the night elf settlement of Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Celestial Presence in Dolanaar",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirit of Elder Bladeleaf manifests amid the village of Dolanaar, resting beneath the sweeping canopy of Teldrassil. Illuminated from above by an unbroken beam of radiance, the elder stands quietly among the busy sentinels and druids of the settlement, greeting wanderers who take the time to pause and pay their respects to the ancestors.",sp=0},{t="Wisdom of the Heavens",b="Elder Bladeleaf speaks of the countless stars in the night sky, reminding those who listen that celestial bodies hold answers to earthly mysteries. In night elf tradition, the stars and heavens are deeply intertwined with spirituality, fate, and the watchful gaze of Elune. Bladeleaf imparts this perspective to travelers before directing them toward other honored spirits across the world, such as Elder Bladeswift.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Bladeleaf?",a="Elder Bladeleaf is an ancestral spirit honored during the seasonal Lunar Festival. He appears in Dolanaar on Teldrassil, illuminated by a column of light from the heavens, and shares quiet reflections on wisdom and the stars.",al={"elder bladeleaf","bladeleaf","who is bladeleaf"}},{q="Where can I find Elder Bladeleaf?",a="Elder Bladeleaf can be found standing in Dolanaar, the primary town in the lower boughs of Teldrassil, marked by a bright shaft of light descending through the trees.",al={"bladeleaf location","where is bladeleaf","find elder bladeleaf"}},{q="Why is Elder Bladeleaf illuminated by light?",a="All the ancestral elders who manifest during the Lunar Festival are marked by a beam of celestial light from the sky, symbolizing their sacred connection to the heavens and the realm of the ancestors.",al={"why beam of light","bladeleaf light beam","shaft of light"}},{q="What does Elder Bladeleaf tell travelers?",a="Elder Bladeleaf muses on how the starry heavens hold answers to worldly mysteries, asking whether the wise and lucky might gaze up to discover truth. He also offers guidance on the whereabouts of other elders, such as Elder Bladeswift.",al={"bladeleaf dialogue","what does bladeleaf say"}},{q="Who does Elder Bladeleaf guide you toward next?",a="Elder Bladeleaf points seekers toward Elder Bladeswift, encouraging travelers to continue their pilgrimage of honoring the ancestors.",al={"next elder after bladeleaf","who does bladeleaf send you to"}},{q="Can Horde players visit Elder Bladeleaf?",a="The Lunar Festival allows all adventurers to honor ancestral spirits, but reaching Elder Bladeleaf requires venturing into Dolanaar, an Alliance settlement deep within Teldrassil, making it dangerous for Horde wanderers.",al={"can horde talk to bladeleaf","bladeleaf horde"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Finding an ancestor within the newly grown World Tree of Teldrassil is a poignant reminder of the enduring legacy of the kaldorei and their deep reverence for the night sky.",["class:Druid"]="The elder's presence serves as an opportunity for druids to meditate upon the bond between the earthly realm beneath the canopy and the celestial truths above.",["faction:Alliance"]="Dolanaar offers safe haven and celebration for Alliance travelers making their pilgrimage through the boughs of Teldrassil during the festival."},kw={"bladeleaf","bladeswift","dolanaar","elder bladeleaf","elders","lunar festival","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:elder-bladeleaf","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:940","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Bladeleaf",id=8715},src={"Bladeleaf the Elder"}}
E["quest:918"] = {t="quest",n="Timberling Seeds",z="teldrassil",s="Timberling Seeds is an early task given by the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil. Concerned by the growing hostility of the local nature elementals, Denalan seeks to harvest their seeds to test whether enriched soil can cultivate calmer, more harmonious growth. The task offers a glimpse into the quiet efforts of night elf herbalists working to understand the subtle afflictions plaguing the World Tree.",h="Timberling Seeds is an early task given by the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Restless Nature",b="Timberlings are nature elementals native to the boughs of Teldrassil, intricately linked to the health and vitality of the flora around them. Ordinarily peaceful reflections of the forest's balance, their recent and inexplicable hostility has alarmed the local night elves. Rather than merely culling them, the botanist Denalan hopes to understand the source of their agitation.",sp=0},{t="Seeds of a New Growth",b="Suspecting the blemish lies deep within the ground itself, Denalan aims to sprout fresh timberlings in enriched, carefully treated loam. By collecting seeds from the wandering timberlings near Lake Al'Ameth, he hopes to nurture a gentler generation of elementals and discover whether the land's corruption can be countered from the roots up.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are timberlings?",a="Timberlings are small plant-like nature elementals found on Teldrassil. They mirror the natural order and life cycle of the great tree's flora and fauna.",al={"timberling lore","what are timberlings","nature elementals teldrassil"}},{q="Why have the timberlings become aggressive?",a="Denalan suspects an underlying flaw or contamination in Teldrassil's soil. As elemental manifestations of the tree's ecology, the timberlings reflect the growing corruption spreading through the island.",al={"why are timberlings angry","timberling hostility","angry timberlings"}},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf naturalist and botanist who tends a small garden retreat on the western shore of Lake Al'Ameth, studying Teldrassil's unusual flora and soils.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","lake al'ameth botanist"}},{q="Where can timberling seeds be gathered?",a="Timberlings roam the shaded thickets, shores, and forest glades surrounding Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",al={"where to find timberling seeds","timberling locations","lake al'ameth seeds"}},{q="What does Denalan plan to do with the seeds?",a="Denalan intends to cultivate the seeds within special, purified soil mixtures he has developed, hoping to grow docile timberlings that are free from the forest's agitation.",al={"what happens to seeds","denalan plan","planting timberling seeds"}},{q="How does this connect to Teldrassil's wider troubles?",a="The aggression of these basic nature spirits is one of the earliest signs that Teldrassil is suffering from an unnatural taint, leading researchers toward deeper investigations in Darnassus.",al={"teldrassil corruption","why is teldrassil sick","tree corruption"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, timberlings are direct barometers of Teldrassil's well-being. Watching these gentle spirits turn feral is a chilling sign that their new home is unwell.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold a deep affinity for nature spirits. Aiding Denalan's study helps preserve elemental balance without relying solely on violent culling.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Gatherers attuned to the flora of Teldrassil can appreciate Denalan's botanical experiments, which explore the delicate relationship between plant seeds and enriched soil."},kw={"botany","denalan","elementals","lake al'ameth","seeds","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Denalan",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=918},src={"Timberling Seeds (Classic)"}}
E["quest:919"] = {t="quest",n="Timberling Sprouts",z="teldrassil",s="Timberling Sprouts is a quest given by the nature-watcher Denalan near Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil. Concerned by the sudden and unnatural proliferation of woodland sprouts around the lake shores, Denalan asks travelers to uproot them before they mature into hostile timberlings. The task highlights early signs that a creeping corruption is disturbing the balance of the newly grown World Tree.",h="Timberling Sprouts is a quest given by the nature-watcher Denalan near Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Weeding Lake Al'Ameth",b="Around the serene banks of Lake Al'Ameth, strange plant-like creatures known as timberlings have begun multiplying at an alarming rate. Rather than thriving in harmony with the woodland, the emerging timberling sprouts display signs of corruption from the moment they take root. Denalan, a dedicated student of nature residing beside the lake, recognizes that these sprouts are beyond healing. Left unchecked, they rapidly mature into aggressive bark-covered creatures that menace local wildlife and unwary travelers. Gathering and destroying the sprouts serves as an immediate line of defense to keep the grove clean.",sp=0},{t="Signs of a Deeper Taint",b="While uprooting sprouts helps manage the local hazard, Denalan notes with dread just how swiftly the sprouts appear. Their unchecked proliferation is an unnatural phenomenon on Teldrassil. Rather than being an isolated infestation, the tainted sprouts are a symptom of a deeper malaise that threatens the roots and soil of the World Tree itself—a riddle Denalan and the druids of Darnassus are racing to unravel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are timberling sprouts?",a="Timberling sprouts are the nascent, juvenile forms of timberlings—small elemental plant beings native to Teldrassil's boughs. Unfortunately, those germinating along Lake Al'Ameth are tainted and rapidly grow into hostile, aggressive creatures.",al={"what are timberlings","timberling sprout lore","what is a sprout"}},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is an herbalist and nature-tender living in a quiet camp near the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He watches over the flora of the bough and studies the ecological shifts and strange corruptions taking hold on Teldrassil.",al={"who gives timberling sprouts","denalan lore","lake al'ameth questgiver"}},{q="Why can't these sprouts simply be healed or purified?",a="Denalan observes that the sprouts are already tainted beyond redemption by the time they surface. Attempting to restore them is futile, making culling the only practical way to prevent them from maturing into dangerous hazards.",al={"can sprouts be saved","why destroy timberlings","are sprouts beyond help"}},{q="Where are the sprouts found?",a="The sprouts take root along the muddy shores, shallows, and lush banks surrounding Lake Al'Ameth in central Teldrassil.",al={"timberling sprout location","where to find sprouts","lake al'ameth sprouts"}},{q="What causes the timberlings to sprout so aggressively?",a="The unnatural surge of hostile timberlings is driven by a corrupting influence spreading into Teldrassil's soil and waters. Even young growths are corrupted before they fully bloom, pointing toward an underlying blight afflicting the young World Tree.",al={"why are timberlings mad","what taints the sprouts","timberling corruption"}},{q="What happens after clearing these sprouts?",a="Denalan continues his investigation into the nature of the lake's sickness, examining samples of soil, seeds, and water to trace the root source of the blight.",al={"next quest after sprouts","what follows timberling sprouts"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Teldrassil is meant to be a fresh sanctuary, making corrupted growth around sacred waters like Lake Al'Ameth a deeply troubling omen.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold responsibility for safeguarding the delicate balance of nature; pruning blighted sprouts is a sad but necessary duty to protect the broader ecosystem.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists have a keen eye for how healthy vegetation ought to grow, recognizing instantly that these sprouts are diseased and unnaturally twisted."},kw={"corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","taint","teldrassil","timberling sprouts","timberlings","weeding"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","quest:997","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=919},src={"Timberling Sprouts"}}
E["quest:927"] = {t="quest",n="The Moss-twined Heart",z="teldrassil",s="The Moss-twined Heart is a strange, corrupted core harvested from the monstrous timberling Blackmoss the Fetid. Smothered in oily, dark moss, the heart unnervingly continues to beat on its own, prompting an investigation by the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.",h="The Moss-twined Heart is a strange, corrupted core harvested from the monstrous timberling Blackmoss the...",sec={{t="A Beating Core",b="Carved from the remains of Blackmoss the Fetid, this Timberling heart is almost unrecognizable beneath a layer of dark, oily moss. The only betrayal of its true nature is a slow, rhythmic pulse that persists even after being severed from the creature. Such unnatural resilience hints that the corruption spreading through Teldrassil's wild plant life is far more pervasive than ordinary rot.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Examination",b="Denalan, a keen researcher of the local flora stationed near Lake Al'Ameth, recognizes the grim reality of the artifact immediately. Timberlings should be gentle beings intertwined with the boughs of the World Tree, yet this heart demonstrates a virulent blighting influence. Intrigued and troubled, Denalan resolves to plant and study the corrupted organ to understand the foul moss taking root in the island's soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Moss-twined Heart come from?",a="The heart is taken from Blackmoss the Fetid, a large and heavily corrupted timberling wandering the wilderness of Teldrassil.",al={"where do i get the heart","moss-twined heart drop","blackmoss the fetid heart"}},{q="Why is the heart still beating?",a="The dark, oily moss infesting the timberling appears to sustain it through unnatural vitality. Even when cut from the creature, the heart maintains a slow, persistent rhythm.",al={"why does heart pulse","still beating heart","timberling heart beat"}},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf naturalist tending a nursery near the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He dedicates himself to studying Teldrassil's flora, sproutings, and the creeping corruption affecting the island's timberlings.",al={"who is denalan","where is denalan","denalan location"}},{q="What will Denalan do with the heart?",a="Denalan decides to plant the heart in an enchanted planter to sprout and isolate the foul moss, hoping to uncover the root cause of the blighted growth.",al={"what happens to the heart","planting the heart quest","denalan heart research"}},{q="What are timberlings supposed to be?",a="Timberlings are naturally peaceful plant-elementals born of the forest. However, throughout Teldrassil, dark forces and unnatural taint have driven many of them mad and aggressive.",al={"what are timberlings","timberling lore","are timberlings evil"}},{q="Is the corruption on the heart magical or natural?",a="The moss appears foul and oily rather than healthy, suggesting an unnatural blight infecting the native ecology of Teldrassil rather than normal wilderness decay.",al={"is the moss magic","source of foul moss","teldrassil moss blight"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, watching the young World Tree Teldrassil foster tainted, aggressive timberlings like Blackmoss is a sobering sign that their new home is troubled by a creeping sickness.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle take keen interest in anomalies like this beating, blighted heart, seeking to diagnose whether the corruption can be purged or if it signals deeper rot.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Any student of plants can see the oily growth on this core is completely unnatural, defying standard botanical traits by keeping a severed heart alive."},kw={"blackmoss the fetid","blight","corruption","denalan","lake al'ameth","moss-twined heart","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:941","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Moss-Twined Heart",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=927},src={"The Moss-twined Heart"}}
E["quest:929"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is a sacred task assigned by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar to draw sanctified waters from the moonwell near Starbreeze Village. In exchange for replenishing the waters of Darnassus, young night elves learn the tragic history that led their people to cultivate the massive boughs of Teldrassil.",h="Crown of the Earth is a sacred task assigned by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar to draw sanctified waters from...",sec={{t="Sustaining the Moonwells",b="The great central moonwell of Darnassus demands constant communion with the lesser fonts scattered across the crown of the World Tree. Druids craft refined jade phials specifically to draw and carry these luminescent waters without disturbing their purity. By sending initiates on foot to Starbreeze Village, the elders ensure both that the civic fountains remain brimming with Elune's grace and that the youth understand the labor required to nourish Teldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Third War",b="Completing this chore rewards the initiate with oral history. Corithras Moonrage recounts the despair that gripped the kaldorei immediately after the Battle of Mount Hyjal. The sacrifice of the ancestral World Tree Nordrassil stripped the night elves of their precious immortality, and amidst the ruin, Illidan Stormrage was unleashed while Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream. This climate of grief and isolation laid the groundwork for Teldrassil's controversial planting.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of drawing moonwell water?",a="The druids residing in Darnassus regularly replenish their primary city moonwell using the waters collected from surrounding forest shrines, sustaining the sacred network across Teldrassil.",al={"why get moonwell water","moonwell water use","purpose of jade phial"}},{q="Where is the moonwell for this task located?",a="The moonwell sits just outside Starbreeze Village, situated to the east of Dolanaar along the forest path.",al={"where is the moonwell","starbreeze moonwell location","starbreeze village well"}},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf druid stationed in Dolanaar who guides young adventurers through the ritual duties and histories surrounding the health of Teldrassil.",al={"who gives the quest","corithras moonrage lore"}},{q="What history does Corithras teach upon return?",a="He explains the catastrophic aftermath of the Battle of Mount Hyjal, recalling how Nordrassil was burned, kaldorei immortality vanished, Illidan was freed, and Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage disappeared.",al={"what does corithras say","crown of the earth lore text"}},{q="Why do night elves feel lost after Mount Hyjal?",a="Nordrassil had bestowed perpetual life and protection to the night elves. Sacrificing the tree's power to annihilate Archimonde shattered their timeless existence, leaving them mortal, directionless, and deeply vulnerable.",al={"why did elves lose immortality","what happened after hyjal"}},{q="What is a Shan'do?",a="Shan'do is an honorific in the Darnassian tongue meaning 'honored teacher', applied here to Malfurion Stormrage, the supreme leader of the druids.",al={"what does shando mean","shando meaning"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every night elf must confront the loss of immortality and the disappearance of Malfurion Stormrage, making this sacred collection ritual an essential lesson in your people's recent grief.",["class:Druid"]="The moonwells are vital conduits of nature and astral magic, serving as living reservoirs that bind your order's duties in Darnassus to the roots of Teldrassil."},kw={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","jade phial","moonwell","nordrassil","starbreeze village","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:shan-do"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="5",faction="Alliance",id=929},src={"Crown of the Earth (3)"}}
E["quest:930"] = {t="quest",n="The Glowing Fruit",z="teldrassil",s="The Glowing Fruit is a quest in Teldrassil initiated by discovering a strange fruited plant growing wild in the forest. Suspecting something unnatural, young adventurers deliver the luminescent specimen to the herbalist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth for study.",h="The Glowing Fruit is a quest in Teldrassil initiated by discovering a strange fruited plant growing wild in...",sec={{t="An Unnatural Harvest",b="While traversing the misty boughs of Teldrassil, explorers occasionally stumble across curious, luminous flora bearing large, round fruit. Given the delicate balance of the World Tree and the recent strange behaviors among the island's wildlife, unusual botanical specimens demand careful investigation. Convinced that the strange growth should not be ignored, adventurers pluck the radiant harvest to bring to someone versed in the flora of the wild.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Investigation",b="At Lake Al'Ameth, the knowledgeable gardener and herbalist Denalan receives the glowing fruit with both fascination and concern. He notes that the specimen appears exotic, speculating that its seeds might have arrived from distant lands across the sea, perhaps even the Eastern Kingdoms. More troubling to Denalan is how the foreign seed reacted with the soil of Teldrassil itself—a reaction that immediately yields an aggressive outburst from hostile boglings as soon as the fruit is handled.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Strange Fruited Plant found?",a="The Strange Fruited Plant grows wild out in the wilds of Teldrassil, tucked among the undergrowth away from the major settlements. Interacting with the plant yields the Glowing Fruit and begins the quest.",al={"where do i find the plant","strange fruited plant location","how to start the glowing fruit"}},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf herbalist and botanist stationed along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He spends his days tending the soil, studying regional flora, and monitoring the strange environmental disturbances affecting Teldrassil.",al={"where is denalan","denalan npc","who turns in glowing fruit"}},{q="Why does the fruit glow?",a="Denalan observes that the fruit belongs to an exotic species foreign to Kalimdor. Its bizarre luminescence and vitality stem from a strange, volatile reaction between the foreign seed and the unique, potent soil of Teldrassil.",al={"why is the fruit glowing","what is wrong with the fruit"}},{q="What happens when you hand the fruit to Denalan?",a="Upon concluding his brief inspection, the strange energies surrounding the fruit cause three hostile boglings to manifest suddenly around Denalan's camp, immediately attacking nearby adventurers.",al={"what spawns after quest","bogling ambush"},sp=1},{q="Where does Denalan think this plant came from?",a="Denalan suspects the plant's seeds may have originated far away across the Great Sea, carried to Kalimdor from the distant eastern continent of Azeroth.",al={"where did seeds come from","fruit origin"}},{q="Does this quest connect to other ecological problems on Teldrassil?",a="Yes. It ties into Denalan's broader research into why the boughs of Teldrassil and its local woodland creatures, like the timberlings and bog beasts, are becoming increasingly agitated and unnatural.",al={"teldrassil corruption","lake al'ameth problems"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids dedicated to preserving nature's balance, discovering foreign, volatile flora thriving unnaturally in Teldrassil's sacred boughs is an immediate red flag.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will appreciate Denalan's botanical insight into how foreign seeds can cross continents and mutate when exposed to enchanted soils.",["race:NightElf"]="Kaldorei youth learn through Denalan that even the young soil of their new home, Teldrassil, is susceptible to unpredictable foreign blights."},kw={"boglings","denalan","glowing fruit","herbalism","lake al'ameth","strange fruited plant","teldrassil","timberlings"},rel={"npc:denalan","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},m={start="Strange Fruited Plant",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=930},src={"The Glowing Fruit"}}
E["quest:931"] = {t="quest",n="The Shimmering Frond",z="teldrassil",s="Discovered among the roots and canopies of Teldrassil, a curious flora radiates with an otherworldly shimmer. Recognizing its rarity, travelers bring a specimen to the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth to uncover its origin.",h="Discovered among the roots and canopies of Teldrassil, a curious flora radiates with an otherworldly shimmer.",sec={{t="A Strange Glow",b="While wandering through the verdant boughs of Teldrassil, observant travelers may stumble across a strange fronded plant. Unlike the usual forest foliage, its fronds catch the light and shimmer with a pulsing, twisting radiance. Such an unnatural presence catches the eye of anyone mindful of the island's delicate, nascent ecosystem.",sp=0},{t="Denalan's Discovery",b="Bringing the cutting to the botanist Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth reveals an unexpected truth. Denalan identifies the plant as an exotic specimen not native to northern Kalimdor, having last encountered its kind decades ago during a journey to the distant Swamp of Sorrows in the Eastern Kingdoms. Fascinated by how such a seed could travel across the ocean and thrive to such impressive size upon the World Tree, Denalan immediately sets to work cultivating and testing the sample.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the strange plant originally come from?",a="According to the botanist Denalan, the plant is native to the Swamp of Sorrows, a murky wetland far to the southeast in the Eastern Kingdoms. He had not seen a living specimen since visiting the marshlands decades earlier.",al={"frond origin","where is frond from","swamp plant"}},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is an inquisitive night elf botanist and herbalist stationed near the banks of Lake Al'Ameth on Teldrassil. He dedicates his time to studying and nurturing Teldrassil's burgeoning plant life, often experimenting with foreign seeds and planters.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan"}},{q="Why is this plant growing on Teldrassil?",a="It remains an ecological mystery. Denalan marvels at how a seed could travel all the way from the Eastern Kingdoms across the Great Sea, yet somehow take root and flourish into such a large specimen in Teldrassil's rich soil.",al={"how did it get to teldrassil","why is frond here"}},{q="What happens after giving the frond to Denalan?",a="Denalan immediately places the specimen into his planter at Lake Al'Ameth to conduct tests. His cultivation quickly causes several sprouted fronds to blossom, leading to further study of the exotic flora.",al={"next quest","denalan test","sprouted fronds"},sp=1},{q="Does this plant cause corruption in Teldrassil?",a="No. While much of Teldrassil's wildlife faces subtle corruption from foul influences, this plant simply appears to be an unusual, misplaced exotic breed rather than an agent of corruption.",al={"is frond corrupted","corrupted plant"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists and plant enthusiasts will appreciate the botanical intrigue of finding a marshland plant thriving thousands of miles from its native ecosystem.",["class:Druid"]="Druids mindful of the Great Tree's balance take note of non-native plant life introduced to Teldrassil's delicate young canopy.",["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves tending to their new home, Denalan's experiments provide vital insight into how resilient Teldrassil's soil truly is."},kw={"botany","denalan","lake al'ameth","shimmering frond","sprouted fronds","strange fronded plant","swamp of sorrows","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:2399","subzone:lake-al-ameth","zone:teldrassil","zone:swampofsorrows"},m={start="Strange Fronded Plant",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=931},src={"The Shimmering Frond"}}
E["quest:932"] = {t="quest",n="Twisted Hatred",z="teldrassil",s="Twisted Hatred is a covert task issued by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Teldrassil. He asks trusted champions to delve into the cavern of Fel Rock to execute Lord Melenas, a satyr marshalling the local grell into an organized, corrupting force dangerously close to night elf settlements.",h="Twisted Hatred is a covert task issued by Tallonkai Swiftroot in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Bitter Disgrace",b="For the night elves, satyrs represent the living memory of ancient betrayal. Born of Highborne who gave themselves to the Burning Legion during the War of the Ancients, these caprine demons serve as a painful, enduring stain upon kaldorei history. That a satyr would establish a foul foothold right here within Teldrassil, the young World Tree supposed to be a sanctuary, is viewed by local defenders like Tallonkai Swiftroot as an acute embarrassment.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at Fel Rock",b="North of the nearby paths lies Fel Rock, a corrupted cavern system infested with feral grell. Lord Melenas has rallied these naturally chaotic creatures into a hostile, organized force under his dark will. Fearing what the satyr intends to unleash upon the boughs of the World Tree, Tallonkai demands that Melenas be eliminated quickly, quietly, and decisively by bringing back his severed head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Melenas?",a="Lord Melenas is a satyr who has claimed the cave of Fel Rock in northern Teldrassil. He commands a brood of aggressive grell warriors and schemes to spread corruption throughout the World Tree.",al={"lord melenas","who is melenas","fel rock boss"}},{q="Where can I find Lord Melenas?",a="He lurks deep within Fel Rock, a jagged cave system located north of Dolanaar in Teldrassil, surrounded by grell and other corrupted creatures.",al={"melenas location","where is melenas","how to find fel rock"}},{q="Why does Tallonkai Swiftroot want this kept secret?",a="Satyrs represent a horrific, ancient chapter of night elven history, having betrayed their people during the War of the Ancients. Having one lurking so boldly within the heart of the newly planted World Tree is considered an utter disgrace that Tallonkai prefers to resolve without widespread panic.",al={"why secret","why must this stay between us","tallonkai secret"}},{q="What is the relationship between satyrs and grell?",a="Grell are small, mischievous, and naturally corrupted wild creatures found across Teldrassil. Satyrs, being cunning and inherently demonic, readily bully or bend such lesser creatures into serving their foul ambitions.",al={"grell and satyrs","why are grell following melenas","satyr grell connection"}},{q="Why are there satyrs on Teldrassil in the first place?",a="Teldrassil was grown only a few years ago without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects. Despite the druids' hopes for a clean sanctuary, corruption and dark beings quickly crept onto the island, with satyrs sneaking in to establish footholds in shadowy places like Fel Rock.",al={"satyrs on teldrassil","how did satyrs get here","teldrassil corruption"}},{q="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?",a="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf guardian stationed near Dolanaar who watches for emerging threats against Teldrassil and tasks adventurers with neutralizing nearby pockets of corruption.",al={"tallonkai","who gives twisted hatred"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every satyr is an ancient reminder of your ancestors' fall to demonic ambition; putting Lord Melenas to the sword is both a duty to the World Tree and an act of ancestral penance.",["class:Druid"]="The vile presence of Melenas and his corrupted grell at Fel Rock poisons the fragile balance of Teldrassil's newly grown wilderness."},kw={"fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},rel={"npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","subzone:fel-rock","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Tallonkai Swiftroot",faction="Alliance",id=932},src={"Twisted Hatred"}}
E["quest:933"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is an Alliance quest given by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar. He directs you to draw water from the moonwell near the Pools of Arlithrien, an area increasingly threatened by crazed Gnarlpine furbolgs. Completing this task uncovers how Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm rallied the night elves to raise Teldrassil in the wake of Malfurion Stormrage's disappearance.",h="Crown of the Earth is an Alliance quest given by Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",sec={{t="A Perilous Moonwell",b="Corithras Moonrage tasks you with taking a tourmaline phial to a moonwell resting southeast of Darnassus's entrance, along the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien. The journey is far from quiet. The once peaceful Gnarlpine furbolgs have succumbed to sudden, violent fury, ambushing travelers and harrying Sentinel patrols throughout the region. What early reports wrote off as isolated skirmishes has escalated into a pervasive threat haunting the new home of the night elves.",sp=0},{t="Fandral Staghelm's Ambition",b="Upon receiving the filled phial, Corithras shares critical history regarding Teldrassil's creation. Following the Third War, Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished, leaving the Cenarion druids leaderless and fractured. In his absence, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm seized the mantle of leadership. Staghelm persuaded the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore that the night elves could not afford idle mourning; they needed to reclaim their lost immortality and heal their civilization by planting a massive new World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the moonwell for this quest?",a="The moonwell is located southeast of the main entrance to Darnassus, situated along the southern shores of the Pools of Arlithrien.",al={"arlithrien moonwell","moonwell location","where to fill phial"}},{q="Why are the Gnarlpine furbolgs attacking?",a="The Gnarlpine were traditionally a peaceful kin of bear-men, but a dark, mindless rage has recently consumed them across Teldrassil. The Sentinels initially dismissed the early attacks as isolated incidents, but the corruption has spread rapidly, turning them into a constant menace to nearby settlements and patrols.",al={"furbolgs mad","gnarlpine aggressive","why furbolgs attack"}},{q="What happened to Malfurion Stormrage?",a="Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage vanished without explanation following the Third War. Even to this day, neither the Cenarion druids nor the night elf leadership know what became of him or where he currently sleeps.",al={"where is malfurion","what happened to stormrage","malfurion missing"}},{q="Who decided to plant Teldrassil?",a="With Malfurion missing, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm stepped up to guide the druids. He convinced the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore to support raising a new World Tree, arguing it was essential for the kaldorei to rebuild and regain the immortality lost during the destruction of Nordrassil.",al={"who made teldrassil","staghelm world tree","why was teldrassil grown"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This leg of your journey explains the controversial political momentum that brought Teldrassil into existence following Malfurion's sudden disappearance.",["class:Druid"]="The Cenarion Circle's fracture under Fandral Staghelm's leadership becomes clearer as Corithras recounts the desperate push to regain ancient immortality."},kw={"corithras moonrage","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","gnarlpine","malfurion stormrage","pools of arlithrien","tourmaline phial"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:pools-of-arlithrien","subzone:dolanaar","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:furbolg","topic:druid","topic:sentinels","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="9",faction="Alliance",id=933},src={"Crown of the Earth (4)"}}
E["quest:934"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Crown of the Earth is a pivotal step in the Dolanaar quest chain investigating the ailments plaguing Teldrassil. Corithras Moonrage tasks adventurers with gathering water from the sacred moonwell in the Oracle Glade, using the journey to reveal the troubling truth behind the World Tree's creation.",h="Crown of the Earth is a pivotal step in the Dolanaar quest chain investigating the ailments plaguing...",sec={{t="The Oracle Glade",b="Corithras Moonrage directs travelers far to the northwest of Teldrassil, nestled beneath the majestic canopy of the Oracle Glade. Resting directly under the massive boughs of the Oracle Tree lies the first and most potent moonwell raised upon the island. Drawing an Amethyst Phial from its shimmering waters brings seekers face to face with the prime sanctuary from which the druids and the tree itself monitor the health of their new homeland.",sp=0},{t="The Denied Blessing",b="Upon returning the phial to Dolanaar, Corithras reveals the dark flaw in Archdruid Fandral Staghelm's grand design. After the sacrifice of Nordrassil at Mount Hyjal, Staghelm sought to restore night elven immortality by planting Teldrassil and asking the Dragon Aspects for their blessings. However, Nozdormu the Timeless One refused, rebuking Staghelm for his sheer arrogance. Queen Alexstrasza followed suit, withholding the Aspect of Life's vital blessing and leaving Teldrassil's growth volatile, imperfect, and vulnerable to deep corruption.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Oracle Glade moonwell located?",a="The moonwell is located in northwestern Teldrassil, situated directly north of the primary road leading into Darnassus. It lies beneath the great boughs of the Oracle Tree.",al={"where is oracle glade","oracle glade moonwell location","oracle well"}},{q="Why did Nozdormu refuse to bless Teldrassil?",a="Nozdormu, the Dragon Aspect of Time, chided Archdruid Fandral Staghelm for his hubris. The dragons viewed the rushed creation of Teldrassil as a selfish attempt by the night elves to reclaim their lost immortality rather than a selfless defense of nature.",al={"why nozdormu refused","dragon blessing teldrassil","why dragons say no"}},{q="Why didn't Alexstrasza bless the new World Tree?",a="Alexstrasza the Life-Binder concurred with Nozdormu's judgment against Staghelm's pride. Without her life-giving blessing, Teldrassil's growth became wild, unstable, and susceptible to the afflictions creeping through its boughs.",al={"alexstrasza blessing","why did alexstrasza refuse","dragon queen teldrassil"}},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf keeper stationed at Dolanaar. He guides young defenders across the boughs of Teldrassil to sample its moonwells and imparts the history of the tree's flawed beginnings.",al={"corithras","who is corithras moonrage"}},{q="Did Teldrassil restore night elf immortality?",a="No. Because Nozdormu refused to bestow his temporal blessing upon Teldrassil, the night elves remain mortal following the loss of Nordrassil at the end of the Third War.",al={"are night elves immortal","teldrassil immortality","do elves live forever again"}},{q="What is the purpose of collecting water from the Oracle Glade?",a="The moonwell beneath the Oracle Tree is the island's first and most powerful well. Drawing its water allows Corithras to assess the underlying spiritual and natural health of Teldrassil.",al={"why get oracle water","amethyst phial purpose"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This task strikes at the heart of modern kaldorei society, explaining why the grand hopes of recovering your immortality after the Third War collapsed under the scrutiny of the Great Aspects.",["class:Druid"]="For the Cenarion Circle, visiting the Oracle Tree highlights the ideological split between Fandral Staghelm's forceful ambitions and the natural balance traditionally preserved by Malfurion Stormrage.",["faction:Alliance"]="Understanding the fragile state of Teldrassil explains the persistent blight and creature madness troubling the Alliance's newest capital territory."},kw={"alexstrasza","amethyst phial","corithras moonrage","fandral staghelm","immortality","moonwell","nozdormu","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:corithras-moonrage","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:teldrassil","subzone:dolanaar","topic:nordrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=934},src={"Crown of the Earth (5)"}}
E["quest:935"] = {t="quest",n="Crown of the Earth",z="teldrassil",s="\"Crown of the Earth\" marks the culmination of the cleansing rites across Teldrassil's sacred moonwells. Handing over the gathered waters to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus underscores the growing anxiety over the World Tree's flawed, unblessed existence.",h="\"Crown of the Earth\" marks the culmination of the cleansing rites across Teldrassil's sacred moonwells.",sec={{t="A Flawed Genesis",b="Teldrassil was raised in the wake of the Third War to grant the night elves a new home and restore their lost immortality. However, the Great Aspects Alexstrasza and Nozdormu withheld their blessings, refusing to sanction the tree's creation. Without their divine protection, Teldrassil has fallen victim to creeping sickness, causing bizarre creatures to erupt from the boughs and once-peaceful furbolg tribes to descend into madness.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to the Arch Druid",b="Corithras Moonrage tasks young adventurers with gathering waters from moonwells across the island to monitor and soothe the bough's ailments. Consolidating these samples into a single vessel, Corithras sends the runner deep into Darnassus to the Cenarion Enclave. There sits Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, the architect of Teldrassil, who views the creeping corruption not as an omen of hubris, but as an annoying burden he alone must solve.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Fandral Staghelm want this moonwell water?",a="Fandral Staghelm commissioned the gathering of moonwell samples across Teldrassil to study and address the corruption seeping through the World Tree. As the leader who championed the tree's planting, he carries the responsibility of finding a solution to the strange beasts and crazed furbolgs unsettling the canopy.",al={"fandral water purpose","why does fandral need the vessel","what is the water for"}},{q="Why is Teldrassil plagued by corruption and crazed beasts?",a="Unlike the ancient World Tree Nordrassil, Teldrassil was planted without the blessings of Alexstrasza the Life-Binder or Nozdormu the Timeless. Denied these primal dragon aspects' protection, the new tree's growth is fundamentally flawed, allowing strange malignancies to take root in the soil and warp nearby wildlife and furbolgs.",al={"why is teldrassil sick","teldrassil corruption","why are furbolgs mad"}},{q="Where is Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm located?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm resides in Darnassus within the Cenarion Enclave. You can find him atop the central druid pavilion overlooking the enclave's sacred groves.",al={"where is fandral","fandral staghelm location","how to find fandral"}},{q="Who is Corithras Moonrage?",a="Corithras Moonrage is a druid stationed at Dolanaar who coordinates the moonwell cleansing efforts across Teldrassil. He gathers the purified phials collected by wanderers, combines them into a single vessel, and directs couriers to deliver them to Arch Druid Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"who gives crown of the earth","corithras role","corithras moonrage"}},{q="What happens after completing this quest?",a="Delivering the filled vessel to Fandral Staghelm concludes the primary Crown of the Earth quest chain in Teldrassil. Staghelm accepts the water rather curtly and directs his attention back to managing the broader threats facing the night elf homeland.",al={"crown of the earth follow up","what comes after crown of the earth 6","next quest after crown of the earth"},sp=1},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so dismissive upon receiving the vessel?",a="Fandral Staghelm is notoriously proud, impatient, and burdened by the daunting task of ruling the Cenarion Circle while Malfurion Stormrage remains absent. He views administrative setbacks and slow messengers with disdain, feeling the heavy yoke of Teldrassil's survival rests entirely on his own shoulders.",al={"why is fandral rude","fandral personality","is fandral always grumpy"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This rite exposes the quiet anxiety beneath your new home: Teldrassil was planted in pride without the Dragon Aspects' blessings, and its growing sickness is a reminder of the fragility of your people's fresh start.",["class:Druid"]="Carrying moonwell waters to the Arch Druid of the Cenarion Circle brings you directly before Fandral Staghelm, showcasing the fierce political and spiritual divide that has gripped druidic leadership in Malfurion's absence.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the wider Alliance, Darnassus is an imposing capital of ancient mystery, but the corrupted wilderness around it proves that even the night elves face internal perils on their own sacred ground."},kw={"alexstrasza","cenarion enclave","corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","darnassus","fandral staghelm","moonwell","nozdormu","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:929","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:corithras-moonrage","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","subzone:cenarion-enclave","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},m={start="Corithras Moonrage",["end"]="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=935},src={"Crown of the Earth (6)"}}
E["quest:937"] = {t="quest",n="The Enchanted Glade",z="teldrassil",s="In the Oracle Glade on northwestern Teldrassil, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak struggles to protect the ancient Oracle Tree from aggressive Bloodfeather harpies. After a dispatched runner bound for Darnassus is slain, defenders are called upon to strike back at the harpies' nests and recover their belts as proof.",h="In the Oracle Glade on northwestern Teldrassil, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak struggles to protect the ancient...",sec={{t="A Glade Under Siege",b="The Oracle Glade is one of Teldrassil's sacred retreats, centered upon a colossal, ancient specimen known as the Oracle Tree. Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak was dispatched with an escort of warriors to keep watch over this venerable bough. Unfortunately, savage Bloodfeather harpies have encroached on the hollows, nesting aggressively throughout the surrounding canopy and threatening anyone who draws near.",sp=0},{t="Severed Lines to Darnassus",b="Tensions peaked when the Oracle Tree attempted to send a courier to the capital city of Darnassus carrying an urgent report. The messenger never cleared the boughs; harpies ambushed and slaughtered the runner before the report could leave the glade. In response, Arynia has tasked local adventurers with culling the flock and retrieving Bloodfeather belts to push back the encroaching flock.",sp=0},{t="A Summons from the Tree",b="Once the immediate threat of the nearby nests is diminished, the ancient tree itself responds. The Oracle Tree sheds a fragment of its enchanted bark, seeking an emissary to deliver its message into the hands of the high leadership of the kaldorei.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?",a="The Bloodfeather clan nests densely across northern Teldrassil. In the Oracle Glade, they have encircled the Oracle Tree, fiercely guarding their roosts and attacking anyone attempting to travel to or from the sacred spot.",al={"harpies in oracle glade","why bloodfeather attack","oracle tree harpies"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak is a Sentinel officer stationed alongside a modest vanguard in the Oracle Glade. Her primary mission is defending the Oracle Tree from surrounding harpies and reestablishing contact with Darnassus.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","who gives the enchanted glade","cloudsbreak lore"}},{q="What happened to the runner sent to Darnassus?",a="The runner dispatched with a report from the Oracle Tree to Darnassus was ambushed and killed along the glade paths by Bloodfeather harpies before reaching safety.",al={"oracle tree messenger","dead runner darnassus"}},{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is a massive, sentient ancient rooted in the Oracle Glade. It observes the boughs of the World Tree and communicates its wisdom and warnings to the night elf leadership.",al={"oracle tree teldrassil","who is the oracle tree"}},{q="What proof does Sentinel Cloudsbreak require?",a="Sentinel Cloudsbreak requires six Bloodfeather belts taken from the slain harpies as concrete proof that their roosts around the glade have been thinned.",al={"bloodfeather belt quest","how many belts","quest proof"}},{q="What happens after culling the harpies?",a="With the immediate perimeter secured, the Oracle Tree sheds a piece of its own bark, opening a direct line of communication for an adventurer to take its long-delayed message toward Darnassus.",al={"next quest after enchanted glade","what does oracle tree do next"},sp=1}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Defending the ancient spirits of the World Tree and safeguarding Sentinels from harpy defilement is a solemn duty for any kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting the Sentinels in securing the sacred groves of Teldrassil strengthens ties with the night elf leadership in nearby Darnassus.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold the sentient ancients in great reverence; clearing harpy infestations that threaten the Oracle Tree helps protect the glade's natural balance."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","bloodfeather","darnassus","harpies","oracle glade","oracle tree","sentinel","teldrassil","the enchanted glade"},rel={"subzone:oracle-glade","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","quest:940","quest:952","zone:teldrassil","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=937},src={"The Enchanted Glade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:938"] = {t="quest",n="Mist",z="teldrassil",s="Mist is an escort quest in the shaded boughs of Teldrassil. After discovering a wounded gray sabercat abandoned deep in the woods, travelers must shepherd her safely back to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak at a nearby moon well.",h="Mist is an escort quest in the shaded boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Wounded Companion",b="Tucked away amid the wild undergrowth of Teldrassil lies Mist, a distinctive gray sabercat marked by severe, slashing lacerations across her back and belly. Rather than acting as a feral beast of the wilds, Mist exhibits remarkable calm and bright intelligence in her blue eyes, immediately looking to friendly travelers for guidance and protection.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Ambush",b="Mist is the beloved companion of Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak. While patrolling the great boughs near the Oracle Tree, Arynia was caught off guard by foul witches who ambushed the pair and separated them. Believing her loyal pet had met a bloody end, Arynia withdrew in grief to the tranquility of a local moon well, where she desperately hoped against hope for Mist's survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mist?",a="Mist is a loyal gray sabercat companion belonging to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak. She is found injured in the forests of Teldrassil after being separated from her master during a violent ambush.",al={"mist cat","what is mist","who is the sabercat"}},{q="Who injured Mist?",a="Mist and her master were ambushed by local witches lurking within the woods of Teldrassil. The attackers managed to separate the pair and inflicted deep lacerations across the cat's back and stomach.",al={"who hurt mist","why is mist bleeding","witches ambush mist"}},{q="Where should Mist be escorted?",a="Mist needs to be brought safely to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak, who is stationed beside the moon well near the Oracle Tree.",al={"where do i take mist","mist turn in","mist destination"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel stationed in Teldrassil. She serves the safety of the boughs and deeply mourned Mist, blaming herself for letting the forest's witches catch them unaware.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak","cloudsbreak","mist owner"}},{q="Why are night elf Sentinels bonded with sabercats?",a="Night elf Sentinels have fought alongside the great cats of Kalimdor for millennia, relying on them as fierce partners in skirmishes, scouts in the shadowy boughs, and trusted lifelong companions.",al={"night elf cat companions","sentinel sabercats","why sabercats"}},{q="Where is the Oracle Tree in relation to this rescue?",a="The Oracle Tree sits in southern Teldrassil, with a nearby moon well providing holy waters where Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak tends to her duties and mourns her lost scout companion.",al={"oracle tree location","moon well mist"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The bond between Sentinel and sabercat is a cornerstone of night elf warfare and forest lore; rescuing Mist upholds that ancient, sacred companionship.",["class:Hunter"]="Any beastmaster will recognize the fierce devotion and intelligent gaze in Mist's eyes, making her safe return to her partner a matter of professional pride.",["faction:Alliance"]="Aiding the Sentinels in Teldrassil cements vital goodwill between the fledgling Alliance and the kaldorei defenders of the world tree."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","mist","moon well","oracle tree","sabercat","sentinel","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Mist",["end"]="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",faction="Alliance",id=938},src={"Mist (quest)"}}
E["quest:940"] = {t="quest",n="Teldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Following the cleansing of the rogue harpies near the Oracle Tree, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak entrusts you with carrying a status report to Darnassus. The inscribed bark is addressed to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm, bearing news of the state of the boughs and the ongoing corruption plaguing the World Tree.",h="Following the cleansing of the rogue harpies near the Oracle Tree, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak entrusts you...",sec={{t="A Messenger to the Stone City",b="Deep in the boughs of Teldrassil, the Oracle Tree watches over the forest. After clearing the harpies from their nests in the Enchanted Glade, Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak decides it is finally safe to dispatch word to the kaldorei leadership. Entrusting you with a piece of inscribed bark, she sends you across the wilderness and into Darnassus—the great 'forest of stone'—to deliver the Oracle Tree's report directly to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm.",sp=0},{t="Staghelm's Ambition and Frustration",b="When presented with the report, Fandral Staghelm receives it with mixed feelings. Though grateful for the news that the harpies were pushed back, the report underlines a deeper truth: as soon as one threat is diminished on Teldrassil, another festers in its place. For Staghelm, who championed the planting of the new World Tree to reclaim the night elves' lost immortality, the ongoing afflictions of the boughs are a bitter reminder that his grand work remains far from finished.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the quest 'Teldrassil'?",a="This quest acts as a narrative bridge connecting your wilderness adventures around the Oracle Tree to the capital city. Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak tasks you with carrying an Inscribed Bark containing the Oracle Tree's report to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"teldrassil quest objective","what does this quest do","teldrassil delivery"}},{q="Who is Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak?",a="Arynia Cloudsbreak is a night elf Sentinel stationed near the Oracle Tree in the Teldrassil wilds. She monitors regional threats like the local Bloodfeather harpies and coordinates forest defenses with Darnassus.",al={"arynia cloudsbreak lore","who starts teldrassil quest"}},{q="Why does Arynia call Darnassus a 'forest of stone'?",a="While the night elves live within the canopy of the World Tree, the city of Darnassus is built with monumental marble and stone temples, bridges, and pavilions. Compared to the untamed wilderness around the Oracle Tree, the capital is a constructed forest of stone.",al={"forest of stone meaning","why forest of stone"}},{q="Why is Fandral Staghelm so concerned about the Oracle Tree's report?",a="Staghelm spearheaded the creation of Teldrassil in hopes of regaining kaldorei immortality after Nordrassil was damaged in the Third War. News from the Oracle Tree confirms that Teldrassil continues to suffer from spreading corruption and wildlife turmoil, putting his ambitions in jeopardy.",al={"fandral staghelm reaction","why is staghelm worried"}},{q="What quest leads into this, and what follows it?",a="This quest immediately follows 'The Enchanted Glade', where you deal with the harpies menacing the Oracle Tree. After delivering the report to Arch Druid Staghelm, he sends you onward to Darkshore with the follow-up quest 'Grove of the Ancients'.",al={"teldrassil quest chain","what quest next"}},{q="Where can Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm be found?",a="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm resides in Darnassus, standing at the summit of the Cenarion Enclave where he oversees the druids of the Cenarion Circle and guides the governance of the kaldorei.",al={"where is fandral","fandral staghelm location"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Delivering this report brings you face-to-face with Arch Druid Staghelm, revealing his personal obsession with restoring kaldorei immortality through the troubled boughs of Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Carrying word from the ancient Oracle Tree directly to the leader of the Cenarion Circle highlights the ongoing struggle to cleanse Teldrassil's natural balance.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions completing their early duties on the island, this mission provides a formal introduction to the night elf capital and its stern leadership."},kw={"arynia cloudsbreak","cenarion enclave","darnassus","fandral staghelm","immortality","inscribed bark","kaldorei","oracle tree","teldrassil"},rel={"npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:sentinel-arynia-cloudsbreak","quest:937","quest:952","zone:darnassus","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid"},m={start="Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak",["end"]="Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm",level="11",faction="Alliance",id=940},src={"Teldrassil (quest)"}}
E["quest:941"] = {t="quest",n="Planting the Heart",z="teldrassil",s="Planting the Heart is a task undertaken for the herbalist Denalan by the shores of Lake Al'Ameth in Teldrassil. After stripping away the suffocating moss from a strange wooden heart taken from a corrupted timberling, Denalan tests whether his specially enriched soil can cleanse and heal the lingering taint within it.",h="Planting the Heart is a task undertaken for the herbalist Denalan by the shores of Lake Al'Ameth in...",sec={{t="A Second Chance at Life",b="While examining the strange wooden organ recovered from the corrupted timberling known as Blackmoss the Fetid, Denalan manages to scrape away the foul moss strangling its surface. Yet despite his efforts, a deeper, unnatural taint still pulses within the wood. Rather than burn or discard it, Denalan relies on his lifelong craft of botany and soil tending. He instructs travelers to bury the heart directly into his personal planter box, trusting the rich nutrients he blended to coax whatever natural vitality remains back toward health.",sp=0},{t="The Miracle of Enriched Earth",b="Placing the blackened wooden heart into Denalan's planter yields an unexpected reaction. The moment it touches the fertile soil, the heart burrows into the dirt as if guided by primal instinct. Moments later, it re-emerges to the surface, cleansed of its foul corruption and pulsing with a gentle, companionable warmth. By purifying the seed of a fallen, tainted creature, Denalan demonstrates that even when the wild denizens of Teldrassil fall prey to unnatural blights, careful nurturing and sacred earth can still restore harmony.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this tainted heart come from?",a="The heart originally came from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling lurking along the shores of Lake Al'Ameth. It was recovered choked with tangled, foul moss before Denalan scraped it clean.",al={"heart origin","where did the heart come from","blackmoss heart"}},{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf botanist and herbalist who tends an isolated camp on the island in Lake Al'Ameth. He spends his days studying Teldrassil's plant life, investigating the strange corruption creeping through the boughs, and mixing enriched soils.",al={"who is denalan","denalan lore"}},{q="Why put the heart in a planter instead of destroying it?",a="Denalan believes in understanding and healing nature rather than merely destroying corrupted beings. He hopes the nutritive soil he prepared can purge the taint and restore the heart's original, pure vitality.",al={"why plant the heart","why heal the heart"}},{q="What happens when you bury the heart?",a="The heart immediately burrows into the soil upon contact. Seconds later, it wriggles back to the surface completely cleansed of its foul taint, pulsing gently as an animated companion.",al={"what happens in the planter","heart burrows"},sp=1},{q="Does this cure the corruption of the timberlings?",a="It cures only this single salvaged heart. While it proves that individual botanical spirits can be cleansed with care and rich soil, the overarching corruption spreading across Teldrassil remains an active danger.",al={"are timberlings cured","curing timberlings"}},{q="Why is the soil in Denalan's planter special?",a="Denalan has spent considerable time experimenting with compost and nutritive soil blends around Lake Al'Ameth, designing dirt potent enough to revitalize sickly flora and purge creeping decay.",al={"denalan soil","planter soil"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For a druid, witnessing a corrupted timberling's core cleansed through rich earth offers a reassuring sign that the unnatural taint afflicting the World Tree's boughs can still be turned back through natural care.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan's mastery over nutrient-rich soil and botanical rejuvenation showcases the vital link between studying the earth and mending damaged plant life.",["race:NightElf"]="Restoring living wood and coaxing life from fallen forest spirits reflects the kaldorei commitment to stewarding nature even in the face of Teldrassil's troubling ailments."},kw={"blackmoss the fetid","cleansed heart","denalan","lake al'ameth","planter","tainted heart","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","quest:927","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Denalan",["end"]="Denalan's Planter",faction="Alliance",id=941},src={"Planting the Heart"}}
E["quest:96630"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="teldrassil",s="The Adventurer is a brief quest set in Teldrassil involving the discovery of a discarded journal in the wilds. The plain notebook recounts the humble travels and camping outings of an unknown traveler, intended for delivery to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.",h="The Adventurer is a brief quest set in Teldrassil involving the discovery of a discarded journal in the wilds.",sec={{t="A Wanderer's Journal",b="Amid the dense boughs and tangled roots of Teldrassil, travelers occasionally stumble across abandoned personal items. This simple journal recounts the unremarkable yet earnest wanderings of a nameless adventurer. Instead of grand heroics or perilous monster hunts, the bulk of its pages enthusiastically document the simple joys of making camp beneath the twilight canopy.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Dolanaar",b="Rather than leaving the personal keepsake to weather in the damp wilderness, the finder is drawn to carry it toward Dolanaar. Lyreena Duskblade, stationed near the night elf settlement, serves as the recipient for the displaced pages, perhaps offering closure or insight into whose travels were left behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the journal mentioned in the quest?",a="It is a plain personal notebook recovered in the wilds of Teldrassil. Its entries detail the quiet life and travels of an unfamiliar figure, highlighting ordinary adventures and an enduring fondness for camping outdoors.",al={"lost journal","what is the book","the adventurer journal"}},{q="Who is Lyreena Duskblade?",a="Lyreena Duskblade is a night elf found near Dolanaar. She is the intended recipient of the lost journal found out in the forest.",al={"lyreena","where is lyreena duskblade","turn in npc"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest takes place in Teldrassil, the great bough of the night elves, focused in the wilderness surrounding the village of Dolanaar.",al={"where is the adventurer quest","quest zone"}},{q="Does the journal describe dangerous monsters or battles?",a="No. The writing is described as quite plain and focuses on the unassuming life and wanderings of an unknown individual, with particular emphasis on how enjoyable camping can be.",al={"journal lore","what is in the journal","what does it say"}},{q="Who can complete this task?",a="This task is strictly for members of the Alliance wandering the starter territory of Teldrassil, particularly novice night elves venturing near Dolanaar.",al={"can horde do this","alliance quest"}},{q="Why turn the journal in to Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the central gathering post and crossroad for that region of Teldrassil, making it the most sensible place to deliver misplaced personal belongings to local sentinels and wardens like Lyreena Duskblade.",al={"why dolanaar","why lyreena"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Young night elves patrolling Teldrassil often find signs of travelers passing through, turning over lost personal relics to sentinels like Lyreena Duskblade.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance novices finding their footing beneath the World Tree, returning misplaced belongings to local scouts helps maintain order in the groves."},kw={"camping","dolanaar","journal","lost journal","lyreena duskblade","teldrassil","the adventurer"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil"},m={start="Object #654846",["end"]="Lyreena Duskblade",level="6",faction="Alliance",id=96630},src={"The Adventurer (Teldrassil)"},fv=true}
E["quest:997"] = {t="quest",n="Denalan's Earth",z="teldrassil",s="Denalan's Earth is an errand running south from the settlement of Dolanaar to the tranquil waters of Lake Al'Ameth. Syral Bladeleaf asks travelers to hand-deliver a delayed shipment of rare, enriched soil to her botanical colleague, Denalan, who studies the boughs and flora of the new World Tree.",h="Denalan's Earth is an errand running south from the settlement of Dolanaar to the tranquil waters of Lake...",sec={{t="A Courier for Dolanaar",b="As travelers pass through Dolanaar on their way south toward Lake Al'Ameth, Syral Bladeleaf flags them down with an overdue errand. Her fellow researcher, Denalan, ordered a special package of rare earth all the way from Darnassus to support his ongoing botanical studies. The parcel was delayed in transit and only recently arrived in Dolanaar. Rather than letting the rich soil spoil or sit idle, Syral seeks an accommodating courier willing to walk it down the forest trail to Denalan's lakeside campsite.",sp=0},{t="Cultivating Teldrassil",b="Denalan maintains a solitary workstation along the eastern shores of Lake Al'Ameth, where he observes how Teldrassil's sapling ecosystem takes root. Teldrassil is young, having grown rapidly in the wake of Mount Hyjal's cataclysm, and its flora behaves in unexpected ways. Denalan uses unique soil mixtures and specimens to test the vitality and behavior of the island's timberlings and native plants, making the fresh shipment of rare earth crucial to his experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Denalan?",a="Denalan is a night elf researcher and herbalist who has set up camp on the eastern shores of Lake Al'Ameth. He dedicates his time to studying, cultivating, and experimenting on Teldrassil's unique plant life.",al={"denalan lore","who is denalan","denalan npc"}},{q="Where is Syral Bladeleaf located?",a="Syral Bladeleaf resides in Dolanaar, the main night elf outpost in central Teldrassil, where she coordinates research supplies and assists travelers journeying across the boughs.",al={"syral bladeleaf location","where is syral"}},{q="What is the rare earth used for?",a="The shipment contains specially enriched soil sent from the capital of Darnassus. Denalan relies on it to nurture experimental plantings and test how Teldrassil's native saplings, like timberlings, react to diverse growing conditions.",al={"what does denalan need the earth for","rare earth purpose"}},{q="Where is Lake Al'Ameth?",a="Lake Al'Ameth lies south of Dolanaar and just east of Shadowglen, forming a peaceful body of water nestled among the southern roots of Teldrassil.",al={"lake al'ameth location","how to get to lake al'ameth"}},{q="Why was the shipment late?",a="The package had to travel out from Darnassus and encountered unspecified transit delays along Teldrassil's winding roads before finally reaching the distribution hub in Dolanaar.",al={"why was the earth late","delayed parcel"}},{q="What does delivering this earth lead to?",a="Upon receiving the rare soil, Denalan recruits the courier to help gather timberling sprouts and seeds along the lake's shores, beginning a deeper series of botanical field studies.",al={"denalan earth follow up","what comes next"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Herbalists will appreciate Denalan's lakeside retreat, as his experiments center on understanding the fragile, burgeoning plant life unique to the newly grown World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids share a natural affinity with Denalan's efforts, as tracking the growth and balance of Teldrassil's flora is essential to safeguarding nature on the new bough.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves emerging from Shadowglen, assisting Syral and Denalan serves as an early introduction to the wider stewardship required to sustain Teldrassil."},kw={"darnassus","denalan","dolanaar","lake al'ameth","rare earth","syral bladeleaf","teldrassil","timberling"},rel={"npc:denalan","npc:syral-bladeleaf","subzone:lake-al-ameth","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:night-elf","topic:alliance"},m={start="Syral Bladeleaf",["end"]="Denalan",faction="Alliance",id=997},src={"Denalan's Earth"}}
E["subzone:aldrassil"] = {t="subzone",n="Aldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Aldrassil is the colossal bough-tree and settlement nestled at the heart of Shadowglen in northeastern Teldrassil. Serving as the primary refuge and training ground for young kaldorei, its carved hollows shelter trainers, merchants, and local leadership.",h="Aldrassil is the colossal bough-tree and settlement nestled at the heart of Shadowglen in northeastern...",sec={{t="Heart of Shadowglen",b="Rising high above the secluded vale of Shadowglen, Aldrassil functions as both shelter and civic hub for young night elves taking their first steps in the world. Built into and around the colossal trunk of this ancient growth, winding ramps lead past class trainers and artisans to the high roost where Tenaron Stormgrip oversees the glade's protection. While the world bough Teldrassil stretches across the horizon, Aldrassil provides a safe, grounded canopy where novices learn their arts before venturing down into the troubled wilds of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Aldrassil?",a="Aldrassil is the massive, hollowed-out tree and settlement situated in the center of Shadowglen, northeastern Teldrassil. It serves as the starting haven where young night elves gather training, goods, and guidance.",al={"aldrassil tree","what is aldrassil","shadowglen big tree"}},{q="Who leads the settlement at Aldrassil?",a="Tenaron Stormgrip oversees Shadowglen from his roost at the very top of Aldrassil, coordinating the defense of the vale and guiding newly awakened kaldorei.",al={"who leads aldrassil","aldrassil leader","tenaron stormgrip location"}},{q="What services can be found here?",a="The tree houses class trainers for young night elf warriors, rogues, druids, hunters, and priests, alongside local supply merchants, armorers, and questgivers attending to the immediate needs of the glade.",al={"trainers in aldrassil","vendors aldrassil","what is in aldrassil"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For many young kaldorei, the carved hollows and ramps of Aldrassil are their first memory of civic life and the foundation of their early training.",["class:Druid"]="Aldrassil demonstrates the kaldorei affinity for living architecture, shaped from living wood without breaking the balance of the forest."},kw={"aldrassil","great tree","kaldorei","night elf starting","shadowglen","teldrassil","tenaron stormgrip"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","npc:tenaron-stormgrip","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Aldrassil"}}
E["subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Ban'ethil Barrow Den",z="teldrassil",s="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred subterranean sanctuary hollowed out within the roots of Teldrassil. Originally created as a resting place for the sleeping Druids of the Talon, the cavern complex has recently fallen into chaos. The corrupted furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe have overrun its chambers, turning a place of peaceful slumber into a perilous den of madness.",h="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a sacred subterranean sanctuary hollowed out within the roots of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Barrow dens serve as sacred resting chambers where night elf druids slumber while projecting their spirits into the Emerald Dream. Ban'ethil Barrow Den was dedicated specifically to sheltering the Druids of the Talon as they communed with nature. Divided into upper and lower subterranean chambers, the den once resonated with tranquil reverie and deep meditative magic. However, the affliction sweeping Teldrassil's wildlife did not spare the Gnarlpine furbolgs, who invaded the complex, turning its hollowed halls into a fortified warren.",sp=0},{t="The Gnarlpine Incursion",b="Driven mad by mysterious corruption taking root across the World Tree, the Gnarlpine tribe drove out or endangered the slumbering druids within Ban'ethil. The furbolgs now fiercely guard the winding tunnels, aggressive toward any night elf who approaches. For the defenders of Teldrassil, reclaiming the barrow den is an urgent priority, not merely to drive back the hostile furbolgs, but to protect the vulnerable druids and sacred relics trapped within its lower depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="Ban'ethil Barrow Den is a subterranean hollow in Teldrassil crafted by the night elves. It was designed to shelter sleeping Druids of the Talon while their spirits roamed the Emerald Dream.",al={"what is ban'ethil","ban'ethil barrow den purpose","what is this cave"}},{q="Why are there furbolgs inside Ban'ethil Barrow Den?",a="The Gnarlpine furbolgs have fallen victim to a spreading corruption affecting Teldrassil's creatures. Driven hostile and territorial, they invaded the barrow den, displacing the keepers and threatening the slumbering druids.",al={"why are gnarlpine in ban'ethil","furbolgs in barrow den","who took over ban'ethil"}},{q="What are the sections of the barrow den?",a="The cavern complex is split into two primary interconnected tiers: the Upper Den near the entrance passages and the Lower Den deeper in the subterranean roots.",al={"ban'ethil layout","upper den lower den","ban'ethil levels"}},{q="Why are barrow dens so important to druids?",a="Barrow dens provide safe, secure physical shelter for druids who enter prolonged, deep slumbers to project their consciousness into the Emerald Dream, leaving their waking bodies helpless for years or decades.",al={"why do druids sleep in barrows","druid barrow dens lore","emerald dream barrow den"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Ban'ethil represents sacred ground for the Cenarion Circle, specifically built to protect Druids of the Talon while communing with the Emerald Dream.",["race:NightElf"]="The occupation of Ban'ethil by corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs is an alarming sign of the growing sickness plaguing their new home of Teldrassil."},kw={"ban'ethil","barrow den","druids of the talon","emerald dream","furbolg","gnarlpine","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:furbolg","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Ban'ethil Barrow Den"}}
E["subzone:ban-ethil-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Ban'ethil Hollow",z="teldrassil",s="Ban'ethil Hollow is a rugged ravine cutting into the woodland just south of the main road connecting Dolanaar and Darnassus. It has become a dangerous haven for corrupted, aggressive furbolgs who pose a constant threat to travelers. Tucked away in the back of the ravine lies the entrance to the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.",h="Ban'ethil Hollow is a rugged ravine cutting into the woodland just south of the main road connecting Dolanaar...",sec={{t="A Perilous Ravine",b="Situated off the highway between Dolanaar and Darnassus, Ban'ethil Hollow is a sharp reminder that the boughs of Teldrassil are not entirely safe. Furbolgs driven mad by the strange affliction plaguing the World Tree have taken refuge throughout the rocky descent. They frequently stalk the nearby path, waiting to ambush unwary couriers and wandering sentinels. Deep within the ravine sits the threshold of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den, where slumbering druids and ancient tunnels face encroachment from the maddened beasts outside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Ban'ethil Hollow located?",a="Ban'ethil Hollow is a ravine in central Teldrassil, located just south of the primary road running between the village of Dolanaar and the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"banethil hollow location","where is ban'ethil hollow","find banethil hollow"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="The furbolgs across Teldrassil have succumbed to a spreading corruption and madness that grips the World Tree's wildlife. Instead of living peacefully alongside the night elves as they historically have, these tribes have become fiercely territorial and violent.",al={"why are furbolgs mad","hostile furbolgs banethil","banethil furbolg attack"}},{q="What is inside the Ban'ethil Barrow Den at the back of the hollow?",a="The Ban'ethil Barrow Den is an underground complex historically used by night elven druids to enter deep hibernation and commune with the Emerald Dream. However, with corruption rising in the hollow, the den has become dangerous ground.",al={"what is in the barrow den","banethil barrow den","den in banethil hollow"}},{q="Is the road above the hollow safe to travel?",a="The main road is generally patrolled by night elf sentinels, but furbolgs from Ban'ethil Hollow often venture up from the ravine to ambush travelers. Travelers making the journey between Dolanaar and Darnassus should remain on their guard.",al={"is the road safe","furbolg ambushes","road to darnassus safe"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the furbolgs fall to madness so close to the road between Dolanaar and Darnassus is a grim sign of Teldrassil's mounting sickness, requiring young sentinels and druids to step in.",["class:Druid"]="The hollow conceals the entrance to Ban'ethil Barrow Den, sacred ground where druids traditionally rest to commune with the Emerald Dream, now endangered by rabid wildlife."},kw={"ambush","ban'ethil barrow den","ban'ethil hollow","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","ravine","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:ban-ethil-barrow-den","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg"},src={"Ban'ethil Hollow"}}
E["subzone:cleft"] = {t="subzone",n="Cleft",z="teldrassil",s="The Cleft is a darkened hollow located northwest of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Once a tranquil corner of the boughs, it has been claimed by the corrupted Gnarlpine furbolgs, who use it as a stronghold to ambush travelers moving along the main highway toward Darnassus.",h="The Cleft is a darkened hollow located northwest of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="Situated off the highway between Dolanaar and Darnassus, the Cleft has turned into one of the most perilous dens on the world tree. Driven mad by the foul taint spreading through Teldrassil, the resident Gnarlpine furbolgs have fortified this subterranean rift under the command of their vicious chieftain, Ursal the Mauler. From this redoubt, the maddened beasts terrorize the local roads, capturing unvigilant night elves and threatening to cut Dolanaar off from the capital.",sp=0},{t="The Roadway Ambushers",b="The threat posed by the Cleft grew dire enough that Moon Priestess Amara and her sentinels were forced to establish a defensive watch along the road outside its entrance. The furbolgs within carried out brazen kidnappings, dragging slumbering night elf druids into the depths of the cave to perform dark rituals. Cleansing the Cleft and slaying Ursal is crucial for the Sentinels to secure the primary artery connecting Teldrassil's villages to Darnassus.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Cleft?",a="The Cleft is a furbolg den located in the boughs of Teldrassil, situated northwest of Dolanaar along the main road that leads toward Darnassus.",al={"what is the cleft","the cleft teldrassil","cleft location"}},{q="Who controls the Cleft?",a="It is occupied by hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs who have fallen victim to Teldrassil's creeping corruption. Their local leader within the cavern is a powerful brute named Ursal the Mauler.",al={"who lives in the cleft","cleft enemies","who rules the cleft"}},{q="Why are the night elves fighting here?",a="The Gnarlpine inside the Cleft have been ambushing travelers along the road to Darnassus. Worse, they kidnapped slumbering druids and held them captive inside the den, forcing Moon Priestess Amara and the Sentinels to intervene.",al={"why attack the cleft","cleft night elf quests","road to darnassus"}},{q="Is the Cleft related to the Cleft of Shadow?",a="No. Despite having a similar name, this Cleft is a furbolg cave in Teldrassil, whereas the Cleft of Shadow is the dark subterranean cavern located inside the Horde capital of Orgrimmar.",al={"cleft of shadow connection","cleft vs cleft of shadow"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Cleft represents a painful tragedy for night elves, watching their longtime furbolg allies succumb to madness and capture sacred druids from their slumber.",["class:Druid"]="The Gnarlpine inside the Cleft dared to abduct dreaming druids from their trances, turning a sacred restorative process into a dangerous trap."},kw={"cleft","darnassus","dolanaar","furbolg","gnarlpine","moon priestess amara","ursal the mauler"},rel={"quest:486","quest:487","npc:moon-priestess-amara","topic:furbolg","subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","subzone:cleft-of-shadow"},src={"Cleft"}}
E["subzone:darnassus"] = {t="subzone",n="Darnassus",z="teldrassil",s="High amidst the sweeping boughs of Teldrassil stands Darnassus, the capital refuge of the kaldorei. Built along tranquil waters and verdant groves, it serves as the spiritual heart of the night elves and the primary Alliance bastion on northern Kalimdor. From here, High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind and Archdruid Fandral Staghelm guide their people through the trials of newfound mortality.",h="High amidst the sweeping boughs of Teldrassil stands Darnassus, the capital refuge of the kaldorei.",sec={{t="Sanctuary in the Boughs",b="Constructed in the aftermath of the Third War, Darnassus was founded to honor the survival of the night elf people after the loss of their sacred World Tree, Nordrassil. Unlike the dense stone metropolises of Ironforge or Stormwind, Darnassus is an open, tranquil settlement of wood-crafted lodges, glowing shrines, and arched bridges spanning crystalline lakes. Vigilant Sentinels, towering ancients of war, and tree-shaping druids keep watch over the paths, ensuring that the peaceful quiet of nature is preserved within the city's borders.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Leadership",b="While Darnassus represents the unity of the kaldorei, its governance reflects subtle fractures. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind presides over civil and military matters from the radiant Temple of the Moon, surrounded by the Sisters of Elune. Meanwhile, the Cenarion Circle's affairs fall under Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who championed the planting of Teldrassil to restore the elves' lost immortality. With Malfurion Stormrage lost in a mysterious slumber deep within the Emerald Dream, Staghelm's aggressive vision for their future frequently creates friction with the more patient priesthood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Darnassus?",a="High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind serves as the primary leader of night elf society from the Temple of the Moon, commanding the Sentinels. Druidic affairs are directed by Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who leads the Cenarion Circle in the absence of Malfurion Stormrage.",al={"darnassus leader","who is in charge of darnassus","night elf leader"}},{q="How do travelers reach Darnassus from outside Teldrassil?",a="Because Darnassus sits atop the massive boughs of a World Tree island, ships and flight paths connect only to Rut'theran Village at the tree's base. From Rut'theran, a magical portal transports visitors up into the city proper.",al={"how to get to darnassus","darnassus entrance","getting into darnassus"}},{q="Why was Darnassus founded so recently?",a="Following the destruction at Mount Hyjal during the Third War, the night elves lost their immortality and their ancient way of life. Fandral Staghelm and his allies planted Teldrassil off the coast of Kalimdor, and Darnassus took root upon its branches as a fresh sanctuary for their people.",al={"why is darnassus new","when was darnassus built","darnassus age"}},{q="Where is Malfurion Stormrage?",a="Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage is missing, his spirit trapped in a deep, unexplained slumber within the Emerald Dream. His absence leaves leadership of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus entirely to Fandral Staghelm.",al={"where is malfurion","is malfurion in darnassus","malfurion status"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Darnassus is the cultural and political capital of the kaldorei, serving as your people's fresh start and sovereign refuge after the harrowing sacrifices of the Third War.",["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers from the Eastern Kingdoms, Darnassus is a secluded, serene haven that stands as the Alliance's essential anchor on the continent of Kalimdor."},kw={"capital","darnassus","kaldorei","staghelm","teldrassil","temple of the moon","tyrande"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","subzone:rut-theran-village","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:malfurion-stormrage","topic:alliance","topic:sentinels"},src={"Darnassus"}}
E["subzone:dolanaar"] = {t="subzone",n="Dolanaar",z="teldrassil",s="Dolanaar is a tranquil night elf settlement nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil. Situated just southwest of Shadowglen, it serves as the first true town young kal'dorei encounter after departing their sheltered training grounds. Here, rangers, druids, and craftsmen gather to guide newcomers and address the strange, encroaching afflictions disturbing the World Tree.",h="Dolanaar is a tranquil night elf settlement nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Crossroads of Boughs",b="Resting beneath the lush canopy southwest of Shadowglen, Dolanaar serves as a vital crossway for travelers traversing Teldrassil. Built in the traditional night elven manner, its homes and platforms sit seamlessly woven into the woodland. The village provides newcomers with their first comprehensive training in trades, martial arts, and nature crafts, as well as a direct hippogryph connection to the capital city of Darnassus. Because of its central location, reports of corrupted wildlife, aggressive furbolgs, and foul mosses from the surrounding boughs inevitably find their way into Dolanaar's council.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dolanaar?",a="Dolanaar is the primary questing hub and outpost for young night elves leaving the novice grounds of Shadowglen. It acts as an administrative outpost in eastern Teldrassil, housing tradesfolk, trainers for martial and magical arts, and links to the capital.",al={"what is dolanaar","dolanaar purpose","why dolanaar matters"}},{q="Where is Dolanaar located?",a="Dolanaar lies in the central-eastern region of Teldrassil, just a short walk down the trail southwest of Shadowglen and east of the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"dolanaar location","where is dolanaar","dolanaar directions"}},{q="How can travelers reach Darnassus from here?",a="Dolanaar maintains a flight path serviced by night elf hippogryphs, allowing travelers to quickly fly directly to Darnassus without navigating the overland paths.",al={"travel to darnassus","flight master dolanaar","dolanaar to darnassus"}},{q="What threats affect Dolanaar?",a="The woodland surrounding Dolanaar suffers from a strange corruption creeping into Teldrassil, leading to diseased beasts, crazed timberlings, and hostile furbolg tribes nearby.",al={"trouble in dolanaar","dolanaar problems","dolanaar quests"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, Dolanaar marks their first steps into the wider world, testing their vows to preserve nature as they witness the growing corruption upon the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Dolanaar is an essential stop for initiates seeking guidance on Teldrassil's ailments and learning to attune their spirits to the natural balance."},kw={"darnassus","dolanaar","kaldorei","night elf town","shadowglen","teldrassil"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dolanaar"}}
E["subzone:fel-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Fel Rock",z="teldrassil",s="Fel Rock is a blighted cavern hidden within the woods just north of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil. Once a tranquil hollow, it has fallen into corruption under the influence of the satyr Lord Melenas and his horde of vicious grells.",h="Fel Rock is a blighted cavern hidden within the woods just north of Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Den of Corruption",b="Tucked away in the forested hills north of Dolanaar, Fel Rock was once an ordinary, peaceful cavern carved into the wood and stone of Teldrassil. Today, it stands as an unsettling reminder of the creeping taint encroaching on the world tree. Twisted roots and unnatural shadows dominate the cavern interior, overrun by swarms of wild grells and grellkin.",sp=0},{t="The Satyr's Hold",b="The corruption within Fel Rock stems from the presence of Lord Melenas, a wicked satyr who has claimed the hollow as a stronghold. From deep within the cave, he orchestrates the spread of malevolent corruption right under the watchful gaze of the night elf sentinels. Druids from Dolanaar, particularly Tallonkai Swiftroot, actively enlist capable defenders to cleanse the cave and slay Melenas before his foul blight can spread further into the surrounding woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Fel Rock located?",a="Fel Rock is located in central Teldrassil, tucked into the hills directly north of the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"fel rock location","where is fel rock","find fel rock"}},{q="Who rules Fel Rock?",a="The cavern is commanded by Lord Melenas, a vile satyr who has made Fel Rock his lair and gathered a host of grells to do his bidding.",al={"who is in fel rock","boss of fel rock","lord melenas location"}},{q="Why are druids concerned about Fel Rock?",a="The presence of a satyr and fel-tainted grells within the world tree's boughs poses an immediate threat to the natural balance of Teldrassil. Druids like Tallonkai Swiftroot dispatch adventurers to cut down Lord Melenas and stem the corruption.",al={"why clean fel rock","fel rock quest","tallonkai swiftroot quest"}},{q="What creatures dwell inside the cavern?",a="Inside Fel Rock, you will encounter aggressive grells, grellkin, and their dark master, the satyr Lord Melenas.",al={"fel rock mobs","what is inside fel rock","fel rock enemies"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the presence of a satyr like Lord Melenas so close to Dolanaar is an alarming affront to Teldrassil that demands swift retribution.",["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle view Fel Rock as a festering wound on the young world tree, requiring immediate purging before demonic corruption spreads."},kw={"dolanaar","fel rock","grell","lord melenas","satyr","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil"},rel={"quest:932","subzone:dolanaar","npc:tallonkai-swiftroot","topic:satyr","zone:teldrassil","topic:druid","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Fel Rock"}}
E["subzone:gnarlpine-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Gnarlpine Hold",z="teldrassil",s="Gnarlpine Hold is a secluded hollow located in the far southwestern reaches of Teldrassil. Once a dwelling place of the native Gnarlpine furbolg tribe, the hold has succumbed to foul demonic corruption, becoming a volatile front line for the defenders of the boughs.",h="Gnarlpine Hold is a secluded hollow located in the far southwestern reaches of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Bastion",b="Tucked away in the southwestern corner of Teldrassil, Gnarlpine Hold was historically inhabited by the local Gnarlpine furbolgs. In recent times, dark demonic corruption has taken root deep within the hollow, displacing or tainting its former residents and bringing forth sinister fiends. A persistent stream of demonic invaders now spills northward from the hold, where the dryad Tarindrella and the stalwart ancients of Teldrassil hold the line in an ongoing battle to cleanse the World Tree.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Gnarlpine Hold located?",a="Gnarlpine Hold lies tucked away in the far southwestern corner of the World Tree Teldrassil, southwest of Dolanaar.",al={"gnarlpine hold location","where is gnarlpine hold"}},{q="Who originally lived here?",a="The hollow was formally home to the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe before corruption spread across their settlements and displaced them.",al={"who lives in gnarlpine hold","gnarlpine hold inhabitants"}},{q="Why are there demons in Gnarlpine Hold?",a="Demonic corruption has recently seized the hollow, manifesting directly within its borders and turning the once-peaceful furbolg haven into an active breach of foul entities threatening Teldrassil.",al={"demons in teldrassil","why demons gnarlpine"}},{q="Who is fighting against the corruption coming from the hold?",a="Just north of the hold, the dryad Tarindrella and several awakened Teldrassil ancients stand vigilant, confronting the demonic forces that spill out from the corruption below.",al={"who fights the demons here","tarindrella fight"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The demonic presence in Gnarlpine Hold represents a direct violation of Teldrassil's sanctity, prompting swift action from local dryads, ancients, and night elf defenders.",["class:Druid"]="For druids attuned to the health of the World Tree, the blight and demonic intrusion festering within Gnarlpine Hold are a stark reminder of the fragile balance on Teldrassil."},kw={"demons","furbolg","gnarlpine","gnarlpine hold","tarindrella","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg"},src={"Gnarlpine Hold"}}
E["subzone:lake-al-ameth"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Al'Ameth",z="teldrassil",s="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest freshwater bodies nestled high in the boughs of Teldrassil, located just south of Dolanaar. Though once a tranquil haven featuring little more than a simple wooden jetty, its shores have grown perilous due to the violent agitation of the local plant life.",h="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest freshwater bodies nestled high in the boughs of Teldrassil, located just...",sec={{t="A Troubled Shoreline",b="Resting immediately south of the village of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth serves as a vital natural basin in the heart of Teldrassil. Despite its serene waters and minimal settlement, peace here has evaporated. Swarms of agitated timberlings and timberling sprouts prowl the water's edge, driven mad by an unnatural sickness spreading through the world tree. Druids and researchers from Dolanaar frequently dispatch travelers to these shores to gather seeds and cull the aggressive creatures before the corruption spreads deeper into the surrounding forest.",sp=0},{t="The Roots of Wrath",b="The hostility around Lake Al'Ameth is directly tied to the woodland spirits losing their balance. Massive, corrupted treants like Oakenscowl lurk in the nearby groves, while natural timberlings lash out at any who approach. For the Cenarion Circle, diagnosing and treating the rot around Lake Al'Ameth is an urgent test of whether Teldrassil's unblessed creation can truly be sustained.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lake Al'Ameth located?",a="Lake Al'Ameth lies directly south of the night elf settlement of Dolanaar in eastern Teldrassil.",al={"lake alameth location","where is lake al'ameth","find lake al'ameth"}},{q="Why are the creatures around Lake Al'Ameth hostile?",a="The timberlings and plant life along the shores have fallen victim to a corrupting sickness afflicting Teldrassil, driving previously harmless woodland spriggans and treants into a territorial rage.",al={"why timberlings angry","lake alameth enemies","aggressive timberlings"}},{q="What structures or landmarks are on the lake?",a="The lake is largely wild and undeveloped, featuring only a simple wooden fishing jetty on its northern bank near the path from Dolanaar.",al={"lake alameth pier","dock at lake alameth"}},{q="Who is Oakenscowl?",a="Oakenscowl is a powerful, corrupted ancient lurking near the groves of Lake Al'Ameth. He serves as an embodiment of the violent rot warping the forest creatures in the area.",al={"what is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lake al'ameth"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth is an alarming sign of the ailments troubling their newly raised home, forcing young defenders to protect the surrounding road.",["class:Druid"]="The wild timberlings around the lake offer druids a hands-on study of the unnatural corruption undermining Teldrassil's flora and fauna."},kw={"dolanaar","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seeds"},rel={"subzone:dolanaar","zone:teldrassil","quest:918","quest:919","quest:2499","quest:922","quest:941","quest:940"},src={"Lake Al'Ameth"}}
E["subzone:oracle-glade"] = {t="subzone",n="Oracle Glade",z="teldrassil",s="Nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, the Oracle Glade is a sacred woodland sanctuary home to the wondrous Oracle Tree and the World Tree's premier moonwell. Despite its serene purpose as a center of communion and vigilance, the glade faces constant harassment from encroaching Bloodfeather harpies.",h="Nestled in northwestern Teldrassil, the Oracle Glade is a sacred woodland sanctuary home to the wondrous...",sec={{t="Heart of the Woodland",b="The Oracle Glade rests quietly between Darnassus and Wellspring Lake, serving as a vital nexus of night elven communion with nature. At its center stands the Oracle Tree, an ancient specimen whose massive boughs evoke the silhouette of an eagle perched atop a bear. Nearby shimmers the first and most potent of Teldrassil's sacred moonwells, an oasis of lunar magic bathed in Elune's grace. Alongside the Circle of the Ancients, the Oracle Tree watches over the island boughs, shedding inscribed bark that acts as vital communiques to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm regarding the World Tree's health.",sp=0},{t="A Bough Besieged",b="The glade's tranquility is fragile. Aggressive Bloodfeather harpies have descended upon the grove, establishing roosts among the high branches and threatening the sacred tree. Sentinels dispatched from Darnassus struggle to root out the avian scavengers, who actively harass traveling druids and taint the natural serenity of the moonwell. Travelers passing through the northern boughs must tread lightly, as the harpies strike swiftly at any who venture near their roosts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Oracle Tree?",a="The Oracle Tree is an ancient, magically nurtured tree shaped like a great eagle resting upon a bear. It monitors the growth and health of Teldrassil, shedding inscribed bark containing detailed reports that the druids deliver directly to Archdruid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.",al={"who is the oracle tree","oracle tree lore","talking tree teldrassil"}},{q="Why are harpies attacking the Oracle Glade?",a="The Bloodfeather clan of harpies has nested in the high canopies of the glade, drawn by its untamed wilderness and magical vitality. They violently defend their roosts and harass the Oracle Tree, requiring local Sentinels to keep them contained.",al={"bloodfeather harpies","why harpies here","oracle glade enemies"}},{q="What is the importance of the moonwell in this glade?",a="The pool in the Oracle Glade is the very first and most powerful moonwell established on Teldrassil. It channels the sacred energies of Elune to nourish the surrounding forest and sustain kaldorei druids and priestesses who come to draw upon its waters.",al={"oracle glade moonwell","first moonwell","teldrassil first moonwell"}},{q="Where is the Oracle Glade located?",a="It is located in northwestern Teldrassil, just west of Wellspring Lake. A southern road connects the glade directly back to the main path circling outside the gates of Darnassus.",al={"oracle glade location","where is oracle glade","how to get to oracle glade"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The Oracle Glade represents the tender care required to nurse Teldrassil to fruition, housing the crown's most potent moonwell and a silent watcher that speaks directly to the Cenarion leadership.",["class:Druid"]="For druids of the wild, the Oracle Tree is a living partner in stewardship, offering written records of the land's health shed directly from its very bark."},kw={"bloodfeather","fandral staghelm","harpies","moonwell","oracle glade","oracle tree","teldrassil","wellspring lake"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","quest:940","quest:937","quest:7383","subzone:wellspring-lake","npc:fandral-staghelm","topic:sentinels","zone:darnassus"},src={"Oracle Glade"}}
E["subzone:pools-of-arlithrien"] = {t="subzone",n="Pools of Arlithrien",z="teldrassil",s="The Pools of Arlithrien are a cluster of secluded springs resting in western Teldrassil, just south of the gates to Darnassus. Once a tranquil retreat centered around a sacred moonwell, the area has fallen into neglect and danger as local wildlife and nearby hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs encroached upon it.",h="The Pools of Arlithrien are a cluster of secluded springs resting in western Teldrassil, just south of the...",sec={{t="A Troubled Sanctuary",b="Tucked along the shaded boughs south of Darnassus, the Pools of Arlithrien were originally meant to be a quiet place of natural harmony. At their heart lies a stone moonwell, a vessel for the waters imbued with the grace of Elune. Yet despite its proximity to the night elven capital, the sanctuary has become perilous. Agitated beasts roam the shallows, and the persistent hostility of the displaced Gnarlpine furbolgs forced the night elves to abandon routine upkeep of the site, leaving a peaceful wonder shadowed by the island's growing malaise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Pools of Arlithrien located?",a="The pools are nestled in the western reaches of Teldrassil, located just south of the main bridge and entryway into the capital city of Darnassus.",al={"pools of arlithrien location","where is arlithrien","arlithrien map"}},{q="Why was the moonwell here abandoned?",a="The night elves withdrew from actively tending the moonwell due to mounting danger. Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs established a threatening presence nearby, and aggressive forest wildlife overran the surrounding waters.",al={"why abandoned","arlithrien moonwell abandoned","empty moonwell"}},{q="What threats can travelers find at the pools?",a="Travelers wandering near the pools must contend with aggressive woodland creatures that have taken over the waters, alongside the looming risk posed by nearby territorial Gnarlpine furbolgs.",al={"arlithrien monsters","pools of arlithrien mobs","enemies at pools"}},{q="Can players still use the moonwell at the Pools of Arlithrien?",a="Yes. Though untended and abandoned by the priesthood and druids due to local dangers, the moonwell itself still holds its sacred waters and remains a functional source of lunar essence.",al={"use arlithrien moonwell","is moonwell active","water at pools"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The abandonment of a holy moonwell so close to Darnassus is a troubling reminder to night elves of the corruption and disruption creeping across Teldrassil.",["class:Druid"]="Druids studying the imbalances of Teldrassil see the unruly wildlife and the neglected moonwell here as another sign that the Great Tree lacks nature's true blessing."},kw={"arlithrien","darnassus","furbolg","gnarlpine","moonwell","pools of arlithrien","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","topic:furbolg"},src={"Pools of Arlithrien"}}
E["subzone:rut-theran-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Rut'theran Village",z="teldrassil",s="Rut'theran Village is a coastal haven nestled at the southern base of Teldrassil. Serving as the primary maritime harbor for Darnassus, it connects the secluded World Tree to the mainland of Kalimdor via ferry and hippogryph routes.",h="Rut'theran Village is a coastal haven nestled at the southern base of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="Gateway to the World Tree",b="Perched at the water's edge below the towering heights of Teldrassil, Rut'theran Village acts as the threshold between the night elven capital and the wider world. While Darnassus rests within the boughs high above, Rut'theran provides the logistical foundation required to sustain it. A mystical portal arches beneath the trees, whisking travelers between the shore and Darnassus in an instant. For journeys across the sea, ferry service runs from the village docks directly to Auberdine on the mainland of Darkshore, accompanied by flight masters tending dedicated roosts of trained hippogryphs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to Darnassus from here?",a="Walk up the gentle slope from the docks toward the giant pavilion tent. Stepping directly into the glowing purple portal on the platform will instantly transport you to the Temple Gardens inside Darnassus.",al={"get to darnassus","portal to darnassus","how to reach darnassus"}},{q="Where does the boat from the dock go?",a="The ship docked at Rut'theran Village, the Moonspray, provides passage across the Veiled Sea to the town of Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore.",al={"where does boat go","rut'theran ferry","ruttheran ship route"}},{q="Why is this village down at sea level instead of up in the tree?",a="Teldrassil's canopy is far too elevated for conventional sailing ships or sea trade. Rut'theran Village was established at its roots to provide a sea-level port and roosting ground, linked to the heights via a permanent teleportation gateway.",al={"why is ruttheran at sea level","why bottom of teldrassil"}},{q="Can I fly anywhere from here?",a="Yes. A hippogryph handler operates from the village roost, offering flight routes across the water to Auberdine in Darkshore, as well as specialized transport for Cenarion Circle druids to Moonglade.",al={"rut'theran flight path","where can hippogryph fly"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids passing through Rut'theran Village can catch hippogryph flights directly across northern Kalimdor to the sacred sanctuary of Moonglade.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil to aid the Alliance, Rut'theran Village is the final farewell to the crown of the World Tree before sailing into mainland Kalimdor."},kw={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","docks","hippogryph","moonspray","port","rut'theran","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","zone:darnassus","subzone:auberdine","subzone:moonspray","zone:darkshore","topic:night-elf","topic:druid","quest:5921"},src={"Rut'theran Village"}}
E["subzone:shadowglen"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowglen",z="teldrassil",s="Shadowglen is a secluded, twilit vale nestled within the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil. Dominated by the great barrow-tree Aldrassil, it serves as the safe haven where young night elves take their first steps into service before journeying out into the wider world.",h="Shadowglen is a secluded, twilit vale nestled within the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Sheltered Cradle",b="Tucked away in the northeastern canopy of Teldrassil, Shadowglen is ringed by high ridges that shelter it from the rest of the world. Bathed in eternal dusk, the vale centers on Aldrassil, a massive barrow-tree whose hollowed trunk houses elders, priestesses, and mentors for young night elves beginning their training. The only route out of the valley leads south through a narrow mountain pass toward Starbreeze Village and Dolanaar, making Shadowglen one of the most naturally fortified and peaceful sanctuaries on the World Tree.",sp=0},{t="Creeping Shadows",b="Despite its tranquil seclusion, Shadowglen is not entirely free from danger. In the extreme northwest lies Shadowthread Cave, a dark cavern infested with venomous spiders that constantly threaten the tranquil glade. Even on the pristine branches of Teldrassil, vigilance is required, and fledgling defenders are tasked with driving back the encroaching vermin and untamed wildlife before venturing into the broader expanse of the boughs beyond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is the sheltered starting grove for the night elves, located in the northeastern reaches of Teldrassil. It is a peaceful, secluded haven centered around the grand tree Aldrassil, where novices train under mentors before journeying across the World Tree.",al={"what is this place","shadowglen lore","about shadowglen"}},{q="What is the massive tree at the center of the glen?",a="The tree is Aldrassil, a barrow-tree that forms the heart of Shadowglen. Its hollowed interior serves as an administrative lodge and training hub where novice night elves meet class trainers, mentors, and caretakers.",al={"big tree in shadowglen","aldrassil","shadowglen tree"}},{q="What threats exist in Shadowglen?",a="The primary threat comes from the northwest in Shadowthread Cave, a cavern infested with venomous spiders that regularly creep out into the glade. Young defenders are tasked with culling the spiders and calming the restless local wildlife.",al={"why are there spiders here","shadowglen dangers","shadowthread cave"}},{q="How do you leave Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is entirely surrounded by ridges except for a single path to the south. Passing through this narrow mountain gap leads southward toward Starbreeze Village and the settlement of Dolanaar.",al={"exit shadowglen","where does the path lead","way out of shadowglen"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Every young night elf begins their active journey here among the sheltered roots of Aldrassil, receiving their first blessings and instructions before facing the perils of Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Situated high on the boughs of Teldrassil and deep behind guarded ports, Shadowglen stands as one of the Alliance's most insulated and well-defended sanctuary vales."},kw={"aldrassil","kaldorei","night elf starting area","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","subzone:aldrassil","subzone:shadowthread-cave","subzone:dolanaar","subzone:starbreeze-village","topic:night-elf","zone:darnassus","subzone:rut-theran-village"},src={"Shadowglen"}}
E["subzone:shadowthread-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowthread Cave",z="teldrassil",s="Shadowthread Cave is a damp cavern carved into the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Traditionally inhabited by indigenous Webwood spiders, the cave has recently turned dangerously aggressive under the dominion of their broodmother, Githyiss the Vile.",h="Shadowthread Cave is a damp cavern carved into the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Brood Growing Restless",b="Tucked away in the shaded perimeter of Shadowglen, Shadowthread Cave has long served as a natural lair for Teldrassil's giant spiders. In earlier years, these arachnids coexisted quietly alongside the nascent boughs of the World Tree. Recently, however, their temperament has turned fiercely territorial. Thick layers of webwood silk now choke the stone corridors, and the aggressive nature of the brood poses an immediate hazard to young kaldorei taking their first steps beyond Aldrassil.",sp=0},{t="Githyiss the Vile",b="The primary menace lurking deep within the cave's darkest recesses is Githyiss the Vile, a monstrous broodmother whose ferocity far outstrips the common webwood crawlers. Novice night elf sentinels and druids are dispatched to the cave to curb the spider infestation and slay Githyiss, ensuring that the corruption touching Teldrassil's wildlife does not overrun the sanctuary of Shadowglen entirely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shadowthread Cave located?",a="Shadowthread Cave lies in the northwest corner of Shadowglen, nestled against the rocky hillside bordering the night elf starting valley in Teldrassil.",al={"shadowthread cave location","where is shadowthread cave","find shadowthread cave"}},{q="Why are the spiders in the cave so aggressive?",a="While spiders have always dwelled within the cave, a foul sickness and growing imbalance across Teldrassil has driven the local wildlife mad, turning the webwood spiders exceptionally violent.",al={"why are spiders hostile","spider corruption shadowthread","why spiders attacking"}},{q="Who is Githyiss the Vile?",a="Githyiss the Vile is a massive, venomous webwood spider matriarch nestled at the deepest point of Shadowthread Cave. She is the mother of the aggressive brood threatening young kaldorei in Shadowglen.",al={"githyiss","who is githyiss","shadowthread spider boss"}},{q="What makes the cave valuable despite the danger?",a="The cave is packed with layers of dense, naturally spun webwood silk, a valuable and resilient crafting material woven by the endless swarms of arachnids inhabiting its dark chambers.",al={"shadowthread silk","spider silk shadowglen"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, clearing Shadowthread Cave and slaying Githyiss the Vile serves as one of their very first trials in defending their sacred home from creeping corruption.",["class:Druid"]="The unchecked aggression of the Webwood brood in Shadowthread Cave is a troubling indicator to druids that the natural harmony of Teldrassil is deeply disturbed."},kw={"githyiss the vile","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider silk","teldrassil","webwood spider"},rel={"subzone:shadowglen","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Shadowthread Cave"}}
E["subzone:starbreeze-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Starbreeze Village",z="teldrassil",s="Starbreeze Village is an abandoned night elf settlement situated east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Once a tranquil woodland hamlet, it has recently fallen to the maddened furbolgs of the Gnarlpine tribe. The ruined settlement now stands as a glaring symbol of the growing corruption seeping into the roots of the World Tree.",h="Starbreeze Village is an abandoned night elf settlement situated east of Dolanaar in Teldrassil.",sec={{t="A Fallen Hamlet",b="Located southeast of Shadowglen and just down the road from Dolanaar, Starbreeze Village was once home to peaceful night elf families living beneath the boughs of Teldrassil. Today, the village lies in shambles, its wooden structures overrun by aggressive Gnarlpine furbolgs. Driven wild by a sinister corruption afflicting the boughs of the World Tree, the beast-men drove the elven residents out and now defend the ruined grounds ferociously.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Ferocitas",b="The Gnarlpine presence in the village is not merely an ordinary territorial raid. Lurking on the outskirts of the settlement is Ferocitas the Dream Eater, an enigmatic, corrupted entity whose presence suggests dark, foul magic is actively driving the furbolgs mad. Together with hulking beasts like Uruson who prowl the paths, these invaders make Starbreeze an active danger to travelers journeying through eastern Teldrassil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Starbreeze Village abandoned?",a="The village was overrun when the Gnarlpine furbolgs fell prey to a spreading corruption within Teldrassil. Driven mad and violent, the furbolgs attacked the night elf inhabitants, forcing them to flee and abandon their homes.",al={"what happened to starbreeze","why is starbreeze ruined","starbreeze empty"}},{q="Who lives in Starbreeze Village now?",a="Hostile Gnarlpine furbolgs now occupy the village. Prominent figures among them include the wandering patrol Uruson and the corrupt figure known as Ferocitas the Dream Eater.",al={"who is in starbreeze","starbreeze mobs","who took over starbreeze"}},{q="Where is Starbreeze Village located?",a="Starbreeze Village is located in eastern Teldrassil, lying southeast of Shadowglen and east of Dolanaar.",al={"where is starbreeze","starbreeze map location","how to find starbreeze"}},{q="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?",a="Ferocitas is a dangerous, corrupted creature found on the outskirts of Starbreeze Village, associated with the dark forces driving the local Gnarlpine tribe into frenzy.",al={"ferocitas lore","who is ferocitas","ferocitas starbreeze"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing an elven settlement so close to Dolanaar fall into ruin is a painful reminder of Teldrassil's precarious state and the corruption gnawing at the World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="The madness consuming the Gnarlpine furbolgs and the defilement of Starbreeze Village directly challenge the Cenarion Circle's charge to restore balance to Teldrassil's wildlife."},kw={"dolanaar","ferocitas","furbolg","gnarlpine","starbreeze","teldrassil","uruson","village"},rel={"zone:teldrassil","topic:furbolg","subzone:dolanaar","quest:2459","subzone:shadowglen","quest:940","zone:darnassus"},src={"Starbreeze Village"}}
E["subzone:wellspring-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Wellspring Lake",z="teldrassil",s="Wellspring Lake is a serene body of fresh water resting high within the boughs of Teldrassil, situated northeast of Darnassus. Fed by natural springs originating from deep within the World Tree, its waters feed the winding Wellspring River. Once a peaceful retreat for night elf fishermen, the lake's shores have fallen prey to the growing corruption unsettling Teldrassil's wildlife.",h="Wellspring Lake is a serene body of fresh water resting high within the boughs of Teldrassil, situated...",sec={{t="A Tainted Refuge",b="Nestled beneath the canopy between Darnassus and the Oracle Glade, Wellspring Lake was long cherished by the Kaldorei as a quiet haven for fishing and contemplation. Its clear waters originate from subterranean springs running through the colossal boughs of the World Tree, which then cascade westward into the Wellspring River. In recent times, however, an insidious blight has begun to seize the surrounding wilds. Aggressive spiders, prowling nightsabers, and agitated timberlings now roam the banks, making what was once an idyllic pond a treacherous place for unwary travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Wellspring Lake located?",a="Wellspring Lake lies in northern Teldrassil, northeast of the capital city of Darnassus and just southeast of the Oracle Glade.",al={"where is wellspring lake","wellspring lake location","how to get to wellspring lake"}},{q="Where does the lake's water come from and go?",a="The lake is fed by natural springs rising deep from within the roots and wood of Teldrassil itself. The excess water drains westward into the Wellspring River.",al={"where does wellspring lake drain","wellspring river source","wellspring lake water source"}},{q="Why is the area around Wellspring Lake dangerous?",a="While it was previously a tranquil spot favored by Kaldorei anglers, the spreading corruption across the World Tree has driven local beasts mad. Prowling nightsabers, giant webwood spiders, and corrupted timberling bark-spirits now stalk the shoreline.",al={"what lives at wellspring lake","wellspring lake mobs","why is wellspring lake hostile"}},{q="Who used to gather at Wellspring Lake?",a="Local night elven fishermen often visited the lake for quiet reflection and angling before the recent blight agitated the wildlife and made the shores hazardous.",al={"wellspring lake history","night elf fishermen lake"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, the degradation of peaceful groves like Wellspring Lake into dangerous monster dens is a painful reminder that something has gone deeply wrong with their young World Tree.",["class:Druid"]="Druids study the agitated timberlings and beasts near Wellspring Lake to understand the source of the unnatural sickness spreading through Teldrassil's waters and soil."},kw={"darnassus","kaldorei","nightsaber","oracle glade","teldrassil","timberlings","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},rel={"subzone:wellspring-river","zone:teldrassil","subzone:oracle-glade","zone:darnassus"},src={"Wellspring Lake"}}
E["subzone:wellspring-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Wellspring River",z="teldrassil",s="The Wellspring River flows from a natural spring within Teldrassil, coursing north out of Wellspring Lake until it plummets off the boughs in a towering waterfall to the ocean far below. Once a peaceful source of fresh water for the World Tree's ecosystem, its banks have grown perilous due to agitated local wildlife.",h="The Wellspring River flows from a natural spring within Teldrassil, coursing north out of Wellspring Lake...",sec={{t="Waters of the World Tree",b="Nourished by the deep natural springs nestled in the boughs of Teldrassil, the Wellspring River carries water north from Wellspring Lake across the verdant forest floor before cascading dramatically over the edge of the great tree down into the sea below. Despite the serene surroundings, the riverbanks are increasingly unsafe. The timberlings that dwell along the water have grown crazed and hostile, violently attacking travelers and druids who attempt to draw near the river's edge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Wellspring River lead?",a="The Wellspring River flows northward out of Wellspring Lake. Eventually, it reaches the rim of Teldrassil's canopy and plunges over the edge in an enormous waterfall that drops all the way down into the surrounding ocean.",al={"where does river flow","wellspring river destination","where does wellspring river go"}},{q="Why are the timberlings along the river attacking people?",a="The timberlings along the Wellspring River have become erratic and crazed, turning on anyone who wanders nearby. This aggression is part of a broader disturbance spreading through Teldrassil's natural wildlife, alarming the local night elven druids.",al={"why are timberlings aggressive","crazed timberlings wellspring","why timberlings hostile"}},{q="Where does the water in the river come from?",a="The river is fed directly by Wellspring Lake, which itself is sustained by a natural freshwater spring rising deep from within the living trunk and boughs of the World Tree.",al={"wellspring water source","where does wellspring water come from"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The corrupted and maddened state of the river's native timberlings is an unsettling sign of the growing sickness creeping through Teldrassil's ecosystem.",["race:NightElf"]="The freshwater waterways flowing from the heart of Teldrassil represent the vitality of the Kaldorei's new home, making the unrest along their banks deeply concerning."},kw={"kaldorei","teldrassil","timberlings","waterfall","wellspring lake","wellspring river"},rel={"subzone:wellspring-lake","zone:teldrassil","quest:940"},src={"Wellspring River"}}
E["zone:teldrassil"] = {t="zone",n="Teldrassil",z="teldrassil",s="Teldrassil, meaning 'Crown of the Earth', is a gargantuan new World Tree raised off Kalimdor's northwest coast. Grown by the druids in the wake of the Third War, its colossal boughs support an entire twilit wilderness and the night elf capital of Darnassus. Yet beneath its tranquil, moonlit canopy, a creeping corruption has begun to stir.",h="Teldrassil, meaning 'Crown of the Earth', is a gargantuan new World Tree raised off Kalimdor's northwest...",sec={{t="A Canopy Upon the Sea",b="Teldrassil is not merely a tree; it is an elevated ecosystem standing tall amidst the waters of the Veiled Sea. Its gargantuan limbs support rolling hills, flowing rivers fed by morning dew, misty lakes, and dense ancient glades. At its western edge sits Darnassus, the grand capital of the kaldorei. At the base of its monumental trunk lies Rut'theran Village, connected to the crown above by a mystical gateway and serving as the island's primary harbor.",sp=0},{t="The Refusal of the Aspects",b="Following the sacrifice of Nordrassil during the Third War and the mysterious disappearance of Shan'do Malfurion Stormrage into the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm convinced the Circle of Ancients to grow a replacement. Staghelm hoped to restore the kaldorei to their lost immortality. However, Nozdormu and the Dragon Aspects deemed the effort hubristic and withheld their blessings. Without their vital warding, Teldrassil's growth has suffered from unnatural flaws.",sp=0},{t="A Creeping Malady",b="Despite its outward majesty, the nascent World Tree harbors a dark sickness. The local wildlife has turned violent: peaceful furbolg tribes have fallen into madness, twisted grells multiply in the barrows, and vile satyrs work dark rites in shadows like Fel Rock. Down upon the shores of Darkshore, sea giants, threshers, and turtles beach themselves to flee the tainted waters around the tree. Naturalists and sentinels now labor frantically across the boughs to identify the shadow slowly strangling their new home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why was Teldrassil grown?",a="After Nordrassil was devastated at the end of the Third War, the night elves lost their immortality. Archdruid Fandral Staghelm pushed the Circle of Ancients and Cenarion druids to plant a new World Tree in the sea, aiming to restore what their people had lost.",al={"why made","who made teldrassil","teldrassil origin"}},{q="Why didn't Teldrassil restore night elf immortality?",a="Nordrassil originally granted immortality because Nozdormu, the Timeless One, blessed it. When Teldrassil was raised, Nozdormu judged the night elves' desire as arrogant and refused to bestow his blessing upon the new tree.",al={"immortality","why not immortal","nozdormu blessing"}},{q="How do you leave Teldrassil?",a="Travelers must head through Darnassus to the pink portal in the Temple Gardens, which transports them down to Rut'theran Village at the trunk's base. From Rut'theran, a ship sails across the sea to Auberdine on the mainland of Darkshore, alongside available hippogryph routes.",al={"how to get out","leave tree","teldrassil boat"}},{q="Why are there no mining nodes in Teldrassil?",a="The entire zone is situated atop the living branches and wood of a colossal World Tree rather than natural continental rock. Because there are no stony subterranean crusts, no metal veins or ore deposits form here, though herbs flourish in great abundance.",al={"where is copper","no ore","teldrassil mining"}},{q="What is causing the furbolgs and beasts to turn mad?",a="A sinister presence has begun to seep into Teldrassil's unblessed roots. Sickness has corrupted the local water and flora, driving peaceful timberlings and the Gnarlpine furbolg tribe into frenzied aggression, while remnants of satyrs actively cultivate the taint.",al={"corrupted furbolgs","gnarlpine mad","what is the corruption"}},{q="What is Shadowglen?",a="Shadowglen is a sheltered, secluded vale on the eastern boughs of Teldrassil surrounding the great tree Aldrassil. It serves as a peaceful sanctuary where young night elves begin their training before venturing into the wider world.",al={"shadowglen","starting area","aldrassil zone"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="This massive tree is your people's fresh beginning after the devastation of Mount Hyjal, but the absence of the Aspects' blessings makes defending it an urgent duty.",["class:Druid"]="With Malfurion trapped in the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the Cenarion Circle here, though many druids worry that Teldrassil was raised in haste.",["faction:Alliance"]="Teldrassil serves as the northernmost bastion of the Alliance in Kalimdor, anchoring naval communication and trade between Darnassus and mainland kingdoms.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Lacking minerals and ore entirely, the tree's verdant canopy makes up for it by acting as a paradise for gatherers of Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot."},kw={"circle of ancients","crown of the earth","darnassus","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","rut'theran","shadowglen","teldrassil","world tree"},rel={"zone:darnassus","zone:darkshore","quest:929","quest:940","npc:fandral-staghelm","npc:tyrande-whisperwind","topic:nordrassil","subzone:rut-theran-village"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Teldrassil (Classic)","Teldrassil"}}
